st/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcbest/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcbest/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcbest/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcbest/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gcbest","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gcbest/prep/commits/f5371bf7a6e18c4439f476b1498d6cfd9212d93e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:11:50Z","email":"12885349+gcbest@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Godfrey Best"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:11:50Z","email":"12885349+gcbest@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Godfrey Best"},"message":"Add React → Angular translation section\n\nNew section 02 teaching how React knowledge transfers to Angular,\nwith real-world examples:\n\n- Mental-shift card and a JSX → template crib sheet\n- 19-row concept map (useState → signal, useEffect → effect/\n  takeUntilDestroyed, key → track, React Router → guards, RTL →\n  TestBed, …), each with the gotcha that catches React devs\n- Limit-breach monitor written both ways side by side (React hooks\n  file vs standalone signals component + OnPush template)\n- Six more real-world translations: context → root service,\n  private route → authGuard, controlled form → reactive form,\n  React.memo → OnPush, RTL → TestBed spec, custom hook →\n  service/directive\n- Folded extras: week-1 gotchas, ten-step conversion checklist,\n  honest React vs Angular scorecard\n\nAlso: styles for crib/concept-map/code-pair layouts (wrapping inside\ncards, scrollable full-width blocks), jump-bar link + hero CTA,\nrenumbered later sections 03–08, README flow update.","tree":{"sha":"bb44bcb9d96e3d4dc27cc0bf0999a7c81b9bb6d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gcbest/prep/git/trees/bb44bcb9d96e3d4dc27cc0bf0999a7c81b9bb6d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gcbest/prep/git/commits/f