rs_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/d672484d03262dccb43d3932e73bc11d7f7ace4f","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKGQ2NzI0ODRkMDMyNjJkY2NiNDNkMzkzMmU3M2JjMTFkN2Y3YWNlNGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/74729d261b9b254dcbca26077d47fa6045f81b42","sha":"74729d261b9b254dcbca26077d47fa6045f81b42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/74729d261b9b254dcbca26077d47fa6045f81b42"}],"sha":"d672484d03262dccb43d3932e73bc11d7f7ace4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/d672484d03262dccb43d3932e73bc11d7f7ace4f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/74729d261b9b254dcbca26077d47fa6045f81b42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T16:12:19Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T16:12:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add website release notes for 2.27 and 2.34 (#26094)\n\nFollow-up to #26092. The page jumped from 2.28.0 on 11 August straight\nto 2.35.0 on 26 August, so a fortnight of shipping read as dead air, and\n2.27.0 had never been covered at all.\n\n**2.34.0** (24 August) — the mobile navigation menu becoming a real page\nwith an address and back navigation (#24168), create actions as icons in\npage headers (#24156) and the bottom bar no longer covering content\n(#24267); editing deactivated objects from Settings (#24258); deleting a\nworkflow step from its diagram node (#24292).\n\n**2.27.0** (4 August) — devices and sessions in Settings > Profile\n(#23645); choosing whether records open in the side panel or as a full\npage (#23614).\n\n### Versions deliberately left unlisted\n\n- **2.29.0, 2.30.0** — all three 11 August tags were cut within 35\nseconds of each other, so the existing 2.28.0 entry already covers that\nwindow.\n- **2.32.0** — tagged on 27 August, *after* 2.35.0, so its range is\nalready covered by the 2.35.0 and 2.37.0 entries.\n- **2.31, 2.33, 2.36, 2.38.0** — never published under `twenty/v*`.\n\n### One judgement call worth a second opinion\n\n`Make cookie sessions the only web auth path` (#24257) landed in the\n2.34.0 window. It matters to self-hosters, but it reads as an upgrade\nnote rather than a product highlight, so it is not in the entry. Happy\nto add it if you would rather the changelog carry it.\n\nEvery highlight was checked against its PR for feature-flag gating; none\nare gated. `support gt/lt comparisons on select and rating filters`\n(#24116) was considered and dropped, since it is a fix for an Apollo\noptimistic-effect crash rather than a user-facing filter capability.\n\nVerified locally: entries render in the right order (2.35.0 → 2.34.0 →\n2.28.0 → 2.27.0 → 2.26.0) with correct dates and working anchors, and\n`nx lint twenty-website` passes.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26094?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"668ee68652b47160666a1c7a69f6c1e77fb0ba67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/668ee68652b47160666a1c7a69f6c1e77fb0ba67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/74729d261b9b254dcbca26077d47fa6045f81b42","verification":{"payload":"tree 668ee68652b47160666a1c7a69f6c1e77fb0ba67\nparent 0abef24d25a5a6d738bbb09a5909e915c2580593\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789575139 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789575139 +0000\n\nAdd website release notes for 2.27 and 2.34 (#26094)\n\nFollow-up to #26092. The page jumped from 2.28.0 on 11 August straight\nto 2.35.0 on 26 August, so a fortnight of shipping read as dead air, and\n2.27.0 had never been covered at all.\n\n**2.34.0** (24 August) — the mobile navigation menu becoming a real page\nwith an address and back navigation (#24168), create actions as icons in\npage headers (#24156) and the bottom bar no longer covering content\n(#24267); editing deactivated objects from Settings (#24258); deleting a\nworkflow step from its diagram node (#24292).\n\n**2.27.0** (4 August) — devices and sessions in Settings > Profile\n(#23645); choosing whether records open in the side panel or as a full\npage (#23614).\n\n### Versions deliberately left unlisted\n\n- **2.29.0, 2.30.0** — all three 11 August tags were cut within 35\nseconds of each other, so the existing 2.28.0 entry already covers that\nwindow.\n- **2.32.0** — tagged on 27 August, *after* 2.35.0, so its range is\nalready covered by the 2.35.0 and 2.37.0 entries.\n- **2.31, 2.33, 2.36, 2.38.0** — never published under `twenty/v*`.\n\n### One judgement call worth a second opinion\n\n`Make cookie sessions the only web auth path` (#24257) landed in the\n2.34.0 window. It matters to self-hosters, but it reads as an upgrade\nnote rather than a product highlight, so it is not in the entry. Happy\nto add it if you would rather the changelog carry it.\n\nEvery highlight was checked against its PR for feature-flag gating; none\nare gated. `support gt/lt comparisons on select and rating filters`\n(#24116) was considered and dropped, since it is a fix for an Apollo\noptimistic-effect crash rather than a user-facing filter capability.\n\nVerified locally: entries render in the right order (2.35.0 → 2.34.0 →\n2.28.0 → 2.27.0 → 2.26.0) with correct dates and working anchors, and\n`nx lint twenty-website` passes.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26094?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqr/zCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPHoQAIjpBMPM6WIQp8pY7tIwAyDt\nuv9biS53pgfBP+qyE0zrCUPPc8Y2XH2V4Yq62fYmn/YXdnV55Ik0FrHII/RTjers\nWC4Z1cfsT3fzq4RtYn3C6j3bc1YYBWZMYvrbmaFym2HYaHlCdxqISETtin8XF2//\nX0/6BffD+RXEgRvLMsSzOMzeu0N5OoonzUYTHr6WrYih1xT+eEL+eUAtptauSd9d\n80SuifOqPeaJh29JDOBRDZZE1sMSh406ATYl7yUP4BTmnjFcCV1609p2qj7xtbKc\ndP1EVwTdUaO9vcBJqKcAuTujvfsq0Kl3M/jNOzpqHzMYjtcOSgRs+70mggCdq3eG\ngIPcU0oqOOE7YSoa9LaiyN3EgFiqaeU0b1gRqUpLQ6/MKZ2ftnu06cDUB8CBNIRw\nEzr/PLUljuAt/kXiaTggT6pjGC4HZ26ojMvfuVv9j8KdwXiloAUnslBneoINS+w/\nDBak1Ulol4tiuLlfjldbYg/00R4mD43zMHR7rh30L1tr2J8L+brDkc9gItzULbEh\nxjdc+DtxWExUtTnvMtHUMtoCXlE2m1z6w1dK25LS7t0fFRqDL+/i2iB+4xGIOdC5\nlTGkrRT7aUI74RmwDWxtE9DeFEQaoetbdlHg//moUuwfnwRmSQrJKyuR1EEqkliD\nI1I0x77uFgOK/48nOfa9\n=Q548\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscripti