t":"2026-09-22T22:58:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/0abef24d25a5a6d738bbb09a5909e915c2580593","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDBhYmVmMjRkMjVhNWE2ZDczOGJiYjA5YTU5MDllOTE1YzI1ODA1OTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028","sha":"7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028"}],"sha":"0abef24d25a5a6d738bbb09a5909e915c2580593","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/0abef24d25a5a6d738bbb09a5909e915c2580593"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:54:13Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:54:13Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(workflow): unblock the 2-41 See Active Version removal on workspaces that still have the item (#26090)\n\n## Problem\n\n`upgrade:2-41:remove-see-active-version-command-menu-item` fails on any\nworkspace that still has the item, aborting the whole upgrade sequence:\n\n```\nCommand menu item 31790508-75ff-4e4c-a768-83bd1b0718e0 in workspace <id> carries\nengine component key FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER, refusing to delete\n[UpgradeSequenceRunnerService] Workspace steps ended with 1 failure(s). Aborting\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nThe guard asserted the row carries\n`EngineComponentKey.SEE_ACTIVE_VERSION_WORKFLOW`. It cannot: the seed\nentry for this item declares a `frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` and\nno engine key, and `CHK_CMD_MENU_ITEM_ENGINE_KEY_COHERENCE` requires any\nrow with a `frontComponentId` to carry `FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER`.\n`SEE_ACTIVE_VERSION_WORKFLOW` is the front-side key, used in\n`EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap` to pick the component to render\n— never the value stored on the command menu item row.\n\nThe assertion therefore could never pass on a seeded row. It went\nunnoticed because workspaces without the item take the earlier \"does not\nexist, skipping\" branch: on the dev instance 74 workspaces skipped and\nthe single workspace that actually holds the row hit the guard.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe item is identified by the `universalIdentifier` it is looked up by;\nthe guard now confirms it a second way that actually carries identity —\nthe front component it renders:\n\n- front-component-rendered: `frontComponentId` resolves to the See\nActive Version front component (`6259a4a5-…`). Checking\n`FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER` alone would prove nothing: every\nfront-component item carries that key.\n- legacy engine-key form: no `frontComponentId` and `engineComponentKey\n= SEE_ACTIVE_VERSION_WORKFLOW`, for workspaces predating the\nfront-component refactor.\n\nAnything else at that identifier still fails loud, and the error now\nnames both the engine key and the front component it found.\n\nConfirmed on the failing dev workspace: the row is\n`FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER` / \"See Active Version\", `frontComponentId` →\n`6259a4a5-428e-41b9-a032-333c2d51e15f` (\"See active version\").\n\n## Why edit the committed command rather than supersede it\n\nA superseding command cannot help here: this one throws before the\nworkspace cursor advances, so it would keep failing and keep aborting\nthe sequence on every run. The command has not applied to the affected\nworkspace, and for the workspaces that \"succeeded\" it was a no-op skip,\nso no already-applied logic changes meaning.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26090?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"23d55908a09757551e4abc20240b738c388d49fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/23d55908a09757551e4abc20240b738c388d49fa"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028","verification":{"payload":"tree 23d55908a09757551e4abc20240b738c388d49fa\nparent 2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1789574053 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789574053 +0000\n\nfix(workflow): unblock the 2-41 See Active Version removal on workspaces that still have the item (#26090)\n\n## Problem\n\n`upgrade:2-41:remove-see-active-version-command-menu-item` fails on any\nworkspace that still has the item, aborting the whole upgrade sequence:\n\n```\nCommand menu item 31790508-75ff-4e4c-a768-83bd1b0718e0 in workspace <id> carries\nengine component key FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER, refusing to delete\n[UpgradeSequenceRunnerService] Workspace steps ended with 1 failure(s). Aborting\n```\n\n## Cause\n\nThe guard asserted the row carries\n`EngineComponentKey.SEE_ACTIVE_VERSION_WORKFLOW`. It cannot: the seed\nentry for this item declares a `frontComponentUniversalIdentifier` and\nno engine key, and `CHK_CMD_MENU_ITEM_ENGINE_KEY_COHERENCE` requires any\nrow with a `frontComponentId` to carry `FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER`.\n`SEE_ACTIVE_VERSION_WORKFLOW` is the front-side key, used in\n`EngineComponentKeyHeadlessComponentMap` to pick the component to render\n— never the value stored on the command menu item row.\n\nThe assertion therefore could never pass on a seeded row. It went\nunnoticed because workspaces without the item take the earlier \"does not\nexist, skipping\" branch: on the dev instance 74 workspaces skipped and\nthe single workspace that actually holds the row hit the guard.\n\n## Fix\n\nThe item is identified by the `universalIdentifier` it is looked up by;\nthe guard now confirms it a second way that actually carries identity —\nthe front component it renders:\n\n- front-component-rendered: `frontComponentId` resolves to the See\nActive Version front component (`6259a4a5-…`). Checking\n`FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER` alone would prove nothing: every\nfront-component item carries that key.\n- legacy engine-key form: no `frontComponentId` and `engineComponentKey\n= SEE_ACTIVE_VERSION_WORKFLOW`, for workspaces predating the\nfront-component refactor.\n\nAnything else at that identifier still fails loud, and the error now\nnames both the engine key and the front component it found.\n\nConfirmed on the failing dev workspace: the row is\n`FRONT_COMPONENT_RENDERER` / \"See Active Version\", `frontComponentId` →\n`6259a4a5-428e-41b9-a032-333c2d51e15f` (\"See active version\").\n\n## Why edit the committed command rather than supersede it\n\nA superseding command cannot help here: this one throws before the\nworkspace cursor advances, so it would keep failing and keep aborting\nthe sequence on every run. The command has not applied to the affected\nworkspace, and for the workspaces that \"succeeded\" it was a no-op skip,\nso no already-applied logic changes meaning.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26090?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqru0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqIwQAC+H4pB+pu0nkPs8kT68EpqV\nOAYcns+l4JnpMuX9NTwKYKmw40oB75KWLqDx68uIpi5+dE5N4Tffta9RlYsy58e/\nofmZaTj0UtUAHQMTAPPDocfllwwH/il6kxSvgFN5qz8Vlh7g2siimOeMXWc/q9yX\nkNBLTOqBUammGk0sOYJsMBpiZg0O43Zy8unDdtOIiyeH4bIdHTztVmR+H/voIFcR\nrZKYbvl+KqsyibwtOof0O+V5bSj16RdKOeSAdbOgxqoi0ENcdQZAe1OsCJVlbqU3\nNFV8xee7IF1qZnYQkHII7N5Y4Dqc+TJgBRI0HAXH68LVYUUfpTGERZl/SBbHuH2f\nbSQ4RFsKvHs7SiY0aBbWRd5Gd5Em338A7t8fdhJVDY/2Y6wPJ9WnFJS38n31Az/z\nejmzteoiMCqnM0m4OdpuRPG/hlZDB9HuaWeH16/zUqEoUnhUfgBUon8JcE+f1/bG\nk2hr1XD0fDtoINKnMDRO2wkuaswQ1Zs/5RdP23pvMTov5NitGWuOEoEiu3+3UqNG\n6jti+BANnmYaBUlwp9KFFcZXnlTIjqMxC5NlRb/DzvJEaCNjrCNJB4Sq36yMB8NT\newG9qFd+duwRxfBH1Xgp65SWASS3PURKfF/AsYWPdwa56EeOLnwC42mEXXWXinW9\nu0SorNqnB/wFc3fX/qsi\n=yy7g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDdiN2Q2Y2JjMzkzZTY5ZmIxYmM2OWI1YzNkY2U2OGFhOGE3NDcwMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8","sha":"2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8"}],"sha":"7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/7b7d6cbc393e69fb1bc69b5c3dce68aa8a747028"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:51:48Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:51:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[1/2 Sidebar] New layout (#25974)\n\n## Summary\n\nUse colored 16px Tabler icons for objects, folders, links, and\nstandalone pages across navigation, headers, pickers, and previews. A\nshared Linaria-based `ColoredIcon` owns sizing, stroke, color, and\nshrink behavior. Preserve initial-avatar fallbacks, favicons, and\nsaved-view/link badges.\n\nAlign workspace, main-page, AI-chat, and side-panel headers to a shared\n48px height, with 32px collapsed navigation buttons. Keep sidebar\ncollapse state across Home, Settings, and AI navigation, and animate\nfolder chevrons and the space around edit-mode actions.\n\nIntentionally update the shared `TintedIconTile` throughout the\napplication to use shade 4 with no border. This applies to all remaining\nconsumers, including record cells, select controls, menu items, and\nside-panel filters, as requested in the design update.\n\n## Figma\n\n<img width=\"1878\" height=\"1492\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa03fdf0-a266-430b-9075-e3dd9132fe17\"\n/>","tree":{"sha":"b62650b95cca75ca797f33e3c88fbc91d50b289f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/b62650b95cca75ca797f33e3c88fbc91d50b289f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8","verification":{"payload":"tree b62650b95cca75ca797f33e3c88fbc91d50b289f\nparent 47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789573908 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789573908 +0000\n\n[1/2 Sidebar] New layout (#25974)\n\n## Summary\n\nUse colored 16px Tabler icons for objects, folders, links, and\nstandalone pages across navigation, headers, pickers, and previews. A\nshared Linaria-based `ColoredIcon` owns sizing, stroke, color, and\nshrink behavior. Preserve initial-avatar fallbacks, favicons, and\nsaved-view/link badges.\n\nAlign workspace, main-page, AI-chat, and side-panel headers to a shared\n48px height, with 32px collapsed navigation buttons. Keep sidebar\ncollapse state across Home, Settings, and AI navigation, and animate\nfolder chevrons and the space around edit-mode actions.\n\nIntentionally update the shared `TintedIconTile` throughout the\napplication to use shade 4 with no border. This applies to all remaining\nconsumers, including record cells, select controls, menu items, and\nside-panel filters, as requested in the design update.\n\n## Figma\n\n<img width=\"1878\" height=\"1492\" alt=\"image\"\nsrc=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fa03fdf0-a266-430b-9075-e3dd9132fe17\"\n/>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrskCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPjsQACVpsvSKt1Byzw2tDAht3Y8P\n3k+96hOfIheQF9rqWRBrOTLnHxbsHRpUToOso2ILFk6wZfZV7yj7hJtSdeiJNifg\ne0X4z50ORee9p7QiyQp2n1wnagGqzUuDn6qM+K6J2Bt4W+cBKq/SEm85Pd5dnEF9\n2GkqccjzrlUqY/Iksc+THp61mUlk4CdxiHw9zYNXw1fKcJpQuXaHGFcGFeFMT7vi\nccD3/VQHyi/chZxPzXbeqJYj9kOSKeSqQtAG07MozgzVoXJqxoSynVRvGGYOTPOk\nF3sFwNVgMuQl7lmsYmdys7VmbH3tsphzM9Kq6N7HUU8BLooxELCBfkzcCMep9Ye2\ntDEdDjIj9oBGnUBvfPC1uxAx98KCGgXlTl0DB1uwrUfrSuFfvKGTedOR4t+D4cwf\nN7mrO1pSLI9+8iDdK5JQQF+VtTBIqE5Abn0sv4SKSFMSP1pNlUpN0c80AESNFflv\njpkbj6ghCJg1X0G2Kk8cV5+HWq7hSQ+WR2EWGvJBG6I2RGUp9jaCTENhDjIvdbQ/\n8U3aAjdyhXEVU70/wrWRG4MaNnuqaGWt7ecGFS39Rob4/tbNczNl6ieJibuw5xti\neOdAC/5g9p0UwPBgUZpKdKyjuRQa6/6sNN5oa2L+wmtIXOoFxRF9xc3y/yoSFIyo\n5fg4CuF1pR6XtexwtPeQ\n=GHj8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDJjZTI0ZTkyNzgwODk2OTIzZGFhZmNhN2EzZGRlYzExY2E0NTZjZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38","sha":"47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38"}],"sha":"2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/2ce24e92780896923daafca7a3ddec11ca456cd8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:49:03Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:49:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add website release notes for 2.39 and 2.40 (#26092)\n\nThe public changelog ends at 2.38.1. This adds the two releases\npublished since: 2.39.0 (9 September) and 2.40.0 (15 September), and\npoints the Releases menu preview at 2.40.0.\n\n**2.40.0** — the five-tier AI model slider, the model detail card (cost,\ncontext, max output, data residency), right-to-left layout for Arabic\nand Hebrew, and the `@` / `/` hints in the AI chat composer.\n\n**2.39.0** — field description tooltips, the workspace switch that\npauses the recording bot, and the audio player for recordings that have\nno video.\n\nHighlights are attributed by PR merge date against the published tag\ntimes, not by the generated release bodies, which group some PRs into\nthe wrong release (`#25257` is listed under 2.39.0 but merged two days\nbefore the 2.38.1 tag).\n\nLeft out deliberately, because users on 2.40 cannot reach them:\nconfigurable search fields (`IS_CONFIGURABLE_SEARCH_FIELDS_ENABLED`, not\nseeded), campaign scheduling (`IS_EMAIL_GROUP_ENABLED`), bulk workflow\ndelete (`IS_WORKFLOW_CORE_INDEX_PAGE_ENABLED`), and the Fathom and\nGranola apps, neither of which is in `MARKETPLACE_VETTED_APPLICATIONS`.\n\n### Note on publishing\n\nMerging this will not put the notes on twenty.com. `cd-deploy-main.yaml`\nonly reaches the **dev** website; the prod deploy is a manual\n`workflow_dispatch` and the last one ran on **29 August**. Everything\nmerged to `packages/twenty-website` since then, including \"Update\nwebsite changelog through 2.38.1\" (#25609), is still not live, which is\nwhy the page currently ends at 2.26.0.\n\nPublishing needs someone to run, after this merges:\n\n```\ngh workflow run deploy-website.yaml --repo twentyhq/twenty-infra --ref main \\\n  -f environment=prod -f ref=main -f prod_confirmation=website\n```\n\nThat deploy also ships the other six website changes merged since 29\nAugust (Organization naming, self-hosted pricing CTAs, the\nterms-of-service update, the enterprise license fix, and the\nEnglish/i18n layout fixes) plus ten translation updates.\n\nVerified locally: page renders both releases with correct dates and\ninline code formatting, `nx lint twenty-website` passes, and typecheck\nreports only a pre-existing stale `.next` artifact error unrelated to\nthese files.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26092?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"636ecfb0380df1197b30d4664e355f62748813b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/636ecfb0380df1197b30d4664e355f62748813b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38","verification":{"payload":"tree 636ecfb0380df1197b30d4664e355f62748813b8\nparent 49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789573743 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789573743 +0000\n\nAdd website release notes for 2.39 and 2.40 (#26092)\n\nThe public changelog ends at 2.38.1. This adds the two releases\npublished since: 2.39.0 (9 September) and 2.40.0 (15 September), and\npoints the Releases menu preview at 2.40.0.\n\n**2.40.0** — the five-tier AI model slider, the model detail card (cost,\ncontext, max output, data residency), right-to-left layout for Arabic\nand Hebrew, and the `@` / `/` hints in the AI chat composer.\n\n**2.39.0** — field description tooltips, the workspace switch that\npauses the recording bot, and the audio player for recordings that have\nno video.\n\nHighlights are attributed by PR merge date against the published tag\ntimes, not by the generated release bodies, which group some PRs into\nthe wrong release (`#25257` is listed under 2.39.0 but merged two days\nbefore the 2.38.1 tag).\n\nLeft out deliberately, because users on 2.40 cannot reach them:\nconfigurable search fields (`IS_CONFIGURABLE_SEARCH_FIELDS_ENABLED`, not\nseeded), campaign scheduling (`IS_EMAIL_GROUP_ENABLED`), bulk workflow\ndelete (`IS_WORKFLOW_CORE_INDEX_PAGE_ENABLED`), and the Fathom and\nGranola apps, neither of which is in `MARKETPLACE_VETTED_APPLICATIONS`.\n\n### Note on publishing\n\nMerging this will not put the notes on twenty.com. `cd-deploy-main.yaml`\nonly reaches the **dev** website; the prod deploy is a manual\n`workflow_dispatch` and the last one ran on **29 August**. Everything\nmerged to `packages/twenty-website` since then, including \"Update\nwebsite changelog through 2.38.1\" (#25609), is still not live, which is\nwhy the page currently ends at 2.26.0.\n\nPublishing needs someone to run, after this merges:\n\n```\ngh workflow run deploy-website.yaml --repo twentyhq/twenty-infra --ref main \\\n  -f environment=prod -f ref=main -f prod_confirmation=website\n```\n\nThat deploy also ships the other six website changes merged since 29\nAugust (Organization naming, self-hosted pricing CTAs, the\nterms-of-service update, the enterprise license fix, and the\nEnglish/i18n layout fixes) plus ten translation updates.\n\nVerified locally: page renders both releases with correct dates and\ninline code formatting, `nx lint twenty-website` passes, and typecheck\nreports only a pre-existing stale `.next` artifact error unrelated to\nthese files.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26092?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrp+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9u4QAEeIQqkl0r30cQ5sAMaumgPj\nRRgcdhBNtCXcUBic3yl7yMqJep41n9fhvjsPjOdKJDCJGFQgT6qXPyDLuNdEiZwq\nWpgGM7lPZO5t6iC7vNegAxPH36bL/QtVVVmMo4vwOEUKxbUyoDvcu/5reITOK+to\nSMoT9uX9gtsgPfs/07WG6z3xNFMDd2zDI2JnKhYAFXGgue90UIQXJV293vp57UzM\nm5lzjCin2F9Shcb11x6Aj48JW411RDYp7SOI4aQSv7y6p0t9a+cX4VWx32p6UMrq\nLPAv6xbrBXRUbzMTam87eLNaUM/Y5xSqj5wH53HiWr/ADLYxZG+KhoKTgx03WDIB\nYKehMbejQA6XjlaouJz6w5p01K9X4q6efIp5o838GmsO1xI7tGhpaM+0Hi8Jmwav\n/zv+2iyJhL1qjjfYkvbBe8fl1xZRWVBxZ1dvB8D8j3SFSAIFvAAmkR1yeNwjeuEw\n7KAQ2MYuaMMjokL8L1LDFqt+TnW6bjCovS5Hqd3/uXFnN6kGoeZsuCarq6Di/SzS\nBEN5VIC+9l0+KIQt5CpcrJPu3q8cWCLlzKiWIoq/NLwdvaS+YHxsylVF30kijL3q\nfi2pKe6Bb4XLNORGv+UWQO2tiElazI6zWtui5nJgL7P2OIUybYtFfgj4zcW8S4Ii\nJubXYFql5U3iVoVkBeEV\n=rwt/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDQ3YjA5ZThmZGE5MTI4NWYxNjNjYWQ5ZTI1MGY1MDJhYjllMmZkMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974","sha":"49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974"}],"sha":"47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/47b09e8fda91285f163cad9e250f502ab9e2fd38"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:38:36Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:38:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Share CSV formatting and composite field labels (#25986)\n\n## Summary\n\nCSV formatting, formula-injection protection, and composite-field labels\ncurrently live in the frontend. Move them into `twenty-shared` so the\nserver exporter can use the same behavior.\n\nUpdate frontend callers and tests to import the shared utilities and\nconstants directly. Existing CSV export and import behavior stays\nsynchronous.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 67 existing CSV export, import-mapping, and utility tests passed.\n- Shared package build, frontend typecheck, lint, and formatting passed.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Shared CSV helpers, this PR.\n2. [Server export\npipeline](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25987), behind\n`IS_ASYNC_CSV_EXPORT_ENABLED`.\n3. [Frontend progress and automatic\ndownload](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25968), with the\nexisting export as the disabled-flag fallback.","tree":{"sha":"599c99c2c24a68a27d0f9f3d1a5a93a8aa35da61","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/599c99c2c24a68a27d0f9f3d1a5a93a8aa35da61"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974","verification":{"payload":"tree 599c99c2c24a68a27d0f9f3d1a5a93a8aa35da61\nparent 5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789573116 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789573116 +0000\n\nShare CSV formatting and composite field labels (#25986)\n\n## Summary\n\nCSV formatting, formula-injection protection, and composite-field labels\ncurrently live in the frontend. Move them into `twenty-shared` so the\nserver exporter can use the same behavior.\n\nUpdate frontend callers and tests to import the shared utilities and\nconstants directly. Existing CSV export and import behavior stays\nsynchronous.\n\n## Validation\n\n- 67 existing CSV export, import-mapping, and utility tests passed.\n- Shared package build, frontend typecheck, lint, and formatting passed.\n\n## Stack\n\n1. Shared CSV helpers, this PR.\n2. [Server export\npipeline](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25987), behind\n`IS_ASYNC_CSV_EXPORT_ENABLED`.\n3. [Frontend progress and automatic\ndownload](https://github.com/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25968), with the\nexisting export as the disabled-flag fallback.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrgMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtJ8QAAy/mg4ZshHS4WVISjLa4IRC\nbKzvbURt7KzS9IaLsnN8opl/4K0TPwpKUaMAy4Z1zCzlkaRem0tXXJSSLwbtqdR1\nMxj70JF5z/1JjK2hk9O7Ho4PVPtT26K8P/4Ft+frDXwxuuojMuZ7RK5Z093R8Uio\nXwbEFDrsRLWcvKf1orBsYJE3B5qDk3hDe8DbOOcpjqi4Y/Yqj9/LjqtweoAjoLQe\npl4Tn49ly6HFZitoP1HdFDXH0v5iafezuJHiojZITYy4r7t8Sb0TMt7G7Gv1iS0e\nEV2/sRn5b/ASuZATO29/r5bhfI2Qitw80G/iFFqr48ETnDvHegXdws98inFIVfmp\ntaRRzgoCFHFQ4I3DortmyKDqCArsV4hfGC1zO3R2KVjleWb5fj2IHnkQ9Vxpdv3i\ngVPu45shtS6x/zuXP2uWV4eXsTDUVUspHVc/Oy6o9DP8wghLdsniJ5mQTCiowCsI\n+OIz8d9YEkyNCIXRtNLLGEYnMa9dfy4vYrKLqj8NGvtqHvTRMHIxa63V+I+6Y37k\nnReycy3ccmMKzWGkMCehUU1hRCg65Y+jGcpUb7hlSCFDOtJkFKZsTWK1Lvb5ist+\nQ8HILwFVM/s65GuAd3eHDySyOPZUeqyrk4IxkL3bc4652d0kFhvTAxiqyklIeWig\nxaqqfguqRBuLXLNya+fW\n=hVfb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDQ5MjE1YmZhM2I5YWRiNTIxNzdmNDZkMjkwMWExNDMyZmVhYjM5NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615","sha":"5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615"}],"sha":"49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/49215bfa3b9adb52177f46d2901a1432feab3974"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:16:58Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:16:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Cache billing entitlements in the workspace cache (#26078)\n\nCache billing entitlements to avoid repeated PostgreSQL reads during\nentitlement checks. Existing listing, usage-limit and record-sharing\ncallers benefit through `BillingSubscriptionService`.\n\nThe workspace-cache provider follows `featureFlagsMap`, loading\nentitlement keys and boolean values through `rowsRequirement`.\nBilling-disabled instances return an empty map without querying billing\nentities, which are not registered in that mode. License validity and\nbilling configuration are still evaluated when checking access.\n\nBoth full and lite `ORMWorkspaceContext` load `billingEntitlements` in\nthe existing bulk cache call and pass it into the repository context.\nThe map is available for future consumers; current record-sharing\nenforcement still uses its entitlement provider. There is no additional\nALS store or auth-context mutation. API throttling uses the workspace\ncache directly because it runs before the ORM context exists.\n\nWebhook and command sync retain direct database reads for transition\ndetection. After saving, they invalidate and recompute entitlements\nunder the existing transition lock. Refresh also runs when persisted\nvalues already match, allowing a retry to repair a failed refresh.\nQuota-counter reset ordering is preserved.\n\nThe existing cache memoizes and deduplicates reads. Other processes can\nretain memoized values for up to 10 seconds, and ORM maps remain\nsnapshots for their context lifetime. Production latency impact has not\nbeen measured.\n\nThe metadata SDK was regenerated because registering the billing cache\nchanges schema type ordering. The regenerated output matches CI, and\ncomparing sorted schemas confirms no GraphQL API change.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Local unit checks passed across billing, sync, usage limits, auth,\ntool dispatch, workspace cache, ORM and record sharing.\n- Server and client SDK typechecks, type-aware lint, and source\nformatting checks passed. Local typechecks used `--preserveSymlinks` for\nshared worktree dependencies.\n- Integration coverage uses real app providers, database rows and\nrepositories: cache reuse, revocation after invalidation, full/lite\nrepository snapshots, live license checks, cache failures, and\nbilling-disabled behavior.\n- CI is running on `12e8bc9e9d`; database-backed integration tests have\nnot been run locally.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26078?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"4c8da73a825ab027aacb1567e1f5b92c7c5a7e4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/4c8da73a825ab027aacb1567e1f5b92c7c5a7e4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615","verification":{"payload":"tree 4c8da73a825ab027aacb1567e1f5b92c7c5a7e4a\nparent 6dddeb133367123d523448d53c820e1eaa5028ee\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789571818 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789571818 +0000\n\nCache billing entitlements in the workspace cache (#26078)\n\nCache billing entitlements to avoid repeated PostgreSQL reads during\nentitlement checks. Existing listing, usage-limit and record-sharing\ncallers benefit through `BillingSubscriptionService`.\n\nThe workspace-cache provider follows `featureFlagsMap`, loading\nentitlement keys and boolean values through `rowsRequirement`.\nBilling-disabled instances return an empty map without querying billing\nentities, which are not registered in that mode. License validity and\nbilling configuration are still evaluated when checking access.\n\nBoth full and lite `ORMWorkspaceContext` load `billingEntitlements` in\nthe existing bulk cache call and pass it into the repository context.\nThe map is available for future consumers; current record-sharing\nenforcement still uses its entitlement provider. There is no additional\nALS store or auth-context mutation. API throttling uses the workspace\ncache directly because it runs before the ORM context exists.\n\nWebhook and command sync retain direct database reads for transition\ndetection. After saving, they invalidate and recompute entitlements\nunder the existing transition lock. Refresh also runs when persisted\nvalues already match, allowing a retry to repair a failed refresh.\nQuota-counter reset ordering is preserved.\n\nThe existing cache memoizes and deduplicates reads. Other processes can\nretain memoized values for up to 10 seconds, and ORM maps remain\nsnapshots for their context lifetime. Production latency impact has not\nbeen measured.\n\nThe metadata SDK was regenerated because registering the billing cache\nchanges schema type ordering. The regenerated output matches CI, and\ncomparing sorted schemas confirms no GraphQL API change.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Local unit checks passed across billing, sync, usage limits, auth,\ntool dispatch, workspace cache, ORM and record sharing.\n- Server and client SDK typechecks, type-aware lint, and source\nformatting checks passed. Local typechecks used `--preserveSymlinks` for\nshared worktree dependencies.\n- Integration coverage uses real app providers, database rows and\nrepositories: cache reuse, revocation after invalidation, full/lite\nrepository snapshots, live license checks, cache failures, and\nbilling-disabled behavior.\n- CI is running on `12e8bc9e9d`; database-backed integration tests have\nnot been run locally.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26078?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrMeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA0cQQAGA+Hi66c5K+8/u3Tz0UkWTk\nVR6e95q5xyakKtdUAwIdAq0a6129tpn4DxqH6y9iG1zWMR+DC3sXZ4BBwPxyDkWW\nbzv0oRS6DWZxP7cL6UDPa0Q1nbycKGBEWK2U4o6Y803/X4fqfwGePYMUlFczKe/P\nCq8c8YZMIdUGNBrFeRNj8p7Sv8FKw4D1R6quli0CnOPucGQtO8/RALmt4SnI6BmN\nzdFcpADoglOylzKOdyJ7WIU3Aa60W8np3TV2iNz7j943NY07iWosCVTxsUEN+Kz4\nmyMruxvsPxcgdt2opZ6HXHwcKEQqyLaWZJ/JVanBQAs1pJgbeGQd0Dk8tjgPpf/v\nHS2yK9k9/vKwNroaG4kDAALdNTW5gdypUx0GrnID9Mw0FOZnVjKq2MzdWaD70n5R\n7ysrLXumoX9F/y/x+z0fhUtJstCB9QVETHiTNmZE7nBMAk4Txbg9YKtZ1abKzH+O\n1qWbAMhI0npQ/1fsnGNIy3auScWsV07tRfBg1flkzT+K3QrCIBFlDilOiYx5coLu\nsnQffN84/gWmoL0pZo30XoMTbDAJE5+3Z0FnnlHshZdKMRdCCRHRSD4sp6+CJOGP\naP7DJIE2+63BGfiFI9NcY6vym3mB5z91HThhZZmR3Zf79RzTQuZuNVxDK8Sd9D9O\nSsc9c0AsJOxVPTKZI1Lt\n=4uBt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDVjY2VhYjcxZTZmMTljZmM2NjY4MmQzODJhZDcxMDQ1M2I1OGQ2MTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/6dddeb133367123d523448d53c820e1eaa5028ee","sha":"6dddeb133367123d523448d53c820e1eaa5028ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/6dddeb133367123d523448d53c820e1eaa5028ee"}],"sha":"5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/5cceab71e6f19cfc66682d382ad710453b58d615"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/6dddeb133367123d523448d53c820e1eaa5028ee/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:17:34Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:17:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Enforce UNLISTED view visibility when resolving query params (#26027)\n\n## What\n\n`ViewQueryParamsService.resolveViewToQueryParams` fetches a view by id\nand returns its name, filters and sorts without checking the view''s\nvisibility. UNLISTED views are private to the user workspace that\ncreated them (the rule `ViewService.findByWorkspaceId` and the view\nupdate tools already enforce), but the AI `get_view_query_parameters`\ntool resolved any view by id, so an agent acting for one member could\nread another member''s private view definition.\n\n## Why\n\nAn UNLISTED view is owner-scoped. Reading its query parameters (name,\nfilters, sorts, object) is an access-controlled read and must be limited\nto the owner, consistent with the existing `createdByUserWorkspaceId`\nchecks on listing and updating views. The `currentWorkspaceMemberId`\nargument was only used to resolve the member''s time zone for filter\nvalues, never for ownership.\n\n## How\n\n- Extract the existing `ViewService.isViewVisibleToUser` predicate into\n`is-view-visible-to-user.util.ts` so listing and resolving share one\nrule: a WORKSPACE view is visible to everyone; an UNLISTED view only to\nits creator (an ownerless UNLISTED view to nobody).\n- Enforce it in `resolveViewToQueryParams`. An inaccessible view raises\nthe same \"not found\" error as a missing one so a non-owner cannot probe\nwhether an UNLISTED view id exists.\n- Thread the caller''s `userWorkspaceId` through the\n`get_view_query_parameters` tool so the check has an identity to compare\nagainst.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nAlice owns an UNLISTED table view \"Alice secret pipeline\" on\n`opportunity`, sorted by `stage`. Bob (another member of the same\nworkspace) asks the assistant for that view id''s query parameters.\n\nBefore (main):\n\n```\nALICE (owner)     -> RESOLVED {\"objectNameSingular\":\"opportunity\",\"filter\":{},\"orderBy\":[{\"stage\":\"DescNullsLast\"}],\"viewName\":\"Alice secret pipeline\",\"viewType\":\"TABLE\"}\nBOB   (non-owner) -> RESOLVED {\"objectNameSingular\":\"opportunity\",\"filter\":{},\"orderBy\":[{\"stage\":\"DescNullsLast\"}],\"viewName\":\"Alice secret pipeline\",\"viewType\":\"TABLE\"}\n```\n\nAfter (this branch):\n\n```\nALICE (owner)     -> RESOLVED {\"objectNameSingular\":\"opportunity\",\"filter\":{},\"orderBy\":[{\"stage\":\"DescNullsLast\"}],\"viewName\":\"Alice secret pipeline\",\"viewType\":\"TABLE\"}\nBOB   (non-owner) -> REJECTED View with id view-secret not found\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n- `is-view-visible-to-user.util.spec.ts` covers WORKSPACE, owner,\nnon-owner, no identity and ownerless UNLISTED cases.\n- `view-tools.factory.spec.ts` asserts the tool forwards\n`userWorkspaceId`.","tree":{"sha":"e2d502325e10ce04f2628ac634fac72dc4153092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/e2d502325e10ce04f2628ac634fac72dc4153092"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/6dddeb133367123d523448d53c820e1eaa5028ee","verification":{"payload":"tree e2d502325e10ce04f2628ac634fac72dc4153092\nparent eea5836bcdac1d5f3b720bc713833014385e3741\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1789571854 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789571854 +0200\n\nEnforce UNLISTED view visibility when resolving query params (#26027)\n\n## What\n\n`ViewQueryParamsService.resolveViewToQueryParams` fetches a view by id\nand returns its name, filters and sorts without checking the view''s\nvisibility. UNLISTED views are private to the user workspace that\ncreated them (the rule `ViewService.findByWorkspaceId` and the view\nupdate tools already enforce), but the AI `get_view_query_parameters`\ntool resolved any view by id, so an agent acting for one member could\nread another member''s private view definition.\n\n## Why\n\nAn UNLISTED view is owner-scoped. Reading its query parameters (name,\nfilters, sorts, object) is an access-controlled read and must be limited\nto the owner, consistent with the existing `createdByUserWorkspaceId`\nchecks on listing and updating views. The `currentWorkspaceMemberId`\nargument was only used to resolve the member''s time zone for filter\nvalues, never for ownership.\n\n## How\n\n- Extract the existing `ViewService.isViewVisibleToUser` predicate into\n`is-view-visible-to-user.util.ts` so listing and resolving share one\nrule: a WORKSPACE view is visible to everyone; an UNLISTED view only to\nits creator (an ownerless UNLISTED view to nobody).\n- Enforce it in `resolveViewToQueryParams`. An inaccessible view raises\nthe same \"not found\" error as a missing one so a non-owner cannot probe\nwhether an UNLISTED view id exists.\n- Thread the caller''s `userWorkspaceId` through the\n`get_view_query_parameters` tool so the check has an identity to compare\nagainst.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nAlice owns an UNLISTED table view \"Alice secret pipeline\" on\n`opportunity`, sorted by `stage`. Bob (another member of the same\nworkspace) asks the assistant for that view id''s query parameters.\n\nBefore (main):\n\n```\nALICE (owner)     -> RESOLVED {\"objectNameSingular\":\"opportunity\",\"filter\":{},\"orderBy\":[{\"stage\":\"DescNullsLast\"}],\"viewName\":\"Alice secret pipeline\",\"viewType\":\"TABLE\"}\nBOB   (non-owner) -> RESOLVED {\"objectNameSingular\":\"opportunity\",\"filter\":{},\"orderBy\":[{\"stage\":\"DescNullsLast\"}],\"viewName\":\"Alice secret pipeline\",\"viewType\":\"TABLE\"}\n```\n\nAfter (this branch):\n\n```\nALICE (owner)     -> RESOLVED {\"objectNameSingular\":\"opportunity\",\"filter\":{},\"orderBy\":[{\"stage\":\"DescNullsLast\"}],\"viewName\":\"Alice secret pipeline\",\"viewType\":\"TABLE\"}\nBOB   (non-owner) -> REJECTED View with id view-secret not found\n```\n\n## Tests\n\n- `is-view-visible-to-user.util.spec.ts` covers WORKSPACE, owner,\nnon-owner, no identity and ownerless UNLISTED cases.\n- `view-tools.factory.spec.ts` asserts the tool forwards\n`userWorkspaceId`.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrMOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdZ0QAJc7LlzA9kodtllvf3lDE+yl\nSzZg2hQDq0goXeIjFR43q2C1KPiCIOSDFOi+VsbJUIXoymfLUxB9SWyDv/NlTyAP\nOhPCbx5rrAIUokkbxRcC08hUFAlwyW5Hp+9KQFyXCNsWFdK4TLQVrOGWAPxTiBra\nm3IcVZtKXwV3D79PN+Q4mYn3QZu0p/SMkcHGE0WD5moWi2eH9y4AwC8VaYkiytBM\njvHZDxEtnbGBXxmMfIa+5Gy2+128Iu3ZlrCn1i5Pjq2mYx+nnaXS7JQU//pXSRdz\nZtlvGjG+K727ZOWcn3/540x0YLHdJkrBumHInNSaUQE5Uh+E/fncCsheCy03KjCm\nOFeGrYeKPm0F6DFW5Kb72AswOnHVwZ03XTNnm6XzW260ua/iCBdQjH62i73D/F6w\nhiDW3k7oOVcAs5AnimYE9yq0EWRzpW+pKj7M1pDkcHtLlV/2HtOO4s7bcyoNi+wu\n+aFCZtXtfyC7Cn3fQ2JlfNpsECIqZk80aINUaFQ1ywo4cRJ7ALz87D93BVPv4xg9\nhkrMu8BRkXagx/Gq3yFSwi5iMnah86FfdLpauqpSljocDHX9jyBTnVol3iUMV4HI\n7eeIIrl69dg1DN1YolAUCghpVQMRujcw6Jay0rntRrVgFk28tzN8qofhnC/5HfcZ\n15VBKNhn1rkBvftQebbH\n=r/+s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.g