6ca768115b6ef5bf85db38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:38:16Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:38:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Block system and relation fields on workspace member settings update (#26026)\n\n## What\n\n`updateWorkspaceMemberSettings` derived its allowed fields as every\nstandard `workspaceMember` field except `id` and `userId`, then spread\n`input.update` into a `save()` that bypasses permission checks. That\nstandard-field set includes the lifecycle/audit columns and every\nrelation, so a caller could set `deletedAt`, `createdAt`/`updatedAt`,\n`createdBy`/`updatedBy`, `position`, `searchVector`, `userEmail`, or a\nrelation field.\n\n## Why\n\nSetting `deletedAt` here soft-deletes a member while bypassing the\ndedicated removal flow and its last-admin protection\n(`validateUserWorkspaceIsNotUniqueAdminOrThrow`), leaving an\ninconsistent membership. Timestamp/actor writes forge the audit trail;\n`userEmail` skips the email-change verification flow; relation writes\ncan rewrite ownership of other records. This endpoint exists for a\nmember to edit their own settings only.\n\n## How\n\nReplace the derived denylist with an explicit **deny-by-default\nallowlist** of editable settings fields (`name`, `colorScheme`,\n`uiScale`, `openRecordIn`, `locale`, `avatarUrl`, `jobTitle`,\n`calendarStartDay`, `timeZone`, `dateFormat`, `timeFormat`,\n`numberFormat`). Anything else — lifecycle, audit/actor, `position`,\n`searchVector`, `userEmail`, relations, custom or future fields — is\nrejected and must go through its own flow. Spec coverage added for each\nrejected class.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe mutation with a lifecycle column in `update` (caller has\n`WORKSPACE_MEMBERS`, or is updating themselves):\n\n```graphql\nmutation {\n  updateWorkspaceMemberSettings(\n    input: { workspaceMemberId: \"<id>\", update: { deletedAt: \"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z\" } }\n  ) { id }\n}\n```\n\nBefore — accepted and written; the member is soft-deleted with no\nlast-admin check:\n\n```\ndeletedAt:     ACCEPTED -> written by save()\ncreatedBy:     ACCEPTED    position: ACCEPTED    userEmail: ACCEPTED    assignedTasks: ACCEPTED\n```\n\nAfter — rejected before the save; only settings fields pass:\n\n```\ndeletedAt:     REJECTED (Cannot update custom workspaceMember field via this endpoint: deletedAt)\ncreatedBy:     REJECTED    position: REJECTED    userEmail: REJECTED    assignedTasks: REJECTED\ntimeZone:      ACCEPTED\n```\n\nScope: every existing caller (profile, theme, onboarding, picture\nuploader) sends only allowlisted fields (`name`, `avatarUrl`,\n`colorScheme`, `uiScale`, `openRecordIn`, `jobTitle`), so no legitimate\nflow changes.","tree":{"sha":"12a50cab27857a1cf41b3fd0dfe936febeb3abe3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/12a50cab27857a1cf41b3fd0dfe936febeb3abe3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/1ac815b13e449ca5386ca768115b6ef5bf85db38","verification":{"payload":"tree 12a50cab27857a1cf41b3fd0dfe936febeb3abe3\nparent 91f18c1fa6d08c9df5591cb54abd49e5241722c8\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1789569496 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789569496 +0000\n\nBlock system and relation fields on workspace member settings update (#26026)\n\n## What\n\n`updateWorkspaceMemberSettings` derived its allowed fields as every\nstandard `workspaceMember` field except `id` and `userId`, then spread\n`input.update` into a `save()` that bypasses permission checks. That\nstandard-field set includes the lifecycle/audit columns and every\nrelation, so a caller could set `deletedAt`, `createdAt`/`updatedAt`,\n`createdBy`/`updatedBy`, `position`, `searchVector`, `userEmail`, or a\nrelation field.\n\n## Why\n\nSetting `deletedAt` here soft-deletes a member while bypassing the\ndedicated removal flow and its last-admin protection\n(`validateUserWorkspaceIsNotUniqueAdminOrThrow`), leaving an\ninconsistent membership. Timestamp/actor writes forge the audit trail;\n`userEmail` skips the email-change verification flow; relation writes\ncan rewrite ownership of other records. This endpoint exists for a\nmember to edit their own settings only.\n\n## How\n\nReplace the derived denylist with an explicit **deny-by-default\nallowlist** of editable settings fields (`name`, `colorScheme`,\n`uiScale`, `openRecordIn`, `locale`, `avatarUrl`, `jobTitle`,\n`calendarStartDay`, `timeZone`, `dateFormat`, `timeFormat`,\n`numberFormat`). Anything else — lifecycle, audit/actor, `position`,\n`searchVector`, `userEmail`, relations, custom or future fields — is\nrejected and must go through its own flow. Spec coverage added for each\nrejected class.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nThe mutation with a lifecycle column in `update` (caller has\n`WORKSPACE_MEMBERS`, or is updating themselves):\n\n```graphql\nmutation {\n  updateWorkspaceMemberSettings(\n    input: { workspaceMemberId: \"<id>\", update: { deletedAt: \"2026-09-16T00:00:00.000Z\" } }\n  ) { id }\n}\n```\n\nBefore — accepted and written; the member is soft-deleted with no\nlast-admin check:\n\n```\ndeletedAt:     ACCEPTED -> written by save()\ncreatedBy:     ACCEPTED    position: ACCEPTED    userEmail: ACCEPTED    assignedTasks: ACCEPTED\n```\n\nAfter — rejected before the save; only settings fields pass:\n\n```\ndeletedAt:     REJECTED (Cannot update custom workspaceMember field via this endpoint: deletedAt)\ncreatedBy:     REJECTED    position: REJECTED    userEmail: REJECTED    assignedTasks: REJECTED\ntimeZone:      ACCEPTED\n```\n\nScope: every existing caller (profile, theme, onboarding, picture\nuploader) sends only allowlisted fields (`name`, `avatarUrl`,\n`colorScheme`, `uiScale`, `openRecordIn`, `jobTitle`), so no legitimate\nflow changes.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqnoCRC1aQ7u