url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/4b0dbc34749aba1c5fb44b890d0e903cfd44aa57","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDRiMGRiYzM0NzQ5YWJhMWM1ZmI0NGI4OTBkMGU5MDNjZmQ0NGFhNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb","sha":"17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb"}],"sha":"4b0dbc34749aba1c5fb44b890d0e903cfd44aa57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/4b0dbc34749aba1c5fb44b890d0e903cfd44aa57"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1488979?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Dewin","id":1488979,"login":"Dewin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0ODg5Nzk=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Dewin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:13:15Z","email":"simon.enerstrand@winvoice.se","name":"Simon Enerstrand"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:13:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(currency): prevent dropping decimal separator and multiplying amount on 0-decimal fields (#25870) (#25904)\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nResolves #25870 where typing a decimal into a currency field with\ndefault 0 decimals dropped the decimal separator (`.` or `,`) and\nconcatenated subsequent digits directly onto the whole number,\nmultiplying the stored value by 10^n (e.g. entering `1234.5678` saved as\n`$12,345,678`).\n\n- Fixes #25870\n\n### Root Cause\n1. In `useCurrencyField.ts`, a currency field with default settings\nreads `decimals` as `DEFAULT_DECIMAL_VALUE = 0`.\n2. When starting an inline edit, `CurrencyInput.tsx` initializes `scale`\nvia `getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput({ value, decimals })`. If the current\nvalue has no decimals, `scale` evaluated to `Math.max(0, 0) = 0`.\n3. In `react-imask`, `IMaskInput` configured with `mask={Number}` and\n`scale={0}` completely disallows the decimal radix character, dropping\nthe separator on keypress while continuing to accept digits typed after\nit as integer digits.\n4. Because currency amounts are stored in database records as integer\nmicros (`1 micro = 10^-6` dollars),\n`convertCurrencyAmountToCurrencyMicros(12345678)` persisted\n`12345678000000` micros instead of the intended fractional amount.\n\n### Changes\n- **Enforced Storage-Safe Scale Floor**: In\n`getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput.ts`, defined `CURRENCY_INPUT_MAX_SCALE =\n6` (matching 6-decimal micros stored precision) so the input mask allows\ntyping fractional amounts up to the system''s full precision\n(`Math.max(CURRENCY_INPUT_MAX_SCALE, decimals, decimalPart?.length ??\n0)`).\n- **Display Formatting Decoupling**: Kept field-level `decimals` setting\nstrictly for display formatting (consistent with how `NumberFieldInput`\noperates).\n- **Regression Tests**: Added comprehensive Jest tests in\n`getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput.test.ts` covering:\n  - Minimum scale guarantee of 6 for 0-decimal and 2-decimal fields.\n- Interactive keystroke simulation appending `1234.5678` under\n`COMMAS_AND_DOT` and `1234,56` under `DOTS_AND_COMMA`, asserting\nunmasked value is preserved as `1234.5678` and not multiplied.\n  - Scale widening for inputs with >6 decimals.\n\n## Verification\n- Ran unit tests locally: `npx.cmd jest\nsrc/modules/ui/field/input/utils/__tests__/getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput.test.ts`\n(12/12 passed).\n- Verified mask unmasked values and formatted representations across\nmultiple locales.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25904?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"58d0cfa87061fca90b129e05ffba4ed54943ebc0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/58d0cfa87061fca90b129e05ffba4ed54943ebc0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb","verification":{"payload":"tree 58d0cfa87061fca90b129e05ffba4ed54943ebc0\nparent eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325\nauthor Simon Enerstrand <simon.enerstrand@winvoice.se> 1789567995 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789567995 +0000\n\nfix(currency): prevent dropping decimal separator and multiplying amount on 0-decimal fields (#25870) (#25904)\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nResolves #25870 where typing a decimal into a currency field with\ndefault 0 decimals dropped the decimal separator (`.` or `,`) and\nconcatenated subsequent digits directly onto the whole number,\nmultiplying the stored value by 10^n (e.g. entering `1234.5678` saved as\n`$12,345,678`).\n\n- Fixes #25870\n\n### Root Cause\n1. In `useCurrencyField.ts`, a currency field with default settings\nreads `decimals` as `DEFAULT_DECIMAL_VALUE = 0`.\n2. When starting an inline edit, `CurrencyInput.tsx` initializes `scale`\nvia `getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput({ value, decimals })`. If the current\nvalue has no decimals, `scale` evaluated to `Math.max(0, 0) = 0`.\n3. In `react-imask`, `IMaskInput` configured with `mask={Number}` and\n`scale={0}` completely disallows the decimal radix character, dropping\nthe separator on keypress while continuing to accept digits typed after\nit as integer digits.\n4. Because currency amounts are stored in database records as integer\nmicros (`1 micro = 10^-6` dollars),\n`convertCurrencyAmountToCurrencyMicros(12345678)` persisted\n`12345678000000` micros instead of the intended fractional amount.\n\n### Changes\n- **Enforced Storage-Safe Scale Floor**: In\n`getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput.ts`, defined `CURRENCY_INPUT_MAX_SCALE =\n6` (matching 6-decimal micros stored precision) so the input mask allows\ntyping fractional amounts up to the system''s full precision\n(`Math.max(CURRENCY_INPUT_MAX_SCALE, decimals, decimalPart?.length ??\n0)`).\n- **Display Formatting Decoupling**: Kept field-level `decimals` setting\nstrictly for display formatting (consistent with how `NumberFieldInput`\noperates).\n- **Regression Tests**: Added comprehensive Jest tests in\n`getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput.test.ts` covering:\n  - Minimum scale guarantee of 6 for 0-decimal and 2-decimal fields.\n- Interactive keystroke simulation appending `1234.5678` under\n`COMMAS_AND_DOT` and `1234,56` under `DOTS_AND_COMMA`, asserting\nunmasked value is preserved as `1234.5678` and not multiplied.\n  - Scale widening for inputs with >6 decimals.\n\n## Verification\n- Ran unit tests locally: `npx.cmd jest\nsrc/modules/ui/field/input/utils/__tests__/getSafeScaleForCurrencyInput.test.ts`\n(12/12 passed).\n- Verified mask unmasked values and formatted representations across\nmultiple locales.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25904?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqQKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAjbUQABU9GFPr81IzHlDk4VKfONP6\nx2wauApCW1OReY4rO1bogVeYgpQWeFkAXuj9JDa2fqD/xXcGbAFskk4dCg5IUhH8\n5bAPQo9mnVqBRFgl8YK/TEqUrcyXIfddUbxN6mm8hgaQ+NN09sq++AGPsR1rzywt\nwD0KqoRHw33aSVGnzk0aajKY++R1Xbjw6uehDLEq//7aiLJsGxAxL3U1nKqpJ00u\n+sWCv7X/Qs3MtRV2WHO4QF/mUAwxR7nmJ3H44Jjzpvg8YA4H2paRgS6FSbS+6QWy\nHsu3op489LHkHXjZWosh4b12KpUHAubSFaTwPthFcuF6GzdEKGWyvltil2Kc2Rpf\ne1HZcfy8gA/RHQbLA0NxBu57Ja0rJ+E8ZD3s58YBzC0QbvfzRa2p7NKVI+9vQz+0\nUTyHJZac8xBENXIt6sxs0MeUXOfLrCaxLln+PAKAQnUkOvJqOcabG7NNgjd9RXSC\n6WE6TZyWOz/jGUlLRsyxKpqgn2Qf9B9e7zlHfDXMRS3FGrVIZg52y+890K2CtiJ5\npIPmhvNETKeQGPsWWrMdDmmrdq+ThTwCnXWrrrGmpAN2LY6cw6RY/2gzDDoDzGxy\nIEhD8Xydi2cOF8qrPygBgWAXLayrf6amL2qcJMUy2YMaEZaUpvNZzdTZCfcTwVyi\norS13LPYJzSXObhRpF5U\n=pmWU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDE3YWIwZTNlNTY5OTkyZWNhYWE4MmY2Mjk3YmE5ODg5YTJhOGNjZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325","sha":"eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325"}],"sha":"17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/17ab0e3e569992ecaaa82f6297ba9889a2a8ccfb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29927851?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/martmull","id":29927851,"login":"martmull","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTI3ODUx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/martmull","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:11:47Z","email":"martmull@hotmail.fr","name":"martmull"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:11:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Make record sharing an enterprise feature (#26070)\n\nRecord sharing was gated by `IS_RECORD_SHARING_ENABLED` alone, was AGPL\nlike the rest of the engine, and its code was spread across\n`engine/record-share/`, a dozen files in `engine/twenty-orm/`, and the\nrecord-share branch of `build-row-access-policy.util.ts`.\n\nThis isolates it into one folder, then gates it behind the enterprise\nplan the way row-level permissions already are. After this it is on only\nwhen the feature flag **and** the entitlement are true.\n\nFive commits, reviewable one by one: three mechanical, two behavioural,\nplus a merge of main and the review fixes.\n\n## 1. Move the module under core-modules\n\n`engine/record-share` → `engine/core-modules/record-share`, alongside\n`billing`, `enterprise` and `usage-limit`. Path move only.\n\n## 2. Pull the scattered query utils in\n\nMoved out of `engine/twenty-orm/`: the five\n`inherited-readability-*.type.ts` files,\n`max-inherited-readability-depth.constant.ts`,\n`resolve-required-record-share-access-levels.util.ts`, and four utils\nwith their specs (`build-record-share-condition`,\n`build-inherited-readability-condition`,\n`resolve-inherited-readability-parents`,\n`resolve-inherited-readability-child-links`).\n\n`build-row-access-policy.util.ts` is split: everything under its\n`buildRecordShareGate` entry point becomes\n`record-share/utils/build-record-share-gate.util.ts`, and what stays is\nthe thin assembler (object-permission check, role predicate, a call into\nthe gate). The gate takes the parent-policy recursion back as an\nargument, so there is no cycle. The shared policy types move to\n`twenty-orm/types/row-access-policy.type.ts` where both sides can reach\nthem.\n\nThree groups stay where they are, because their directories are \"all\nsiblings of this shape live here\": the schema-builder type registries\n(`share-with.input-type`, `record-share-access-level.enum-type`),\n`assert-share-with-arg.util` among its fifteen siblings, and the\nper-object `compute-record-share-standard-*` utils.\n\n## 3. License headers\n\n`/* @license Enterprise */` across the now-single folder and the six\nrecord-share integration suites. Shared infrastructure stays AGPL\n(`workspace-repository.ts`, `build-row-access-policy.util.ts`,\n`call-webhook-jobs.job.ts`,\n`common-create-many-query-runner.service.ts`), and nothing in\n`twenty-shared` is marked since the root LICENSE puts that package under\nMIT.\n\nOne file in the folder is deliberately left unmarked:\n`omit-restricted-fields-from-event.util.ts` (which arrived on main after\nthis branch opened) filters restricted fields out of events, which is\nobject/field permissions rather than record sharing. Happy to move it\nout of the folder if you''d rather the folder be uniformly enterprise.\n\n## 4. The RECORD_SHARING entitlement\n\nNew `BillingEntitlementKey.RECORD_SHARING`.\n`RecordSharingFeatureService` is the single place that answers whether\nrecord sharing is on: the feature flag AND the entitlement.\n\nThe entitlement is resolved through a provider discovered at runtime\n(`findProviderInstance`/`DiscoveryService`), the same pattern as\n`UsageLimitEntitlementProvider`, because `TwentyOrmModule` is `@Global`\nand cannot import `BillingModule`. The billing implementation delegates\nto `getWorkspaceEntitlementValue`, which resolves to\n`enterprisePlanService.isValid() && (!IS_BILLING_ENABLED ||\nstripeValue)` — the same condition `hasRowLevelPermissionFeature` spells\nout inline for RLS.\n\nWhen discovery finds no provider at all, the verdict is `false` and the\nservice logs the misconfiguration: an instance that cannot check the\nentitlement must not unlock the feature. `BillingModule` is registered\nunconditionally in `core-engine.module.ts`, so that path is only\nreachable on a build that dropped it.\n\nNo call site reads it in this commit.\n\n## 5. Enforce it\n\nThe verdict is resolved once per request context and carried next to\n`featureFlagsMap`, so the two synchronous readers keep reading\nsynchronously:\n\n- `ORMWorkspaceContext` → `WorkspaceInternalContext` →\n`WorkspaceRepository.isRecordSharingEnabled()`\n- `CommonExtendedQueryRunnerContext` →\n`CommonCreateManyQueryRunnerService`\n\n`RecordAccessPolicyService.buildEventRecordAccessGate` and\n`call-webhook-jobs.job.ts` are already async and ask the service\ndirectly, which covers webhooks, subscriptions and workflow\ndatabase-event triggers.\n\n### Cost\n\nThe feature flag is checked first, so a workspace with the flag off\nnever reads the entitlement at all. With the flag on and billing\nenabled, the cost is one `billingEntitlement` row read per request\ncontext in `WorkspaceOrmManager.loadWorkspaceContext`, and one per event\nbatch on the event path — the gate memoizes the verdict next to the\nrecord shares it already memoizes, so subscriber count does not multiply\nit. Self-hosted pays nothing either way: `IS_BILLING_ENABLED=false`\nshort-circuits to the enterprise key check with no query.\n\n### Behaviour when the entitlement is lost\n\nNo revoke-time cleanup. Losing the entitlement makes the gate read\nPRIVATE and INHERITED objects as open again, so records that were gated\nbecome readable workspace-wide — Codex flagged this and the mechanism is\nreal. Two things qualify it: turning `IS_RECORD_SHARING_ENABLED` off\nalready does exactly this today, so the PR adds a second\n(billing-driven, less deliberate) trigger rather than a new failure\nmode; and it is unreachable right now, since the flag is off by default\nwith no UI, so no workspace has gated records to expose. Deliberate call\nfor this PR — the billing-lapse behaviour is worth settling before the\nfeature actually ships. The alternative, enforcing the ACLs\nunconditionally and gating only feature management on the entitlement,\nwas considered and not taken here.\n\n## Merge of main\n\nMain moved under this branch''s feet: `EventRecordShareGate` became\n`EventRecordAccessGate`, `buildEventRecordShareGate` became\n`buildEventRecordAccessGate` with a role-readability pre-filter, and\n`omit-restricted-fields-from-event.util.ts` plus its spec landed in the\nrecord-share folder. Those came along into the new location.\n`unsatisfiable-record-filter.constant.ts`, also new on main, stayed in\n`twenty-orm/constants/` — it is an RLS filter constant, not record\nsharing, and git only suggested moving it because this branch emptied\nthat directory.\n\n## Also in here\n\n- A race in `quick-lead-workflow.integration-spec.ts`, unrelated to this\nchange, that turned `server-integration-test (10)` red:\n`waitForWorkflowRunStatus` returns as soon as the run reaches `RUNNING`,\nwhile the form step moves out of `NOT_STARTED` on a later write. Added\n`waitForWorkflowRunStepStatus` and had the test wait for the step; no\nassertion removed.\n\n## Needed outside this PR\n\nThe Organization plan needs a `RECORD_SHARING` lookup key in Stripe\nbefore cloud workspaces can be entitled —\n`buildBillingEntitlementsFromLookupKeys` writes a row per enum key and\nreads `true` only when a product carries the matching key. Existing\nworkspaces pick up their row from the `billing-sync-entitlements`\ncommand. Self-hosted and CI are unaffected.\n\n## Row-level security, noted but not done\n\nSame scattering problem, smaller: seven RLS-only utils sit in\n`engine/twenty-orm/utils/` (six already carry the Enterprise header,\n`validate-predicate-value-compatibility.util.ts` does not), plus\n`buildRolePredicate` in `build-row-access-policy.util.ts`. Those could\nmove into the existing\n`metadata-modules/row-level-permission-predicate/` module the same way.\nWhat cannot move is its registration in the `ALL_*` syncable-entity\nconstants and the application-manifest converters — RLS predicates are\nsyncable metadata entities, and those live under `metadata-modules` by\nconvention.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` in twenty-server: clean.\n- `oxlint --type-aware` and `oxfmt --check` on all changed files: clean.\n- Jest across `record-share`, `logic-function`, `twenty-orm`,\n`subscriptions`, `api/common`, `webhook` and `workflow-trigger`: all\npassing.\n- `record-sharing-feature.service.spec.ts` covers the flag × entitlement\nmatrix and the missing-provider case; the publisher spec pins the\none-read-per-batch behaviour (it fails with three reads without the\nmemoization).\n- The six record-share integration suites need no edits: `.env.test`\nships an `ENTERPRISE_VALIDITY_TOKEN` and billing is off in tests, so the\nentitlement resolves true.","tree":{"sha":"49976fb7df6fbf73d18e79caf9001027a63cced2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/49976fb7df6fbf73d18e79caf9001027a63cced2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325","verification":{"payload":"tree 49976fb7df6fbf73d18e79caf9001027a63cced2\nparent 172dbaee1af0083689f9cd2e31ca1545267fb5d1\nauthor martmull <martmull@hotmail.fr> 1789567907 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789567907 +0000\n\nMake record sharing an enterprise feature (#26070)\n\nRecord sharing was gated by `IS_RECORD_SHARING_ENABLED` alone, was AGPL\nlike the rest of the engine, and its code was spread across\n`engine/record-share/`, a dozen files in `engine/twenty-orm/`, and the\nrecord-share branch of `build-row-access-policy.util.ts`.\n\nThis isolates it into one