vice.ts`), and nothing in\n`twenty-shared` is marked since the root LICENSE puts that package under\nMIT.\n\nOne file in the folder is deliberately left unmarked:\n`omit-restricted-fields-from-event.util.ts` (which arrived on main after\nthis branch opened) filters restricted fields out of events, which is\nobject/field permissions rather than record sharing. Happy to move it\nout of the folder if you''d rather the folder be uniformly enterprise.\n\n## 4. The RECORD_SHARING entitlement\n\nNew `BillingEntitlementKey.RECORD_SHARING`.\n`RecordSharingFeatureService` is the single place that answers whether\nrecord sharing is on: the feature flag AND the entitlement.\n\nThe entitlement is resolved through a provider discovered at runtime\n(`findProviderInstance`/`DiscoveryService`), the same pattern as\n`UsageLimitEntitlementProvider`, because `TwentyOrmModule` is `@Global`\nand cannot import `BillingModule`. The billing implementation delegates\nto `getWorkspaceEntitlementValue`, which resolves to\n`enterprisePlanService.isValid() && (!IS_BILLING_ENABLED ||\nstripeValue)` — the same condition `hasRowLevelPermissionFeature` spells\nout inline for RLS.\n\nWhen discovery finds no provider at all, the verdict is `false` and the\nservice logs the misconfiguration: an instance that cannot check the\nentitlement must not unlock the feature. `BillingModule` is registered\nunconditionally in `core-engine.module.ts`, so that path is only\nreachable on a build that dropped it.\n\nNo call site reads it in this commit.\n\n## 5. Enforce it\n\nThe verdict is resolved once per request context and carried next to\n`featureFlagsMap`, so the two synchronous readers keep reading\nsynchronously:\n\n- `ORMWorkspaceContext` → `WorkspaceInternalContext` →\n`WorkspaceRepository.isRecordSharingEnabled()`\n- `CommonExtendedQueryRunnerContext` →\n`CommonCreateManyQueryRunnerService`\n\n`RecordAccessPolicyService.buildEventRecordAccessGate` and\n`call-webhook-jobs.job.ts` are already async and ask the service\ndirectly, which covers webhooks, subscriptions and workflow\ndatabase-event triggers.\n\n### Cost\n\nThe feature flag is checked first, so a workspace with the flag off\nnever reads the entitlement at all. With the flag on and billing\nenabled, the cost is one `billingEntitlement` row read per request\ncontext in `WorkspaceOrmManager.loadWorkspaceContext`, and one per event\nbatch on the event path — the gate memoizes the verdict next to the\nrecord shares it already memoizes, so subscriber count does not multiply\nit. Self-hosted pays nothing either way: `IS_BILLING_ENABLED=false`\nshort-circuits to the enterprise key check with no query.\n\n### Behaviour when the entitlement is lost\n\nNo revoke-time cleanup. Losing the entitlement makes the gate read\nPRIVATE and INHERITED objects as open again, so records that were gated\nbecome readable workspace-wide — Codex flagged this and the mechanism is\nreal. Two things qualify it: turning `IS_RECORD_SHARING_ENABLED` off\nalready does exactly this today, so the PR adds a second\n(billing-driven, less deliberate) trigger rather than a new failure\nmode; and it is unreachable right now, since the flag is off by default\nwith no UI, so no workspace has gated records to expose. Deliberate call\nfor this PR — the billing-lapse behaviour is worth settling before the\nfeature actually ships. The alternative, enforcing the ACLs\nunconditionally and gating only feature management on the entitlement,\nwas considered and not taken here.\n\n## Merge of main\n\nMain moved under this branch''s feet: `EventRecordShareGate` became\n`EventRecordAccessGate`, `buildEventRecordShareGate` became\n`buildEventRecordAccessGate` with a role-readability pre-filter, and\n`omit-restricted-fields-from-event.util.ts` plus its spec landed in the\nrecord-share folder. Those came along into the new location.\n`unsatisfiable-record-filter.constant.ts`, also new on main, stayed in\n`twenty-orm/constants/` — it is an RLS filter constant, not record\nsharing, and git only suggested moving it because this branch emptied\nthat directory.\n\n## Also in here\n\n- A race in `quick-lead-workflow.integration-spec.ts`, unrelated to this\nchange, that turned `server-integration-test (10)` red:\n`waitForWorkflowRunStatus` returns as soon as the run reaches `RUNNING`,\nwhile the form step moves out of `NOT_STARTED` on a later write. Added\n`waitForWorkflowRunStepStatus` and had the test wait for the step; no\nassertion removed.\n\n## Needed outside this PR\n\nThe Organization plan needs a `RECORD_SHARING` lookup key in Stripe\nbefore cloud workspaces can be entitled —\n`buildBillingEntitlementsFromLookupKeys` writes a row per enum key and\nreads `true` only when a product carries the matching key. Existing\nworkspaces pick up their row from the `billing-sync-entitlements`\ncommand. Self-hosted and CI are unaffected.\n\n## Row-level security, noted but not done\n\nSame scattering problem, smaller: seven RLS-only utils sit in\n`engine/twenty-orm/utils/` (six already carry the Enterprise header,\n`validate-predicate-value-compatibility.util.ts` does not), plus\n`buildRolePredicate` in `build-row-access-policy.util.ts`. Those could\nmove into the existing\n`metadata-modules/row-level-permission-predicate/` module the same way.\nWhat cannot move is its registration in the `ALL_*` syncable-entity\nconstants and the application-manifest converters — RLS predicates are\nsyncable metadata entities, and those live under `metadata-modules` by\nconvention.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `tsgo -p tsconfig.json --noEmit` in twenty-server: clean.\n- `oxlint --type-aware` and `oxfmt --check` on all changed files: clean.\n- Jest across `record-share`, `logic-function`, `twenty-orm`,\n`subscriptions`, `api/common`, `webhook` and `workflow-trigger`: all\npassing.\n- `record-sharing-feature.service.spec.ts` covers the flag × entitlement\nmatrix and the missing-provider case; the publisher spec pins the\none-read-per-batch behaviour (it fails with three reads without the\nmemoization).\n- The six record-share integration suites need no edits: `.env.test`\nships an `ENTERPRISE_VALIDITY_TOKEN` and billing is off in tests, so the\nentitlement resolves true.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqOzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaY4QAAyUqYcGeP6ZQC4WHJqAyUl+\n9PQsfpJaF7ijmnADNsH7VYznZH3CvvpX+hXHNAHx+1FZbK6bUX63t4gSuS+hTMqs\n9B5ZUfDfn+lfdHdF3+zU7xzxJ/4XbaisleW3Urdh0ZEoJz3KN7DR66CrhjuIZdB+\nNUmqcDllYR7aHOorZuisewk8v5EuCDJPOerLsFBHmdv+GdLsSpRVPztI9i4MiXyN\nvHXSSgjNs0r2hJXfdNtDuBFAvUOrPtMM2KcA083KhaSxACoZVEXZGey0BcCmpoM+\nr6VcfTqpOFmdefT/2+6cFB6auEVsf8AdZb2jVi4nW5iykZo1tkHBk3Mgft/09OKL\nfVB2W16LBQ6Jef8iyeUyLTufVmdcDE3FlvErtPLqE25s6qzUb8jX1AAx4WkopynN\nFkODBHZSemB/xc5vd1leVS8ZOy2y7d80NX7HIleVevmcO6ReFszs05Q4AiOkiDL8\nnr95iqe5qWLd3B4mstgo5lVezpTXdvucN9xtpzsHykxgQlrHlDfJn9XihuuNHs9s\n+4NqZhvNMtms6vDxLb/w5bKaZLBPjgLGzjausfq9KeSnT2pEZgmGH+31/G4Bw+nc\nuz2T15PSHncjZvvfF6T/OeBroW0WHaLzq7krHFLpzaY0ZhDkSWoSiMHuG2QonC5e\nMhPdoWLi0Z0N+bE1q67H\n=1zxP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKGViOGE5NmJkZWE0M2ZkZjVhMzAyOGRkZTM1ZTU3MDk5MTE1MDQzMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/172dbaee1af0083689f9cd2e31ca1545267fb5d1","sha":"172dbaee1af0083689f9cd2e31ca1545267fb5d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/172dbaee1af0083689f9cd2e31ca1545267fb5d1"}],"sha":"eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/eb8a96bdea43fdf5a3028dde35e5709911504325"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45004772?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/172dbaee1af0083689f9cd2e31ca1545267fb5d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:08:51Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T14:08:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor(server): bind resolved application packages to their registration (#26077)\n\nTightens application package resolution so the artifact the server\ninstalls always matches the registration it was requested for.\n\n- New `isValidNpmVersionSpec` / `assertValidNpmVersionSpec` util: the\ninstall flow accepts an exact semver version (build metadata included)\nor a dist-tag, and rejects ranges, partial versions, a leading `v`,\nwhitespace, and anything containing a slash or percent sign. Rejections\nsurface as `INVALID_INPUT` before any registry call.\n- `ApplicationPackageFetcherService` percent-encodes both the package\nand the version in the registry metadata URL, parses the metadata with a\nzod schema that requires `name`, and refuses metadata or a downloaded\n`package.json` whose name is not the registration''s `sourcePackage`.\nAfter resolving from any source, a manifest whose\n`application.universalIdentifier` differs from the registration''s is\ncleaned up and rejected. These are `PACKAGE_RESOLUTION_FAILED`: the\nfault is the registry or the artifact, not the caller.\n- `ApplicationRegistrationClaimService` reuses the version validation\nand percent-encodes the version in the provenance attestation URL.\n- Tarball upload reads the application identifier from the manifest\nonly, and requires it to be a valid UUID. The `universalIdentifier`\nargument of `uploadAppTarball` is deprecated and ignored rather than\nremoved so existing SDK clients keep working; dropping it is a\nfollow-up.\n- Tests: a unit spec for the version validator; a new integration spec\ndriving `installApplication` against a stubbed registry\n(`stubNpmRegistry` and `buildNpmRegistryPackage` utils) covering the\nversion check, the metadata and package.json name checks, the manifest\nidentifier check, and a happy path; `app-distribution` covers a tarball\nwith a missing or non-UUID manifest identifier.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26077?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"c9be1a74c599bc0ef9585f7bcc0e625606fd7778","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/c9be1a74c599bc0ef9585f7bcc0e625606fd7778"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/172dbaee1af0083689f9cd2e31ca1545267fb5d1","verification":{"payload":"tree c9be1a74c599bc0ef9585f7bcc0e625606fd7778\nparent fd030f83d06b35b09aaa982dd9ffb846efe0b099\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1789567731 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789567731 +0000\n\nrefactor(server): bind resolved application packages to their registration (#26077)\n\nTightens application package resolution so the artifact the server\ninstalls always matches the registration it was requested for.\n\n- New `isValidNpmVersionSpec` / `assertValidNpmVersionSpec` util: the\ninstall flow accepts an exact semver version (build metadata included)\nor a dist-tag, and rejects ranges, partial versions, a leading `v`,\nwhitespace, and anything containing a slash or percent sign. Rejections\nsurface as `INVALID_INPUT` before any registry call.\n- `ApplicationPackageFetcherService` percent-encodes both the package\nand the version in the registry metadata URL, parses the metadata with a\nzod schema that requires `name`, and refuses metadata or a downloaded\n`package.json` whose name is not the registration''s `sourcePackage`.\nAfter resolving from any source, a manifest whose\n`application.universalIdentifier` differs from the registration''s is\ncleaned up and rejected. These are `PACKAGE_RESOLUTION_FAILED`: the\nfault is the registry or the artifact, not the caller.\n- `ApplicationRegistrationClaimService` reuses the version validation\nand percent-encodes the version in the provenance attestation URL.\n- Tarball upload reads the application identifier from the manifest\nonly, and requires it to be a valid UUID. The `universalIdentifier`\nargument of `uploadAppTarball` is deprecated and ignored rather than\nremoved so existing SDK clients keep working; dropping it is a\nfollow-up.\n- Tests: a unit spec for the version validator; a new integration spec\ndriving `installApplication` against a stubbed registry\n(`stubNpmRegistry` and `buildNpmRegistryPackage` utils) covering the\nversion check, the metadata and package.json name checks, the manifest\nidentifier check, and a happy path; `app-distribution` covers a tarball\nwith a missing or non-UUID manifest identifier.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26077?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqMECRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR+0QAB18krzOUBjxH9FxA82Zy22l\naZOz6xV6eUslswcoLYGIsVMVyVZZfOK+kbmS9bRNWF12EZuk2J6iMWdnSiQMsLzL\n1w53gllKut48W5sdi/4pwN2X5D9HfNcA7Z+tft92g0BmG7j3wxUSAUuKAFL2jfPK\nS6TDbcJ2yQ3frI50KwUBwtecrM6XGH1gaCeojOkP3ooW71RPxpDKC+T2ocTWsjZS\naUTNm8s/7Maz95Q3h3teI64TDSILkzmO9Bwral2sGON1S9hpD5I