/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/fd030f83d06b35b09aaa982dd9ffb846efe0b099","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKGZkMDMwZjgzZDA2YjM1YjA5YWFhOTgyZGQ5ZmZiODQ2ZWZlMGIwOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122","sha":"644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122"}],"sha":"fd030f83d06b35b09aaa982dd9ffb846efe0b099","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/fd030f83d06b35b09aaa982dd9ffb846efe0b099"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:59:59Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:59:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(rest): forward flatIndexMaps to the merge query runner (#26063)\n\n## Context\n\nSentry\n[TWENTY-SERVER-JXS](https://twenty-v7.sentry.io/issues/7714403030/) —\n`InternalServerErrorException: Missing flatIndexMaps in\nqueryRunnerContext`, culprit `PATCH /rest/*path/merge`. 109 events / 2\nworkspaces in prod. Every REST merge request 500s.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`RestApiBaseHandler.buildCommonOptions` computes and returns\n`flatIndexMaps` (from the metadata cache). The create-one and\ncreate-many handlers forward it into the query-runner context, but\n`rest-api-merge-many.handler.ts` destructured `buildCommonOptions`\n**without** `flatIndexMaps` and built the context passed to\n`CommonMergeManyQueryRunnerService.execute` without it.\n\nThe merge query runner requires `flatIndexMaps` — it uses it for\nduplicate-key / conflict handling when migrating related records onto\nthe priority record (`computeDuplicateKeyColumnGroupsForJoinColumn` →\n`getConflictingFields`) — and guards with:\n\n```ts\nif (!isDefined(flatIndexMaps)) {\n  throw new CommonQueryRunnerException(''Missing flatIndexMaps in queryRunnerContext'', ...);\n}\n```\n\nSo the context always arrived with `flatIndexMaps === undefined` and\nmerge threw a 500 before doing any work.\n\nThe GraphQL merge path is unaffected: it builds the context via\n`createQueryRunnerContext`, which spreads the full\n`WorkspaceSchemaBuilderContext` (where `flatIndexMaps` is a required\nfield), so it was never dropped.\n\n## Change\n\n- Forward `flatIndexMaps` from `buildCommonOptions` into the merge\nquery-runner context, matching the create handlers.\n- Add `rest-api-core-merge.integration-spec.ts`. The REST merge endpoint\nhad **no** integration coverage (create/update/delete/find/group-by all\ndo), which is why this shipped broken. The new suite merges two people\nand asserts a 200 with the priority record returned and the duplicate\nsoft-deleted, plus a `dryRun` case that leaves both records intact.\n\n## Verification\n\nLint, format and typecheck pass on the changed files. The integration\nsuite requires the full running stack; it runs in CI\n(`test:integration:with-db-reset`). Before this fix the new merge test\nwould reproduce the 500.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26063?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"89b7c2572f65848ef14bfe6f3d9ece6b0fcf22b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/89b7c2572f65848ef14bfe6f3d9ece6b0fcf22b6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122","verification":{"payload":"tree 89b7c2572f65848ef14bfe6f3d9ece6b0fcf22b6\nparent 8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1789567199 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789567199 +0000\n\nfix(rest): forward flatIndexMaps to the merge query runner (#26063)\n\n## Context\n\nSentry\n[TWENTY-SERVER-JXS](https://twenty-v7.sentry.io/issues/7714403030/) —\n`InternalServerErrorException: Missing flatIndexMaps in\nqueryRunnerContext`, culprit `PATCH /rest/*path/merge`. 109 events / 2\nworkspaces in prod. Every REST merge request 500s.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`RestApiBaseHandler.buildCommonOptions` computes and returns\n`flatIndexMaps` (from the metadata cache). The create-one and\ncreate-many handlers forward it into the query-runner context, but\n`rest-api-merge-many.handler.ts` destructured `buildCommonOptions`\n**without** `flatIndexMaps` and built the context passed to\n`CommonMergeManyQueryRunnerService.execute` without it.\n\nThe merge query runner requires `flatIndexMaps` — it uses it for\nduplicate-key / conflict handling when migrating related records onto\nthe priority record (`computeDuplicateKeyColumnGroupsForJoinColumn` →\n`getConflictingFields`) — and guards with:\n\n```ts\nif (!isDefined(flatIndexMaps)) {\n  throw new CommonQueryRunnerException(''Missing flatIndexMaps in queryRunnerContext'', ...);\n}\n```\n\nSo the context always arrived with `flatIndexMaps === undefined` and\nmerge threw a 500 before doing any work.\n\nThe GraphQL merge path is unaffected: it builds the context via\n`createQueryRunnerContext`, which spreads the full\n`WorkspaceSchemaBuilderContext` (where `flatIndexMaps` is a required\nfield), so it was never dropped.\n\n## Change\n\n- Forward `flatIndexMaps` from `buildCommonOptions` into the merge\nquery-runner context, matching the create handlers.\n- Add `rest-api-core-merge.integration-spec.ts`. The REST merge endpoint\nhad **no** integration coverage (create/update/delete/find/group-by all\ndo), which is why this shipped broken. The new suite merges two people\nand asserts a 200 with the priority record returned and the duplicate\nsoft-deleted, plus a `dryRun` case that leaves both records intact.\n\n## Verification\n\nLint, format and typecheck pass on the changed files. The integration\nsuite requires the full running stack; it runs in CI\n(`test:integration:with-db-reset`). Before this fix the new merge test\nwould reproduce the 500.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26063?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqqDvCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8eUQADR8ph18C5Xmcvm72kp7mT1q\nXrF5WNT+ktDeiSJa09y1Ll6YaABchciMfb35VU13+CbrOuA/8ojEiVD991Zjfhap\nI5LnG2IoKr836enhYl7dYjTY176be3RpIz3fzWWt7kVcmqoiKxzozA4oP3ls4LT3\nrbzsNlNyd7+VNu+8ruYBZZ4pSjWqDVL0Z4ZA2IeDkYk3A8UbRjCKECPXimSY8ckg\nLTi2zU7RO8UqIfl9hyFFLh2Op4Mbpu6NzhMH78knGWPrKxz33hgTO3zH8mf5WPJ9\nK8kB0FvMSIntc7qqtJWvoCgHf6Wi94qgjTGEcGkvbKwHJak6tSUorz6r3yYO+Vgc\ndeUiprSxQyuXF5Hdcnw77LSSYt1e5ruucOW8uKoIKBFWCejq+wgu4srM9eHVJUAl\nq9KdDe0FVEjCoF+/ng7BGKowafMSIuNU63rF0bl9ngHM7zjV0OwqXT5DnLvdUMj6\nrBbSL5L3KpXFQAHbUUOo4hexFFP9r7SzlNnQYXUQfkhB5b2ObQ4FbBC3LdU5bTZZ\nhZwKIzayXETG1ovVu9TJIjPfynghOVxi5dnU/3zd4h3TWops6tRLqJjnFAmY8714\n/HMNoE7sGgWPy67KPhEKk6HIKMTPmLf5Y8tzESQOwmg7soKjqaTUqpiJZdrWEDpx\nnI5c8YQjBOnSvZzpR75l\n=Xfdj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDY0NGNmMjQyNmM1MDYxZjM2OGViMmZmZTI0YjFlMGRmZmIxOGIxMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0","sha":"8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0"}],"sha":"644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/644cf2426c5061f368eb2ffe24b1e0dffb18b122"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19412894?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Bonapara","id":19412894,"login":"Bonapara","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDEyODk0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bonapara","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:52:54Z","email":"tdesfrancs@gmail.com","name":"Thomas des Francs"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:52:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"[forms 1/3] Make record creation commands available across objects (#25890)\n\nWith the record creation form flag enabled, show Create commands for\nevery eligible active object from any command-menu location, using the\nobject''s icon and respecting record permissions.\n\nAn explicit creation target makes cross-object creation independent of\nthe current page. Same-object index creation preserves view defaults and\ngroup placement; trash views use global creation to avoid inheriting\ndeletedAt filters. The shared creation hook initializes the form with\ncontextual defaults and handles persistence and navigation. No workspace\nmigration is required.\n\nUtility coverage lives in adjacent .util.spec.ts files. Creation-flow\nstories include clicking Create Company through the real command\nprovider, menu renderer, and command runner from a Task context and\nwithout object context. These new browser cases have not been run yet.\nAll 19 focused utility tests and focused lint pass; the local full\ntypecheck reports errors outside the changed files.\n\nForm presentation changes are in #26031. Keyboard submission and its\nexplanatory comment are split into #26064, stacked on this PR.","tree":{"sha":"c352ad0842980578e03ba4767b417241c33868ee","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/c352ad0842980578e03ba4767b417241c33868ee"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0","verification":{"payload":"tree c352ad0842980578e03ba4767b417241c33868ee\nparent 2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789566774 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789566774 +0000\n\n[forms 1/3] Make record creation commands available across objects (#25890)\n\nWith the record creation form flag enabled, show Create commands for\nevery eligible active object from any command-menu location, using the\nobject''s icon and respecting record permissions.\n\nAn explicit creation target makes cross-object creation independent of\nthe current page. Same-object index creation preserves view defaults and\ngroup placement; trash views use global creation to avoid inheriting\ndeletedAt filters. The shared creation hook initializes the form with\ncontextual defaults and handles persistence and navigation. No workspace\nmigration is required.\n\nUtility coverage lives in adjacent .util.spec.ts files. Creation-flow\nstories include clicking Create Company through the real command\nprovider, menu renderer, and command runner from a Task context and\nwithout object context. These new browser cases have not been run yet.\nAll 19 focused utility tests and focused lint pass; the local full\ntypecheck reports errors outside the changed files.\n\nForm presentation changes are in #26031. Keyboard submission and its\nexplanatory comment are split into #26064, stacked on this PR.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqp9GCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ1oQAH7aMpwUd++KTlHZrlVEYAVa\nEkQZrgC7jxsi9t9tYt5/Fc7eFNqxWRkEM7kMpbWVs9Al9L83cGF/9in1L5UsZkfU\n4wsOE9dQX24Q1G+/ponir2z18GNbEKCqGRB/oUXHr/JD/35c8TkPWHjHmeo+tQV5\nipxuD0vKeWxVadRXxskLUBJ6cTjsrZwTkHPzB5gKpiv2UCxdoIsCoCARJmaFtaWs\nQ7odIjb2BAwtHEj00ZImp252XJEawxRJ2TctSDK77x1Ifg1IRMOMWdp/ZX6quLOa\nB+UMFQf4d95DyH8L4Th4eIuucWPqne7qoUfJJ8bYQ7sF0jrieQiOEEFXloip9mqJ\nz8qKkpjKbS0gNbUrYXRyqxeO4peUp2lUbeM1pUpbEErhdxlu/E8TNhRmk4GFX5qP\nyea8vA0xgsyHQixRD7r71sRe4DwyEKM1COiQj5aG8zvcVfFtvyk+tfi75edHb6t4\n2bmSY9y47vFxJhkPQhZLLBBTLBUI9EbKIFrlRVwsRSIDrDcau57NNqbU9GZwreJ6\n4v2tq0Ak/BVW0pcJ2/7JFpXbwPc2gyJ1xsxQE3d91jU4bO/dmh5GQd09IdnksQDT\ngNaTI3QF7e72BrKyvgoeR6ZHubX3jc/jrZohQTwI8EY8GEUlbHOK4og46grp8xk7\nBm9/Clzi393DLXdhMfEG\n=fqj0\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDhhMGQ3NmRlMjQ5MGU1OGQ5ZjhmN2Q3M2Q2ODZlNjJlNmI4MTYyYzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a","sha":"2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a"}],"sha":"8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/8a0d76de2490e58d9f8f7d73d686e62e6b8162c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22936103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/thomtrp","id":22936103,"login":"thomtrp","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyOTM2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/thomtrp","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:44:46Z","email":"thomas.trompette@sfr.fr","name":"Thomas Trompette"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:44:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(view): seed a user-owned initial view per object alongside the INDEX view (#25416)\n\n## What this does\n\nEvery object today has exactly one view users land on: the locked\n`INDEX` view. It has to stay locked because deep links filter against it\n— the \"See all\" action on a relation widget navigates to the related\nobject''s index with `viewId: indexViewId` plus its own filter, and that\nonly works if the view carries no user filters or grouping of its own.\n\nThat single view is doing two jobs. This is the server half of splitting\nthem: each object also gets a plain table view the user owns outright.\n\n- `createOneObject` seeds the view (system and caller fields, label\nidentifier first) in the same migration as the object itself, when the\nobject is created under the workspace-custom application. This mirrors\nhow the navigation menu item is created, and deliberately does not go\nthrough the metadata side-effect engine: that engine emits entities it\nthen reconciles, and this view must never be reconciled.\n- `upgrade:2-41:seed-object-initial-view` backfills existing workspaces\nby copying each object''s `INDEX` layout, for twenty-standard and\nworkspace-custom objects only.\n\nThe initial view is **hidden from every read path** until\n`IS_INITIAL_OBJECT_VIEW_ENABLED` is on for the workspace. So this can\nship and backfill long before the client is ready for it.\n\n## Ownership and convergence\n\nThe initial view and its view fields are written with\n`isSystemSideEffect: false`, under the **workspace-custom application**\nrather than the object''s own application. Both halves matter:\n\n- `isSystemSideEffect: false` means the engine writes them once and\nnever reconciles them, so a user can group, filter, rename or delete the\nview and it sticks.\n- Owning them under workspace-custom keeps them out of the\ntwenty-standard from/to sync, which infers deletion from missing\nentities with a plain set difference over `universalIdentifier`. An\ninitial view filed under twenty-standard would be reaped on the next\nstandard sync, taking the user''s filters and column changes with it.\nThis is the same reason `ViewService` files user-created views there.\n\nThree triggers, one derivation:\n\n- **Object creation** — `ObjectMetadataService.createOne` emits the view\nand its view fields in the same migration as the object, for objects\ncreated under the workspace-custom application.\n- **Provisioning** — `synchronizeTwentyStandardApplicationOrThrow` runs\nits own seeding pass after syncing standard metadata, scoped to the\nstandard objects it just synced, so a workspace created after this\nrelease is seeded on the spot and the backfill never has to run twice.\nIt also covers a standard object added in a later release, since that\nsync runs again.\n\n- **Upgrade** — `upgrade:2-41:seed-object-initial-view` backfills\nexisting workspaces, scoped to the twenty-standard and workspace-custom\napplications: an application''s objects belong to its manifest, so this\nnever writes views into a third-party application''s surface. The command\nowns its orchestration end to end, so later changes to shared code\ncannot alter what an already-shipped command does.\n\nThe three writers share only the pure\n`computeMissingInitialObjectViewOperations` util, fed an explicit object\nlist by each caller; there is no shared seeding service.\n\nThey cannot collide or duplicate:\n\n- Seeding happens only on workspace-custom object creation:\n`createOneObject` compares the resolved owner application to\nworkspace-custom before emitting anything. Manifest and standard syncs\ngo through the from/to migration path and never reach this code, so\napplication syncs stay pure projections of their manifest.\n- View and view-field identifiers are deterministic (workspace-custom\napplication + object identifier; `getViewFieldUniversalIdentifier` under\nthe initial view for fields), so both paths derive the same row\nidentities.\n- The seed migration runs all of a workspace''s creates in one\ntransaction, so a failed run commits nothing and a retry starts clean:\nan object is skipped whenever its initial view already exists (live or\nsoft-deleted), with no per-field diffing. An earlier revision recovered\npartial runs field by field; it was removed because the atomic migration\nmakes that state unreachable, and re-diffing a user-owned view would\nwrongly reconcile it.\n\n## Rollout\n\n`IS_INITIAL_OBJECT_VIEW_ENABLED` (default off) decouples the backfill\nfrom the client. Without it there are two failure windows:\n\n- Client hides `INDEX` before the duplicate exists -> the user sees no\nview at all.\n- Backfill creates the duplicate before the client hides `INDEX` -> the\nuser sees two identically named views.\n\nThe flag closes both, because the initial view simply does not exist as\nfar as any reader is concerned while the flag is off:\n\n1. **This PR ships, flag off.** The backfill can run whenever. Initial\nviews are created but filtered out of every read, so behaviour is\nunchanged.\n2. **The client ships** (#25682). Still inert, because the flag is off.\n3. **Flip the flag per workspace.** The initial view appears and `INDEX`\nis hidden from the switcher in the same instant.\n4. **Teardown, once every workspace is flipped:** the filter, the flag,\nand the client''s flag branch all come out, and `INDEX` is hidden\nunconditionally.\n\nAfter teardown the behaviour is: `INDEX` is never in the switcher and is\nreachable only by an explicit deep link or direct URL; the duplicate is\nthe landing view and behaves like any user-created view. If the user\ndeletes every view on an object, `INDEX` shows again — that is a\nview-count fallback and needs no flag.\n\n### Where the filter lives\n\n- `ViewService.getFilteredFlatViews` — the choke point behind the\ncollection reads.\n- `MinimalMetadataService` — the bootstrap views payload, which does not\ngo through `ViewService`.\n\nBoth apply `isInitialObjectView`, a pure per-row predicate: a view is\nthe initial one when its own `universalIdentifier` equals the identifier\nderived from its own application and object. No application lookup, no\nobject-map recompute, nothing that can throw, and the cost is one hash\nper view only while the flag is off.\n\nReads by id (`findById`, `findByIdWithRelations`) are deliberately\n**not** filtered. The row id is a `v4`, not the deterministic\nidentifier, so it is not guessable, and the flag exists to control what\nthe picker shows rather than to be an access-control boundary.\n\nThe write side is not gated by the flag either: the view is created\nwhenever an object is created, and simply stays hidden until the flag is\non.\n\nAn earlier revision used a `ViewKey.DEFAULT` marker instead; it was\ndropped because it put a transitional value in a public enum and\n`CreateViewInput` let any API caller claim it. A later revision resolved\nthe hidden set through a service that looked up the workspace-custom\napplication on every read; that was replaced by the per-row predicate\nabove, which cannot throw on a workspace whose application registration\nis missing.\n\n## Also not addressed\n\n- **Application-owned objects installed after the backfill.** The\nbackfill seeds every existing non-remote object with a live `INDEX`\nview, app-owned ones included, so they get a user-owned view. But the\ncreate-time handler only fires for workspace-custom objects, so an app\nobject installed later gets none. Closing that means letting an\napplication sync emit workspace-custom rows, which stops the sync being\na pure projection of its manifest - a design call, and a blocker for the\nteardown step above.\n- **New fields do not append to the initial view.** That follows from\nthe ownership decision and is intended, but it is worth re-litigating: a\nnew custom field is invisible in the view people use until they add the\ncolumn.\n- **View ordering.** Felix noted Opportunity ends up with two same-level\nviews and Kanban should sort first. The initial view takes a fixed\nposition, which keeps it out of first place, but nothing reorders\nexisting views.\n- **The initial view name is a plain English literal**, while\n`INDEX_VIEW_NAME` is an i18n template resolved at read time. A\nnon-English workspace shows the two side by side in different languages,\nand an object rename does not propagate to the initial view.\n\n## Testing\n\n- `twenty-server` and `twenty-shared` typecheck clean; oxlint and oxfmt\nclean.\n- Unit specs for the deterministic identifiers, the initial view shape,\nand the initial field set (caller field included, label identifier at\nposition 0, user-owned keying).\n- Backfill run against a real workspace: 63 initial views and their\nfields created, exactly one per object, no duplicates, and invisible in\nthe UI while the flag was off.\n- Browser pass with the flag on: the initial view becomes the landing\nview, `INDEX` drops out of the switcher, a deep link to the `INDEX` view\nid still renders it, and deleting the initial view falls back to\n`INDEX`.\n- Not run locally: the integration suites.","tree":{"sha":"394f2e02b712e5e0110b19f44e4e98aaa4eb19b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/394f2e02b712e5e0110b19f44e4e98aaa4eb19b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a","verification":{"payload":"tree 394f2e02b712e5e0110b19f44e4e98aaa4eb19b1\nparent a7e2fbbc501270b8b6e7ce71a164da0ffb316be2\nauthor Thomas Trompette <thomas.trompette@sfr.fr> 1789566286 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789566286 +0000\n\nfeat(view): seed a user-owned initial view per object alongside the INDEX view (#25416)\n\n## What this does\n\nEvery object today has exactly one view users land on: the locked\n`INDEX` view. It has to stay locked because deep links filter against it\n— the \"See all\" action on a relation widget navigates to the related\nobject''s index with `viewId: indexViewId` plus its own filter, and that\nonly works if the view carries no user filters or grouping of its own.\n\nThat single view is doing two jobs. This is the server half of splitting\nthem: each object also gets a plain table view the user owns outright.\n\n- `createOneObject` seeds the view (system and caller fields, label\nidentifier first) in the same migration as the object itself, when the\nobject is created under the workspace-custom application. This mirrors\nhow the navigation menu item is created, and deliberately does not go\nthrough the metadata side-effect engine: that engine emits entities it\nthen reconciles, and this view must never be reconciled.\n- `upgrade:2-41:seed-object-initial-view` backfills existing workspaces\nby copying each object''s `INDEX` layout, for twenty-standard and\nworkspace-custom objects only.\n\nThe initial view is **hidden from every read path** until\n`IS_INITIAL_OBJECT_VIEW_ENABLED` is on for the workspace. So this can\nship and backfill long before the client is ready for it.\n\n## O