316be2"}],"sha":"2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/2cb6c6da94e8be914aede6f2aa716f8594915d1a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/a7e2fbbc501270b8b6e7ce71a164da0ffb316be2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:41:37Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:41:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Consume the OAuth authorization code atomically (#26025)\n\n## What\n\n`exchangeAuthorizationCode` loads the authorization code, checks it is\nnot yet revoked, runs PKCE/redirect/client validation, and only then\nmarks it revoked with an **unconditional** `update` — with no `WHERE\nrevokedAt IS NULL` and no transaction around the read and the write. Two\nconcurrent redemptions of the same single-use code can both pass the\nrevoked check before either has written, and each is issued an\naccess/refresh token pair.\n\n## Why\n\nAn authorization code must be redeemable exactly once (RFC 6749 §4.1.2).\nThe revoked-code check and the revocation write were not atomic, so the\nsingle-use guarantee did not hold under concurrency, and the\nreplay-detection warning never fired for the racing request.\n\n## How\n\nReplace the unconditional revocation with an atomic conditional one —\n`UPDATE … SET revokedAt = now() WHERE id = ? AND revokedAt IS NULL` —\nand check the affected-row count. The database serializes the flip, so\nexactly one concurrent redemption wins; any other is rejected with\n`invalid_grant` **before** any token is issued. The consume stays after\nPKCE/redirect/client validation, so an invalid request still does not\nburn the code.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nTwo redemptions of the **same** authorization code, interleaved so both\nread the code as not-yet-revoked (the race window):\n\n```bash\n# both sent within the race window, same code\ncurl -X POST https://<host>/oauth/token -d ''grant_type=authorization_code&code=<code>&client_id=<id>&client_secret=<secret>&redirect_uri=<uri>'' &\ncurl -X POST https://<host>/oauth/token -d ''grant_type=authorization_code&code=<code>&client_id=<id>&client_secret=<secret>&redirect_uri=<uri>'' &\n```\n\nBefore — both succeed; one code yields two token pairs:\n\n```\nredemption #1: TOKENS ISSUED\nredemption #2: TOKENS ISSUED\n```\n\nAfter — only the first wins:\n\n```\nredemption #1: TOKENS ISSUED\nredemption #2: REJECTED: invalid_grant - Authorization code has already been used\n```\n\nReproduced by driving `exchangeAuthorizationCode` with a repository stub\nthat models the database''s single conditional flip (the first write\naffects one row, the second affects zero), so the outcome reflects only\nhow the consume step is written.\n\nScope: sequential reuse was already rejected by the existing `revokedAt`\ncheck; this closes the concurrent case. No change to token payloads,\ngrant validation order, or public-client behavior.","tree":{"sha":"41542a1528da0a1948b47c0e9675d2c3e39898f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/41542a1528da0a1948b47c0e9675d2c3e39898f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/a7e2fbbc501270b8b6e7ce71a164da0ffb316be2","verification":{"payload":"tree 41542a1528da0a1948b47c0e9675d2c3e39898f9\nparent 3627c6b7a78aa3fb15aa979a24f703c03a75b9bc\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1789566097 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789566097 +0000\n\nConsume the OAuth authorization code atomically (#26025)\n\n## What\n\n`exchangeAuthorizationCode` loads the authorization code, checks it is\nnot yet revoked, runs PKCE/redirect/client validation, and only then\nmarks it revoked with an **unconditional** `update` — with no `WHERE\nrevokedAt IS NULL` and no transaction around the read and the write. Two\nconcurrent redemptions of the same single-use code can both pass the\nrevoked check before either has written, and each is issued an\naccess/refresh token pair.\n\n## Why\n\nAn authorization code must be redeemable exactly once (RFC 6749 §4.1.2).\nThe revoked-code check and the revocation write were not atomic, so the\nsingle-use guarantee did not hold under concurrency, and the\nreplay-detection warning never fired for the racing request.\n\n## How\n\nReplace the unconditional revocation with an atomic conditional one —\n`UPDATE … SET revokedAt = now() WHERE id = ? AND revokedAt IS NULL` —\nand check the affected-row count. The database serializes the flip, so\nexactly one concurrent redemption wins; any other is rejected with\n`invalid_grant` **before** any token is issued. The consume stays after\nPKCE/redirect/client validation, so an invalid request still does not\nburn the code.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nTwo redemptions of the **same** authorization code, interleaved so both\nread the code as not-yet-revoked (the race window):\n\n```bash\n# both sent within the race window, same code\ncurl -X POST https://<host>/oauth/token -d ''grant_type=authorization_code&code=<code>&client_id=<id>&client_secret=<secret>&redirect_uri=<uri>'' &\ncurl -X POST https://<host>/oauth/token -d ''grant_type=authorization_code&code=<code>&client_id=<id>&client_secret=<secret>&redirect_uri=<uri>'' &\n```\n\nBefore — both succeed; one code yields two token pairs:\n\n```\nredemption #1: TOKENS ISSUED\nredemption #2: TOKENS ISSUED\n```\n\nAfter — only the first wins:\n\n```\nredemption #1: TOKENS ISSUED\nredemption #2: REJECTED: invalid_grant - Authorization code has already been used\n```\n\nReproduced by driving `exchangeAuthorizationCode` with a repository stub\nthat models the database''s single conditional flip (the first write\naffects one row, the second affects zero), so the outcome reflects only\nhow the consume step is written.\n\nScope: sequential reuse was already rejected by the existing `revokedAt`\ncheck; this closes the concurrent case. No change to token payloads,\ngrant validation order, or public-client behavior.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqpyhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAEpIQADp6p3qS8wlkAbX0jrRADHG1\nQZI1/ILeQUo4IEos5+dboWnMV5n9V1LRNjCohHvudsZJAI2EgiJcQFC9MgPYzIvO\nEgH5HrhKUjWkchjVpzfT8xj1k6yR0to44GhDOvzEDZg1P2tYNqrFaTIvs/uH0NMr\nA3aXxkTB43eg+NJ9sncu3ljx2mJl37jD65D98zEJUD113ZjRIYcgzeAsW2mQVgPU\naO7SPtrt6t3DxKZ4XJnY3gLHRa8YQyoH9Mv5s+nmfoHbqxcJocx558fuil8z/DeK\nLYM71gDPG68Ln0l5+Yw1MwxkW4VmRRpundSi7SO5Pi2VbUylDuV1/rCU8YknzN5O\n0imm/oOMn3Y8Zuuum9Qh7Kd1TZtWrAt/rTfXCHwJDFKQqkjdrfTO3eM5as3JoSjc\nTUQc6ZSAltyxlIwEmrDPC6znkeEL8ffQvQ7QHJU0SVlj7+/Ek4tcJBZzHSRJqeTl\noFats+OeNQgQ68Gw2kTq/cwPufcBjMqvuJ1ihAa8q84AhL/cfdPTjZI/kUaha731\n/zur4rYvhaTq9sPaSzFr18ve1LMGnDe2ypfRnzIImrdMfoJy9OZDSjmvxG3cCdBN\nh4KlQq9pcDu4R8eguXQ+a2SN/jI2tgq/mCR0Hluxy67X0dACiFsPMjZzw6f2kBNC\nEjJHU31dZWYElbYuOzFq\n=dBO9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:18Z"}},