YWEzZmIxNWFhOTc5YTI0ZjcwM2MwM2E3NWI5YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/ba8ca7343f1b6131c5b06576ac8851d8c020f771","sha":"ba8ca7343f1b6131c5b06576ac8851d8c020f771","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/ba8ca7343f1b6131c5b06576ac8851d8c020f771"}],"sha":"3627c6b7a78aa3fb15aa979a24f703c03a75b9bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/3627c6b7a78aa3fb15aa979a24f703c03a75b9bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/ba8ca7343f1b6131c5b06576ac8851d8c020f771/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:25:53Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:25:53Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Write roles and permission flags on pull (#25994)\n\nStacked on #25984 (row-level permission predicates export).\n\n## What\n\n`yarn twenty pull` now writes the roles and permission flags the server\nexports:\n\n- **Permission flags:** `definePermissionFlag()` files in\n`src/permission-flags/`.\n- **Roles:** `defineRole()` files in `src/roles/`, with object\npermissions, field permissions, row-level permission predicate groups,\npredicates and permission flags inline.\n- **The default role:** written with `defineApplicationRole()`, and the\napplication config then drops `defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier`. The\nconfig keeps it when the default role is not one of the app''s own roles,\nas for the workspace Custom application, whose export carries the Admin\nplaceholder.\n\nDetails:\n\n- **Derived identifiers:** an object or field permission identifier that\nequals the one the build derives\n(`getObjectPermissionUniversalIdentifier` /\n`getFieldPermissionUniversalIdentifier`) is left out. Any other\nidentifier is kept, so re-applying matches the same rows.\n- **Enums:** predicate operands, group logical operators and system\npermission flags are written as `RowLevelPermissionPredicateOperand`,\n`RowLevelPermissionPredicateGroupLogicalOperator` and\n`SystemPermissionFlag` members, so the files typecheck.\n- **Change detection:** the planner now also compares an existing file''s\ndefine function with the one pull would write. A role that became or\nstopped being the default is rewritten even when its config did not\nchange, so a tree never ends up with two `defineApplicationRole` files\nor none. `ScannedSourceFile` now records the define function for this.\n- **Base file:** a base whose roles or permission flags are not lists is\nignored.\n- **Docs:** `sync-and-recovery.mdx` lists the new files and no longer\nsays roles and permissions are not exported.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`build-pull-entities.spec.ts`:**\n  - file paths for roles and flags;\n  - `defineApplicationRole` only for the exported default role;\n  - the application config with and without the default role written;\n  - derived permission identifiers left out, others kept.\n- **`write-define-file.spec.ts`:** enum members in a role file, and a\npermission flag file.\n- **`plan-pull-writes.spec.ts`:**\n  - a default role file written with `defineRole` is regenerated;\n  - one written with `defineApplicationRole` is left untouched;\n- fixtures now carry the define function, and the example of a kind pull\ncannot write is a logic function instead of a role.\n- **`pull-base-file.spec.ts`:** roles and permission flags must be\nlists.\n- **`pull-round-trip.integration.spec.ts`:** these rebuild unchanged\nthrough the real build, and the default role resolves from its file:\n  - a permission flag;\n- a default role with one derived and one explicit permission\nidentifier;\n  - a role with nested predicate groups, a predicate and a system flag.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25994?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"ccaf15ac69cb29a9346709cdea8b11c65de52b2a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/ccaf15ac69cb29a9346709cdea8b11c65de52b2a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/ba8ca7343f1b6131c5b06576ac8851d8c020f771","verification":{"payload":"tree ccaf15ac69cb29a9346709cdea8b11c65de52b2a\nparent e78e52716e301ab3e96d525530623120acd387d7\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789565153 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789565153 +0000\n\nWrite roles and permission flags on pull (#25994)\n\nStacked on #25984 (row-level permission predicates export).\n\n## What\n\n`yarn twenty pull` now writes the roles and permission flags the server\nexports:\n\n- **Permission flags:** `definePermissionFlag()` files in\n`src/permission-flags/`.\n- **Roles:** `defineRole()` files in `src/roles/`, with object\npermissions, field permissions, row-level permission predicate groups,\npredicates and permission flags inline.\n- **The default role:** written with `defineApplicationRole()`, and the\napplication config then drops `defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier`. The\nconfig keeps it when the default role is not one of the app''s own roles,\nas for the workspace Custom application, whose export carries the Admin\nplaceholder.\n\nDetails:\n\n- **Derived identifiers:** an object or field permission identifier that\nequals the one the build derives\n(`getObjectPermissionUniversalIdentifier` /\n`getFieldPermissionUniversalIdentifier`) is left out. Any other\nidentifier is kept, so re-applying matches the same rows.\n- **Enums:** predicate operands, group logical operators and system\npermission flags are written as `RowLevelPermissionPredicateOperand`,\n`RowLevelPermissionPredicateGroupLogicalOperator` and\n`SystemPermissionFlag` members, so the files typecheck.\n- **Change detection:** the planner now also compares an existing file''s\ndefine function with the one pull would write. A role that became or\nstopped being the default is rewritten even when its config did not\nchange, so a tree never ends up with two `defineApplicationRole` files\nor none. `ScannedSourceFile` now records the define function for this.\n- **Base file:** a base whose roles or permission flags are not lists is\nignored.\n- **Docs:** `sync-and-recovery.mdx` lists the new files and no longer\nsays roles and permissions are not exported.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **`build-pull-entities.spec.ts`:**\n  - file paths for roles and flags;\n  - `defineApplicationRole` only for the exported default role;\n  - the application config with and without the default role written;\n  - derived permission identifiers left out, others kept.\n- **`write-define-file.spec.ts`:** enum members in a role file, and a\npermission flag file.\n- **`plan-pull-writes.spec.ts`:**\n  - a default role file written with `defineRole` is regenerated;\n  - one written with `defineApplicationRole` is left untouched;\n- fixtures now carry the define function, and the example of a kind pull\ncannot write is a logic function instead of a role.\n- **`pull-base-file.spec.ts`:** roles and permission flags must be\nlists.\n- **`pull-round-trip.integration.spec.ts`:** these rebuild unchanged\nthrough the real build, and the default role resolves from its file:\n  - a permission flag;\n- a default role with one derived and one explicit permission\nidentifier;\n  - a role with nested predicate groups, a predicate and a system flag.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25994?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqpjwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAs3QQABNTEcivmTjG47aWbWC56tsZ\nVFmure6dLmTsSdaTrD4P0j/WTFzWl4O87op9IXXl7VMAT44QFf+wFICM7frqVsga\neiIlU+ELhAIGGmY7V8JH8Bhpr8Zq/ziEdryomITLb6vK4xy+aFfp5RXhSSIURVA5\npo9/3MnE/2Njfr7EPId6gejEGDTFjF/Q0QcWuo1VcgEqLvw0r/2bpRbuV68nv6TC\nUpO7MM2XwAjOgJD3Os/tdup4+hQx1KGergCcrpZ7mLtcOurbCNjNk0fLbtsLz43o\nGrYMgPNBAg+PqLf2pVg370HiFufZcmHOgXKd0bwJSiOUtKjTnjbAB3YPa2G5F6lM\nCXilu5h7qpfB4gIcG4ZiXAwymI5vKzOaTOYvzKPAGg+dMVAN0pYUrENQ+buetX9w\ny1z0wj9fRxME6Et5FQgQUmBt5Zn7IiAG/fxTCl0mE0IDEBMJLpcsG4s0l7tAi/kX\nr6t8KYYsfZuw9LZo9D7X6YGN/D/mdIEpYSc