ty-desync/commits/b99496205a23a3a880a68a7d8080f73af4b002fc"}],"sha":"81546a67866b2a4b4e6289cf4cae31e12f56c670","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/81546a67866b2a4b4e6289cf4cae31e12f56c670"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71827178?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bosiraphael","id":71827178,"login":"bosiraphael","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxODI3MTc4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bosiraphael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/b99496205a23a3a880a68a7d8080f73af4b002fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:11:25Z","email":"71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Raphaël Bosi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:11:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Replace frontend snackbars with twenty-ui toasts (#25664)\n\nMoves frontend notifications into `twenty-ui` and removes the snackbar\nmanager abstraction.\n\n`useToast()` exposes `enqueueToast` and `closeToast`, with queue limits,\ndeduplication, and exit animations. A Base UI store keeps toast state\nisolated per provider.\n\n`mountedToasterCount` tracks mounted `<Toaster>` renderers separately\nfrom the toast array: a renderer can have an empty queue, and toasts can\nbe queued before any renderer mounts. Dismissed toasts remain for exit\nanimations while a renderer is mounted and are removed immediately\notherwise. When the last renderer unmounts, unfinished exits are removed\nand visible toasts are preserved. Using a count keeps this cleanup\ncorrect when multiple renderers share a provider.\n\nError formatting and translations remain in the frontend. The SDK’s\n`enqueueSnackbar` API stays compatible.","tree":{"sha":"ad4962204e6a688c09ef08f5b7e4fe72f6743563","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/ad4962204e6a688c09ef08f5b7e4fe72f6743563"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/b99496205a23a3a880a68a7d8080f73af4b002fc","verification":{"payload":"tree ad4962204e6a688c09ef08f5b7e4fe72f6743563\nparent 6d98456d58459917639b34b4ea17fd669cfd198b\nauthor Raphaël Bosi <71827178+bosiraphael@users.noreply.github.com> 1789564285 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789564285 +0000\n\nReplace frontend snackbars with twenty-ui toasts (#25664)\n\nMoves frontend notifications into `twenty-ui` and removes the snackbar\nmanager abstraction.\n\n`useToast()` exposes `enqueueToast` and `closeToast`, with queue limits,\ndeduplication, and exit animations. A Base UI store keeps toast state\nisolated per provider.\n\n`mountedToasterCount` tracks mounted `<Toaster>` renderers separately\nfrom the toast array: a renderer can have an empty queue, and toasts can\nbe queued before any renderer mounts. Dismissed toasts remain for exit\nanimations while a renderer is mounted and are removed immediately\notherwise. When the last renderer unmounts, unfinished exits are removed\nand visible toasts are preserved. Using a count keeps this cleanup\ncorrect when multiple renderers share a provider.\n\nError formatting and translations remain in the frontend. The SDK’s\n`enqueueSnackbar` API stays compatible.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----B