ser_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/6d98456d58459917639b34b4ea17fd669cfd198b","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDZkOTg0NTZkNTg0NTk5MTc2MzliMzRiNGVhMTdmZDY2OWNmZDE5OGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/1e9afea6c0d0c9b9a0ae64afe4b19f2f90bc2347","sha":"1e9afea6c0d0c9b9a0ae64afe4b19f2f90bc2347","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/1e9afea6c0d0c9b9a0ae64afe4b19f2f90bc2347"}],"sha":"6d98456d58459917639b34b4ea17fd669cfd198b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/6d98456d58459917639b34b4ea17fd669cfd198b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/1e9afea6c0d0c9b9a0ae64afe4b19f2f90bc2347/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:03:06Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T13:03:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Export row-level permission predicates and groups (#25984)\n\nStacked on #25975 (roles export).\n\n## What\n\n`exportApplication` now writes an application''s row-level permission\npredicates and predicate groups under their role, instead of reporting\nthem as unsupported:\n\n- **Predicate groups:** `logicalOperator` and the object are always\nwritten; `parentPredicateGroupUniversalIdentifier` and `position` only\nwhen set.\n- **Predicates:** the object, field and `operand` are always written.\n`value`, `subFieldName`, the workspace member field and subfield,\n`predicateGroupUniversalIdentifier` and `position` are written only when\nset. `value` is written as stored, so a JSON string stays a string and\nan object stays an object.\n\nA group or predicate is reported unsupported instead of exported when:\n- its role belongs to another application;\n- its object, field or workspace member field is unsupported or does not\nexist;\n- the group it belongs to, or its parent group, is not exported under\nthe same role. That covers groups that are unsupported, soft-deleted,\nmissing, on another role, or in a parent cycle, and the rule cascades\ndown the tree.\n\nSoft-deleted predicates and groups, which the settings page leaves\nbehind when you remove a rule, are not written. They keep their existing\n`EXCLUDED` coverage row.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- Like view filter values, a predicate `value` can hold record ids from\nthe workspace it was exported from (for example `selectedRecordIds` on a\nrelation field). Re-applying in the same workspace works; applying to\nanother workspace keeps ids that point nowhere.\n- Soft-deleted predicates and groups are left out of the manifest, so a\nsync with deletions inferred hard-deletes them. They are already\ninactive, so nothing changes at runtime, and an additive sync\n(`--no-delete`) plans nothing. Deletion inference does not skip\nsoft-deleted rows for any kind today; that is left for a follow-up.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Inverse converter specs (both kinds):** manifest to flat and back is\nidentical, flat to manifest and back has no diff, unset properties are\nomitted, and values such as `false`, `0`, an empty string, a JSON string\nand an array are kept as they are.\n- **`reconstruct-roles-manifest.util.spec.ts`:**\n  - a nested group tree with a predicate;\n  - an unsupported object cascading to child groups and predicates;\n  - an unsupported field and workspace member field;\n  - a role outside the application;\n  - missing, soft-deleted and cyclic parent groups;\n- one coverage row per row, with soft-deleted rows left to the\nclassifier.\n- **Compared-properties guard:** covers both kinds.\n- **Export integration spec:**\n- The test application role now has a two-level group tree and a\npredicate. The manifest and coverage snapshots are updated, and the\nadditive dry run still returns no actions.\n- The Custom application role case adds a group and two predicates\nthrough the metadata API, then removes one. The export contains the\ngroup and the remaining predicate, reports the removed one as excluded,\nand re-syncs with no actions.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25984?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"d1f21b78986be5739bf495ca7fea28c89263ea42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/d1f21b78986be5739bf495ca7fea28c89263ea42"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/1e9afea6c0d0c9b9a0ae64afe4b19f2f90bc2347","verification":{"payload":"tree d1f21b78986be5739bf495ca7fea28c89263ea42\nparent 4092e47b5197994c2a3c5cb74eaec3948152b5f9\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789563786 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789563786 +0000\n\nExport row-level permission predicates and groups (#25984)\n\nStacked on #25975 (roles export).\n\n## What\n\n`exportApplication` now writes an application''s row-level permission\npredicates and predicate groups under their role, instead of reporting\nthem as unsupported:\n\n- **Predicate groups:** `logicalOperator` and the object are always\nwritten; `parentPredicateGroupUniversalIdentifier` and `position` only\nwhen set.\n- **Predicates:** the object, field and `operand` are always written.\n`value`, `subFieldName`, the workspace member field and subfield,\n`predicateGroupUniversalIdentifier` and `position` are written only when\nset. `value` is written as stored, so a JSON string stays a string and\nan object stays an object.\n\nA group or predicate is reported unsupported instead of exported when:\n- its role belongs to another application;\n- its object, field or workspace member field is unsupported or does not\nexist;\n- the group it belongs to, or its parent group, is not exported under\nthe same role. That covers groups that are unsupported, soft-deleted,\nmissing, on another role, or in a parent cycle, and the rule cascades\ndown the tree.\n\nSoft-deleted predicates and groups, which the settings page leaves\nbehind when you remove a rule, are not written. They keep their existing\n`EXCLUDED` coverage row.\n\n## Known limitations\n\n- Like view filter values, a predicate `value` can hold record ids from\nthe workspace it was exported from (for example `selectedRecordIds` on a\nrelation field). Re-applying in the same workspace works; applying to\nanother workspace keeps ids that point nowhere.\n- Soft-deleted predicates and groups are left out of the manifest, so a\nsync with deletions inferred hard-deletes them. They are already\ninactive, so nothing changes at runtime, and an additive sync\n(`--no-delete`) plans nothing. Deletion inference does not skip\nsoft-deleted rows for any kind today; that is left for a follow-up.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Inverse converter specs (both kinds):** manifest to flat and back is\nidentical, flat to manifest and back has no diff, unset properties are\nomitted, and values such as `false`, `0`, an empty string, a JSON string\nand an array are kept as they are.\n- **`reconstruct-roles-manifest.util.spec.ts`:**\n  - a nested group tree with a predicate;\n  - an unsupported object cascading to child groups and predicates;\n  - an unsupported field and workspace member field;\n  - a role outside the application;\n  - missing, soft-deleted and cyclic parent groups;\n- one coverage row per row, with soft-deleted rows left to the\nclassifier.\n- **Compared-properties guard:** covers both kinds.\n- **Export integration spec:**\n- The test application role now has a two-level group tree and a\npredicate. The manifest and coverage snapshots are updated, and the\nadditive dry run still returns no actions.\n- The Custom application role case adds a group and two predicates\nthrough the metadata API, then removes one. The export contains the\ngroup and the remaining predicate, reports the removed one as excluded,\nand re-syncs with no actions.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25984?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqpOaC