jk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/c7955dc991c850dda60a21456d09a9eb5c3e4189","sha":"c7955dc991c850dda60a21456d09a9eb5c3e4189","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/c7955dc991c850dda60a21456d09a9eb5c3e4189"}],"sha":"4092e47b5197994c2a3c5cb74eaec3948152b5f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/4092e47b5197994c2a3c5cb74eaec3948152b5f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1834158?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/Weiko","id":1834158,"login":"Weiko","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MzQxNTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Weiko","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/c7955dc991c850dda60a21456d09a9eb5c3e4189/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:38:38Z","email":"corentin@twenty.com","name":"Weiko"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:38:38Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Export roles, permissions and permission flags (#25975)\n\nStacked on #25966 (derived permission identifiers). Without it, a role\ncreated in the UI could not be exported and re-applied, because its\npermission identifiers would collide.\n\n## What\n\n`exportApplication` now reconstructs the application''s roles and the\npermission flags it declares, instead of reporting them as unsupported:\n\n- **Roles:** every capability flag and assignability flag is written\nout, plus `description` and `icon` when set.\n- **Object and field permissions:** nested under their role. Permission\nbooleans that are unset are omitted.\n- **Role permission flags:** folded into the role''s\n`permissionFlagUniversalIdentifiers`, sorted, pointing at either a\nstandard flag or one of the application''s own flags.\n- **Permission flags declared by the application:** always with their\n`permissionType`.\n\nEvery application-owned role, object permission, field permission, role\npermission flag and permission flag gets exactly one coverage row. A\npermission is reported unsupported instead of exported when:\n- its role belongs to another application;\n- its object or field belongs to the application but is itself\nunsupported;\n- its object, field or flag does not exist.\n\nStill unsupported in this PR:\n- row-level permission predicates and groups (next PR, before the SDK\nwrites roles);\n- agent role assignments.\n\nMember and API key role assignments stay excluded.\n\n## Round-trip fix\n\nObject permission booleans are nullable columns, but a manifest can only\nomit them. The forward converter turned an omitted boolean into\n`undefined`, which never equals the stored `null`, so an object\npermission with an unset boolean diffed forever.\n\nThe converter now defaults to `null`, and `ObjectPermissionEntity` types\nthe four booleans as `boolean | null` like `FieldPermissionEntity`. The\nchange is type-only: the columns are unchanged.\n\n## Default role\n\n`application.defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier` keeps its current value.\nFor the workspace Custom application, whose own `defaultRoleId` is null,\nthat is still the Admin placeholder.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Inverse converter parity specs (four converters):** manifest to flat\nand back, and flat to manifest and back with no diff, including unset\nbooleans.\n- **`reconstruct-roles-manifest.util.spec.ts`:**\n  - nesting and flag sorting;\n  - a permission on a role outside the application;\n  - references to an unsupported or missing object, field or flag;\n  - exactly one coverage row per row.\n- **Compared-properties guard:** now covers role, object permission,\nfield permission, role permission flag and permission flag.\n- **Export integration spec:**\n- The test application now declares a permission flag, and its role has\nan object permission, a field permission and flag references. The\nmanifest and coverage snapshots are updated, and the additive dry run\nstill returns no actions.\n- A new Custom application case creates a role with object, field and\nflag permissions through the metadata API, exports it, and re-syncs it\nwith no actions.\n- **Migrations:** the type change on `ObjectPermissionEntity` produces\nno schema change; `database:migrate:generate` reports none.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25975?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"1d36952fa25aa41202fbc2979443da09d51d9ae9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/1d36952fa25aa41202fbc2979443da09d51d9ae9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/c7955dc991c850dda60a21456d09a9eb5c3e4189","verification":{"payload":"tree 1d36952fa25aa41202fbc2979443da09d51d9ae9\nparent 8bc36528d5acda7f07ab38c288e1b025a6ec345b\nauthor Weiko <corentin@twenty.com> 1789562318 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789562318 +0000\n\nExport roles, permissions and permission flags (#25975)\n\nStacked on #25966 (derived permission identifiers). Without it, a role\ncreated in the UI could not be exported and re-applied, because its\npermission identifiers would collide.\n\n## What\n\n`exportApplication` now reconstructs the application''s roles and the\npermission flags it declares, instead of reporting them as unsupported:\n\n- **Roles:** every capability flag and assignability flag is written\nout, plus `description` and `icon` when set.\n- **Object and field permissions:** nested under their role. Permission\nbooleans that are unset are omitted.\n- **Role permission flags:** folded into the role''s\n`permissionFlagUniversalIdentifiers`, sorted, pointing at either a\nstandard flag or one of the application''s own flags.\n- **Permission flags declared by the application:** always with their\n`permissionType`.\n\nEvery application-owned role, object permission, field permission, role\npermission flag and permission flag gets exactly one coverage row. A\npermission is reported unsupported instead of exported when:\n- its role belongs to another application;\n- its object or field belongs to the application but is itself\nunsupported;\n- its object, field or flag does not exist.\n\nStill unsupported in this PR:\n- row-level permission predicates and groups (next PR, before the SDK\nwrites roles);\n- agent role assignments.\n\nMember and API key role assignments stay excluded.\n\n## Round-trip fix\n\nObject permission booleans are nullable columns, but a manifest can only\nomit them. The forward converter turned an omitted boolean into\n`undefined`, which never equals the stored `null`, so an object\npermission with an unset boolean diffed forever.\n\nThe converter now defaults to `null`, and `ObjectPermissionEntity` types\nthe four booleans as `boolean | null` like `FieldPermissionEntity`. The\nchange is type-only: the columns are unchanged.\n\n## Default role\n\n`application.defaultRoleUniversalIdentifier` keeps its current value.\nFor the workspace Custom application, whose own `defaultRoleId` is null,\nthat is still the Admin placeholder.\n\n## Tests\n\n- **Inverse converter parity specs (four converters):** manifest to flat\nand back, and flat to manifest and back with no diff, including unset\nbooleans.\n- **`reconstruct-roles-manifest.util.spec.ts`:**\n  - nesting and flag sorting;\n  - a permission on a role outside the application;\n  - references to an unsupported or missing object, field or flag;\n  - exactly one coverage row per row.\n- **Compared-properties guard:** now covers role, object permission,\nfield permission, role permission flag and permission flag.\n- **Export integration spec:**\n- The test application now declares a permission flag, and its role has\nan object permission, a field permission and flag references. The\nmanifest and coverage snapshots are updated, and the additive dry run\nstill returns no actions.\n- A new Custom application case creates a role with object, field and\nflag permissions through the metadata API, exports it, and re-syncs it\nwith no actions.\n- **Migrations:** the type change on `ObjectPermissionEntity` produces\nno schema change; `database:migrate:generate` reports none.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25975?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN 