cross those merged changes.\n\n- Give Companion constants, types, utilities, and handlers their own\nfiles, with matching names and adjacent tests. Keep the SDK-required\napplication-config.ts entry point.\n- Separate logic-function registrations from their handlers, preserving\nall entity identifiers, routes, and behavior.\n- Split Button, IconButton, and AnimatedPlaceholder types into\nindividual files and update consumers. Preserve the public\ntwenty-ui/input and twenty-ui/feedback exports.\n- Consolidate the identical APP_DISPLAY_NAME constants and split the\nintegration-test setup/teardown files.\n\nValidation: 298 Companion unit tests pass; Companion, UI, and desktop\ntypechecks pass; scoped lint passes; the SDK manifest/application build\nand desktop production build pass. A structural comparison confirms all\n191 app declarations retain their logic. Live server installation was\nnot rerun.\n\nStack: #25632 and #25633 are merged. Merge #25616 → #25900 → this PR.\nThis PR targets #25900’s branch so its diff contains only this cleanup.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25977?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"1fba33a6adea4aadcb5b4f47caf27e421c976a04","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/1fba33a6adea4aadcb5b4f47caf27e421c976a04"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/8bc36528d5acda7f07ab38c288e1b025a6ec345b","verification":{"payload":"tree 1fba33a6adea4aadcb5b4f47caf27e421c976a04\nparent 0de4040d62ab50908706822b0996e3e9f46d61e8\nauthor Thomas des Francs <tdesfrancs@gmail.com> 1789562285 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789562285 +0000\n\nDesktop Recorder: align merged integration and UI naming conventions (#25977)\n\nThe merged Desktop Recorder changes in #25632 and #25633 still grouped\nexports and used filenames that did not follow the frontend conventions.\nThis follow-up addresses Félix’s request across those merged changes.\n\n- Give Companion constants, types, utilities, and handlers their own\nfiles, with matching names and adjacent tests. Keep the SDK-required\napplication-config.ts entry point.\n- Separate logic-function registrations from their handlers, preserving\nall entity identifiers, routes, and behavior.\n- Split Button, IconButton, and AnimatedPlaceholder types into\nindividual files and update consumers. Preserve the public\ntwenty-ui/input and twenty-ui/feedback exports.\n- Consolidate the identical APP_DISPLAY_NAME constants and split the\nintegration-test setup/teardown files.\n\nValidation: 298 Companion unit tests pass; Companion, UI, and desktop\ntypechecks pass; scoped lint passes; the SDK manifest/application build\nand desktop production build pass. A structural comparison confirms all\n191 app declarations retain their logic. Live server installation was\nnot rerun.\n\nStack: #25632 and #25633 are merged. Merge #25616 → #25900 → this PR.\nThis PR targets #25900’s branch so its diff contains only this cleanup.\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/25977?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img