er}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/prastoin","id":45004772,"login":"prastoin","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MDA0Nzcy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/prastoin","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/3c3615daae519cdfc9e9777f6094a648e6e46d72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T08:34:26Z","email":"45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Paul Rastoin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T08:34:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(upgrade): pin 2.20 messageList view command to its original columns (#26006)\n\nFixes #25993\n\n## Problem\n\n`upgrade:2-20:create-message-list-view` read its column list from the\ncurrent `STANDARD_OBJECTS.messageList.views.allMessageLists.viewFields`.\nThat definition now includes the `description` column, which was added\nlater along with the `messageList.description` field by\n`upgrade:2-39:sync-message-list-record-page`.\n\nA workspace upgrading from before 2.20 runs the 2.20 command first, so\nit tried to create the `description` view field before the 2.39 command\nhad created the field metadata and failed with `INVALID_VIEW_DATA /\nField metadata not found`, aborting the whole workspace upgrade.\n\n## Fix\n\nPin the 2.20 command to the four columns the view had at the time:\n`name`, `members`, `campaigns`, `createdAt`. The `description` column\nstays with the 2.39 command, which already creates it when missing.\n\nThe spec uses the same pinned list, seeds the standard maps with\n`description` present so the mocks mirror the real standard application,\nand adds a test asserting the 2.20 command never creates the\n`description` column.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Spec passes (6 tests); dry run now reports 4 view columns, matching\nthe workaround the reporter validated on a real 2.18 instance.\n- oxlint with the type-aware server config reports 0 errors on both\nfiles.\n- Server typecheck shows no errors in the 2-20 files.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_019DFU2jivSWxPFxFuXkQpmK)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26006?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","tree":{"sha":"e3a34c98976e01b87a613c5088bed572c2b093e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/e3a34c98976e01b87a613c5088bed572c2b093e2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/3c3615daae519cdfc9e9777f6094a648e6e46d72","verification":{"payload":"tree e3a34c98976e01b87a613c5088bed572c2b093e2\nparent b56329258f2cd013f456aa0b4ff406d270eb4ff0\nauthor Paul Rastoin <45004772+prastoin@users.noreply.github.com> 1789547666 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789547666 +0000\n\nfix(upgrade): pin 2.20 messageList view command to its original columns (#26006)\n\nFixes #25993\n\n## Problem\n\n`upgrade:2-20:create-message-list-view` read its column list from the\ncurrent `STANDARD_OBJECTS.messageList.views.allMessageLists.viewFields`.\nThat definition now includes the `description` column, which was added\nlater along with the `messageList.description` field by\n`upgrade:2-39:sync-message-list-record-page`.\n\nA workspace upgrading from before 2.20 runs the 2.20 command first, so\nit tried to create the `description` view field before the 2.39 command\nhad created the field metadata and failed with `INVALID_VIEW_DATA /\nField metadata not found`, aborting the whole workspace upgrade.\n\n## Fix\n\nPin the 2.20 command to the four columns the view had at the time:\n`name`, `members`, `campaigns`, `createdAt`. The `description` column\nstays with the 2.39 command, which already creates it when missing.\n\nThe spec uses the same pinned list, seeds the standard maps with\n`description` present so the mocks mirror the real standard application,\nand adds a test asserting the 2.20 command never creates the\n`description` column.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Spec passes (6 tests); dry run now reports 4 view columns, matching\nthe workaround the reporter validated on a real 2.18 instance.\n- oxlint with the type-aware server config reports 0 errors on both\nfiles.\n- Server typecheck shows no errors in the 2-20 files.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude\nCode](https://claude.ai/code/session_019DFU2jivSWxPFxFuXkQpmK)_\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated description by cubic. -->\n<a\nhref=\"https://cubic.dev/pr/twentyhq/twenty/pull/26006?utm_source=github\"\ntarget=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\ndata-no-image-dialog=\"true\"><picture><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"><source\nmedia=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\"\nsrcset=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-light.svg\"><img\nalt=\"Review in cubic\"\nsrc=\"https://www.cubic.dev/buttons/review-in-cubic-dark.svg\"></picture></a>\n<!-- End of auto-generated description by cubic. -->","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqlSiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAWRMQAK5ZruYqDGJ+8EuDd4roK/zr\nQDAMwA0qeSRg7Mc7iSTrA9lsIgXYr0MUGjekw2GZdSUGdgNfTzCMVJnISzRo9/mH\nwgIM7tFbQF634gSGMYSoagjqUVHnjvFVGVzrzp85GV4etISCS/6yvpthv8+M3VMc\nuChznznLMGSuDWW7TDyccLLFXhspdDyEQzpV5BJEUJvYTXGsA0qVLLSAqqKS61j/\nnQSXXaZgNxMsilj1qhpqEK5AeG5O1D1Lmrckd2IvWiEaLOYxBRtgdaLXqu10Hgxe\nVUu0OnvQQCa1RWSVttGqAcKGtYlE2w7VfkuIbNVHwbGWmBfq+ptdlWtjJbkw0C+p\nTdisHotuCbj38EfkOdjmjj6FqVXI1lrZnguniXbF4B8HTAVrTaqfwkF0yCwfmf1i\n6D5eHF5w/LWJowSgs/ZWpkEUJkdAnUji2r5djlYlnILhHKWlxcy/ZPRLsmZ+9niX\nqwaZkNIjFoXI77axqsdm3eeimf43hWGq8ETT2CLt5anFXgM1s7J+g7CR5geShM1C\nxh+UBMuzMviJ+a8XsLJDYc6uuFafZNpTaYuGp54GZe1szsFCAS+qh6sLf2FzL1Sv\nfXVpxWOIiLo+38Wul8sAWeZS3bj39lMMukI8MuLv95y4FRJCQ8f0nFQuqiC3Cpm7\nUnMofMqm6q3J2q8t8m9E\n=RgPN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/3c3615daae519cdfc9e9777f6094a648e6e46d72","node_id":"C_kwDOUmZXItoAKDNjMzYxNWRhYWU1MTljZGZjOWU5Nzc3ZjYwOTRhNjQ4ZTZlNDZkNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commit/b56329258f2cd013f456aa0b4ff406d270eb4ff0","sha":"b56329258f2cd013f456aa0b4ff406d270eb4ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/b56329258f2cd013f456aa0b4ff406d270eb4ff0"}],"sha":"3c3615daae519cdfc9e9777f6094a648e6e46d72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/3c3615daae519cdfc9e9777f6094a648e6e46d72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12035771?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/charlesBochet","id":12035771,"login":"charlesBochet","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMDM1Nzcx","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/charlesBochet","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/commits/b56329258f2cd013f456aa0b4ff406d270eb4ff0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T08:22:46Z","email":"charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Charles Bochet"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T08:22:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Require client authentication for OAuth token introspection (#26023)\n\n## What\n\nThe RFC 7662 token introspection endpoint (`POST /oauth/introspect`)\nonly verified a client secret when one was supplied. A confidential\nclient''s token metadata (active status, subject, scope, workspace,\nexpiry) could therefore be introspected with just the public `client_id`\nand no secret.\n\n## Why\n\nRFC 7662 §2.1 requires the introspection endpoint to authenticate the\ncaller, and the discovery document already advertises\n`introspection_endpoint_auth_methods_supported: [\"client_secret_post\"]`\n— but introspection did not enforce it. The authorization-code grant\n(`exchangeAuthorizationCode`) and the refresh-token grant\n(`refreshTokenGrant`) both already reject a confidential client that\nomits its secret; introspection was the one grant missing that gate.\nWithout it, the endpoint is a token-validity oracle and an\ninformation-disclosure vector for any holder of a valid token plus the\n(public) `client_id`.\n\n## How\n\n`introspectToken` now rejects a confidential client (one with\n`oAuthClientSecretHash`) that presents no non-empty secret, returning `{\nactive: false }` before any token is validated — so nothing about the\ntoken can leak. Public clients (no secret) are unaffected. The\nconfidential-client check is a shared `isConfidentialClient` predicate\nwith unit coverage.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nRequest — note there is no `client_secret`, only the public `client_id`:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://<host>/oauth/introspect \\\n  -H ''Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded'' \\\n  --data-urlencode ''token=<a valid access or refresh token>'' \\\n  --data-urlencode ''client_id=<the confidential client_id>''\n```\n\nBefore — the token''s metadata is returned:\n\n```json\n{\"active\":true,\"sub\":\"...\",\"client_id\":\"...\",\"token_type\":\"Bearer\",\"scope\":\"api profile\",\"aud\":\"<workspaceId>\",\"iss\":\"...\",\"exp\":...,\"iat\":...}\n```\n\nAfter — nothing is disclosed:\n\n```json\n{\"active\":false}\n```\n\nScope: the existing cross-client check already limits introspection to\ntokens issued to the supplied `client_id`, and public clients are\nunchanged, so no legitimate flow is affected.","tree":{"sha":"35fe183632f9fa617edb7e0e0893ddbf02894fd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/trees/35fe183632f9fa617edb7e0e0893ddbf02894fd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Desync-ai/twenty-desync/git/commits/b56329258f2cd013f456aa0b4ff406d270eb4ff0","verification":{"payload":"tree 35fe183632f9fa617edb7e0e0893ddbf02894fd3\nparent 733f4b53581de88ed38bb9628d001126c3fb3cad\nauthor Charles Bochet <charlesBochet@users.noreply.github.com> 1789546966 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789546966 +0000\n\nRequire client authentication for OAuth token introspection (#26023)\n\n## What\n\nThe RFC 7662 token introspection endpoint (`POST /oauth/introspect`)\nonly verified a client secret when one was supplied. A confidential\nclient''s token metadata (active status, subject, scope, workspace,\nexpiry) could therefore be introspected with just the public `client_id`\nand no secret.\n\n## Why\n\nRFC 7662 §2.1 requires the introspection endpoint to authenticate the\ncaller, and the discovery document already advertises\n`introspection_endpoint_auth_methods_supported: [\"client_secret_post\"]`\n— but introspection did not enforce it. The authorization-code grant\n(`exchangeAuthorizationCode`) and the refresh-token grant\n(`refreshTokenGrant`) both already reject a confidential client that\nomits its secret; introspection was the one grant missing that gate.\nWithout it, the endpoint is a token-validity oracle and an\ninformation-disclosure vector for any holder of a valid token plus the\n(public) `client_id`.\n\n## How\n\n`introspectToken` now rejects a confidential client (one with\n`oAuthClientSecretHash`) that presents no non-empty secret, returning `{\nactive: false }` before any token is validated — so nothing about the\ntoken can leak. Public clients (no secret) are unaffected. The\nconfidential-client check is a shared `isConfidentialClient` predicate\nwith unit coverage.\n\n## Reproduction\n\nRequest — note there is no `client_secret`, only the public `client_id`:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://<host>/oauth/introspect \\\n  -H ''Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded'' \\\n  --data-urlencode ''token=<a valid access or refresh token>'' \\\n  --data-urlencode ''client_id=<the confidential client_id>''\n```\n\nBefore — the token''s metadata is returned:\n\n```json\n{\"active\":true,\"sub\":\"...\",\"client_id\":\"...\",\"token_type\":\"Bearer\",\"scope\":\"api profile\",\"aud\":\"<workspaceId>\",\"iss\":\"...\",\"exp\":...,\"iat\":...}\n```\n\nAfter — nothing is disclosed:\n\n```json\n{\"active\":false}\n```\n\nScope: the existing cross-client check already limits introspection to\ntokens issued to the supplied `client_id`, and public clients are\nunchanged, so no legitimate flow is affected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqlHdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAqtoQAK29C0+meBFXdcboOOMmy3yH\nBH6OCXOYg9mBHSLJLJ5+9m4cA32Y4IXLbf4TRaNau0KgLZyPXGcG7gK+HdmSvhQy\n8oQdQJukkXPLzLYVBDQ3rESDKnMiKOU7FdVNQz3ww7yK250bnZcR2WuMAnYe8UmL\nj9ZtrBZGGq3BlczbUZW/e8UsBYp1utvnDW0ZSA2xUqT8uc9PeQT1ZO1cwZzXyXij\nFW+5kB5bdyPNv4C7clR+1v9k4TetzwC1tC/GBNKAnozpuyYxs95TbTLdw6N1rXNt\n5fhzyWUzhX/n7bHGgtAwGIfoKl/uN5QBfBwP85WdZai3fhIiNtn4HG/sirOJ594+\n/6VNuTRJAUXWJ+hh9Vv2YxrpoYvHKYDJgU3+O9yLg2vKeFUIRZj48cwyXglh7w2t\nT/6vvv1SMNK6B/+HYUvSf/pcpFAgqKkgALNd5dvqS68ewG+Acf2BpMEZwVvdP6+U\nGHERwTqiSoqnwvF1I4Hf7VLrLq+nIhLWlLvnlQfwnvuJqALWb0tORK5UVx/04D6q\nA5/VFSuxYBdR8FKulFFpsqCQgkNoo3H5UM3B8lmdBagdBx7rJXRGxSFYFtwtKjHD\nnWZmF6M7M9U/bXh67B3zz1yQUci/xXTdfjg+dYBTshqN+2yPN5PKi6jOXNWfCnmc\nUYAJb1PH2ao7lky2RQoO\n=BbK7\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T22:58:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_u