ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/42e2bafcd9689f5be434a9a2888c6e9d15d3b8b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:58:49Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:58:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(asyncapi): let the CloudEvent type pattern accept a .v<N> suffix (#56)\n\nADR 0016 publishes NetworkOrderAcknowledged as the breaking v2 type (NetworkOrderAcknowledged.v2), but the shared CloudEvent schema''s type pattern ended at the event name, so the AsyncAPI document was invalid against its own examples. The AsyncAPI generator rejected it (warehouse-docs could not build this context''s event reference); this repo''s Spectral job only lints the OpenAPI so it never noticed.\n\nAllow an optional .v<N> suffix in the pattern and document it.","tree":{"sha":"71edc3601dab24351d67e6e6b7eccf774bab2d67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/71edc3601dab24351d67e6e6b7eccf774bab2d67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/