ira@gmail.com","name":"claudioed"},"message":"docs(executive): add executive briefing deck\n\nAdds `executive/index.html`: a self-contained reveal.js executive deck covering strategy, architecture, observability, competitive position and next steps for this repo. Open it in a browser (loads reveal.js 6.0.0 from jsDelivr, pinned with an SRI hash; no vendored library code in this repo); no build step. Full source text is in the speaker notes (press S).\n\nNo code, config, workflow or chart changes; the folder is outside `.github/`, `charts/` and the docs site, so `repo_lint` and the docs build are unaffected. Fleet-wide gap analysis lives in `warehouse-docs/executive/competitive-gaps.html`.","tree":{"sha":"adb773b02a30c87484f9ec1fbbe0da00dc3a513f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/adb773b02a30c87484f9ec1fbbe0da00dc3a513f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/5bb9c661d6a859e731e6d7f7ba3b4789175d3184","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/5bb9c661d6a859e731e6d7f7ba3b4789175d3184","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDViYjljNjYxZDZhODU5ZTczMWU2ZDdmN2JhM2I0Nzg5MTc1ZDMxODQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/083a316701e8001cba6084b220f5bdbcc03bbd09","sha":"083a316701e8001cba6084b220f5bdbcc03bbd09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/083a316701e8001cba6084b220f5bdbcc03bbd09"}],"sha":"5bb9c661d6a859e731e6d7f7ba3b4789175d3184","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/5bb9c661d6a859e731e6d7f7ba3b4789175d3184"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/083a316701e8001cba6084b220f5bdbcc03bbd09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:31:50Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T23:31:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: NetworkOrderSubmitted + settle-time NetworkOrderAcknowledged; cycle-time eligibility (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#53)\n\n* feat(events): NetworkOrderSubmitted at SUBMITTED; NetworkOrderAcknowledged only on settle (v2)\n\nReceiveNetworkDemand now raises NetworkOrderSubmitted (what the old\nAcknowledged announced). ReconcileSubmittedOrders raises\nNetworkOrderAcknowledged in the same atomic scope as the\nSUBMITTED -> ACKNOWLEDGED save. Acknowledged is published as the\nbreaking-change v2 wire type (\".v2\" type suffix + \":v2\" dataschema) on\nthe integration and analytics topics through the outbox; Submitted is v1.\n\nThe analytics projector handles Submitted (claimed, no report effect),\nAcknowledged v2 and the historic v1 (same counter, same latency, so a\nreplay keeps the report numbers). Tests: unit (use cases, wire goldens,\nconsumer) and a testcontainers Kafka+Postgres projector test with a v1\nreplay.\n\n* feat(capability): a path is eligible for a cutoff only if CycleTimeP95 <= cutoff - now\n\nthroughputFeasible now honours the cycle-time input ADR 0001 names: paths\nwhose CycleTimeP95 exceeds the time left to the cutoff are excluded from\nthe summed remaining capacity. Missing/zero cycle time stays eligible\n(fail-open); no capacity scaling. If every path is ruled out by cycle\ntime the offer is a proven zero (THROUGHPUT_CONSTRAINED), not the\nphysical fallback.\n\n* docs: ADRs 0016/0017, AsyncAPI v2 Acknowledged + Submitted, DDD pages (audit decisions 2026-10-06)\n\n- ADR 0016 (NetworkOrderSubmitted + settle-time Acknowledged v2) and\n  ADR 0017 (CycleTimeP95 eligibility), registered in the ADR index.\n- apis/asyncapi.yaml: NetworkOrderSubmitted v1, NetworkOrderAcknowledged\n  .v2 type/:v2 dataschema on both channels, projector behaviour.\n- docs/ddd: domain-events, eventstorming (hotspots resolved, diagrams\n  fixed), sequence/message-flow/class diagrams, aggregate and bounded\n  context canvases, ubiquitous language.","tree":{"sha":"ce9ba79576478154243ae76b574417af1d48ce22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/ce9ba79576478154243ae76b574417af1d48ce22"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/083a316701e8001cba6084b220f5bdbcc03bbd09","verification":{"payload":"tree ce9ba79576478154243ae76b574417af1d48ce22\nparent fa8c1c56b8063e1aa2cd5a072d8142afa85f8ba9\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791329510 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791329510 -0300\n\nfeat: NetworkOrderSubmitted + settle-time NetworkOrderAcknowledged; cycle-time eligibility (audit decisions 2026-10-06) (#53)\n\n* feat(events): NetworkOrderSubmitted at SUBMITTED; NetworkOrderAcknowledged only on settle (v2)\n\nReceiveNetworkDemand now raises NetworkOrderSubmitted (what the old\nAcknowledged announced). ReconcileSubmittedOrders raises\nNetworkOrderAcknowledged in the same atomic scope as the\nSUBMITTED -> ACKNOWLEDGED save. Acknowledged is published as the\nbreaking-change v2 wire type (\".v2\" type suffix + \":v2\" dataschema) on\nthe integration and analytics topics through the outbox; Submitted is v1.\n\nThe analytics projector handles Submitted (claimed, no report effect),\nAcknowledged v2 and the historic v1 (same counter, same latency, so a\nreplay keeps the report numbers). Tests: unit (use cases, wire goldens,\nconsumer) and a testcontainers Kafka+Postgres projector test with a v1\nreplay.\n\n* feat(capability): a path is eligible for a cutoff only if CycleTimeP95 <= cutoff - now\n\nthroughputFeasible now honours the cycle-time input ADR 0001 names: paths\nwhose CycleTimeP95 exceeds the time left to the cutoff are excluded from\nthe summed remaining capacity. Missing/zero cycle time stays eligible\n(fail-open); no capacity scaling. If every path is ruled out by cycle\ntime the offer is a proven zero (THROUGHPUT_CONSTRAINED), not the\nphysical fallback.\n\n* docs: ADRs 0016/0017, AsyncAPI v2 Acknowledged + Submitted, DDD pages (audit decisions 2026-10-06)\n\n- ADR 0016 (NetworkOrderSubmitted + settle-time Acknowledged v2) and\n  ADR 0017 (CycleTimeP95 eligibility), registered in the ADR index.\n- apis/asyncapi.yaml: NetworkOrderSubmitted v1, NetworkOrderAcknowledged\n  .v2 type/:v2 dataschema on both channels, projector behaviour.\n- docs/ddd: domain-events, eventstorming (hotspots resolved, diagrams\n  fixed), sequence/message-flow/class diagrams, aggregate and bounded\n  context canvases, ubiquitous language.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxYTmCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9zcQAFq4N7h7za3J1/pGekqUw4Ah\nGOvnhkegUi0fk07m5xUAXaShVZ0T9uNo7h7VDuaGfuoyIw2g2LNxg6/A9EEMdIJB\nQXlIMbqphAwxks2DJmo/Gjk0yuIb3c8Lw3C3rfHSTLQjbTLppR8EcLus57tfFYBG\nf11LZeq2YanYXXYDPbvnS4qCsJe/zgWnddjDXNoipbNPqEUlZEwf9hnk2k8oceJI\n4uIhVYCQfsc+tWSrK1rCjxfm/perSHPfSp9NVL8Qr+ZnpbCIIn6NRo5vS3cmLXmh\nrnt4fYsVlaSzUK1iDMkK1aYxH9Pn5FsnX6jJRYzejVh3yCJVM7FHI3XOlrRcgT6h\nE4PfiSy66Z3sdYQjLakTdebyt/jjbNzJLzJSCBJg/oiQarXGg8QLpMsDZlUehnjB\n9Bz1+iEAPQJsZSgY9x4JG5/Tw0Su1V8cM+51aaE71HbZaCpowKPbPM2F9CmF2XVQ\n6CO9hTlKR9jcb1z3UvXBXqodOugY7BY4gBBlc1HAYzFcl+G0j7ZT4gwLQ2R0ykfU\n41i4ZbdmX97viWsUVTvUlDsOEuPpJJvOdi5oHKQt0J3UvqnfHBP/Af5TwuakJ2a8\nUk4yv561LYlfq2HO1yg99bkMezMWPIe1ErUAi0RWZtP4d/1zj2XV/AZCS8b7+y9e\n3kXYtduLWZjz85ZqkF7m\n=cwzl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T23:31:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/us