hubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/7bdd6eaed730f126d3870ae101449850d6b7c365/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:35:16Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T14:35:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#50)\n\n* fix(http): map ErrConfirmBeforeAcknowledge to 409 and allow POST in CORS\n\nPOST /network-orders/{ref}/shipment-confirmation on an order that is not\nACKNOWLEDGED returned 500 internal-error because statusFor/problemFor had\nno case for ErrConfirmBeforeAcknowledge. Map it to 409 with its own\nproblem type (confirm-before-acknowledge). CORS allowed only GET/OPTIONS,\nso the browser could not call the new POST cross-origin; allow POST.\n\nTests: TestHandleConfirmShipment_BeforeAcknowledgeReturns409,\nTestCORSPreflightAllowsPostForShipmentConfirmation, and the error is\nadded to TestEveryMappedErrorHasItsOwnProblemType.\nDocs: sequence-diagrams, eventstorming, bounded-context-canvas.\n\n* fix(analytics): count SUBMISSION_FAILED rejections in the acknowledgement report\n\nApplyNetworkOrderRejected claimed a SUBMISSION_FAILED event but\ncontributed to no counter, so rejections found by reconciliation\n(the network refused a submitted acknowledgement) vanished from the\nreport. Add acknowledgement_rollup.orders_rejected_submission_failed\n(additive analytics migration 0002, NOT NULL DEFAULT 0; history is not\nback-filled) and surface it as ordersRejectedSubmissionFailed in the\nreport row, the REST DTO and the MCP view.\n\nTests: memory store (counted once, deduped; unknown reason claimed but\nnot counted), reports handler JSON, and the testcontainers Postgres\nround trip (exactly 1 after an idempotent double apply).\n\n* docs(contracts): align OpenAPI/AsyncAPI with the code; ADR 0015; DDD pack\n\nOpenAPI: add GET /capability-offers and POST\n/network-orders/{networkRef}/shipment-confirmation (204/404/409/422/500),\nthe CapabilityOffer schema, the capability-offers tag, the single-write\nwording, and the ordersRejectedSubmissionFailed report field.\n\nAsyncAPI: put AcknowledgementDeadlineAtRisk on the analytics channel,\ndescribe five events, point contact.url at IQVO, drop the stale\n\"no use case calls ConfirmShipment\" text, and document that\nNetworkOrderAcknowledged is published at SUBMITTED (before\nreconciliation) with no event on SUBMITTED -> ACKNOWLEDGED. Docs only:\nno event type, dataschema or payload changes.\n\nADR 0015 records the additive contract corrections and the two design\nnotes deliberately left undecided (acknowledgement event timing,\nCycleTimeP95). docs/ddd pages that listed these as gaps or hotspots are\nupdated; Mermaid validated.\n\n* docs: fix stale comments and descriptions found by the docs audit\n\n- shared.NetworkOrderShipmentConfirmed: ConfirmNetworkOrderShipment\n  (ADR 0014) now calls ConfirmShipment; document that.\n- shared.NetworkOrderAcknowledged: document the SUBMITTED publication\n  timing; RejectionReason: four reasons, not three.\n- mcp.Deps cited ADR 0009 for the shipment-confirmation endpoint; it is\n  ADR 0014.\n- list_network_orders description and the operating prompt now mention\n  SUBMITTED and SUBMISSION_FAILED.\n- migrations/0001 idx_network_orders_local_order comment: comment-only\n  edit (golang-migrate stores versions, not checksums) stating that no\n  code queries the index yet and why (ADR 0014).","tree":{"sha":"d372be669872bb600adb6cd4895ce1b86ec1029f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/d372be669872bb600adb6cd4895ce1b86ec1029f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/7bdd6eaed730f126d3870ae101449850d6b7c365","verification":{"payload":"tree d372be669872bb600adb6cd4895ce1b86ec1029f\nparent bb8dc827ab541f9c18b483a322b21a1591bd3980\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791297316 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791297316 -0300\n\nfix: resolve findings from the 2026-10-05 docs audit (#50)\n\n* fix(http): map ErrConfirmBeforeAcknowledge to 409 and allow POST in CORS\n\nPOST /network-orders/{ref}/shipment-confirmation on an order that is not\nACKNOWLEDGED returned 500 internal-error because statusFor/problemFor had\nno case for ErrConfirmBeforeAcknowledge. Map it to 409 with its own\nproblem type (confirm-before-acknowledge). CORS allowed only GET/OPTIONS,\nso the browser could not call the new POST cross-origin; allow POST.\n\nTests: TestHandleConfirmShipment_BeforeAcknowledgeReturns409,\nTestCORSPreflightAllowsPostForShipmentConfirmation, and the error is\nadded to TestEveryMappedErrorHasItsOwnProblemType.\nDocs: sequence-diagrams, eventstorming, bounded-context-canvas.\n\n* fix(analytics): count SUBMISSION_FAILED rejections in the acknowledgement report\n\nApplyNetworkOrderRejected claimed a SUBMISSION_FAILED event but\ncontributed to no counter, so rejections found by reconciliation\n(the network refused a submitted acknowledgement) vanished from the\nreport. Add acknowledgement_rollup.orders_rejected_submission_failed\n(additive analytics migration 0002, NOT NULL DEFAULT 0; history is not\nback-filled) and surface it as ordersRejectedSubmissionFailed in the\nreport row, the REST DTO and the MCP view.\n\nTests: memory store (counted once, deduped; unknown reason claimed but\nnot counted), reports handler JSON, and the testcontainers Postgres\nround trip (exactly 1 after an idempotent double apply).\n\n* docs(contracts): align OpenAPI/AsyncAPI with the code; ADR 0015; DDD pack\n\nOpenAPI: add GET /capability-offers and POST\n/network-orders/{networkRef}/shipment-confirmation (204/404/409/422/500),\nthe CapabilityOffer schema, the capability-offers tag, the single-write\nwording, and the ordersRejectedSubmissionFailed report field.\n\nAsyncAPI: put AcknowledgementDeadlineAtRisk on the analytics channel,\ndescribe five events, point contact.url at IQVO, drop the stale\n\"no use case calls ConfirmShipment\" text, and document that\nNetworkOrderAcknowledged is published at SUBMITTED (before\nreconciliation) with no event on SUBMITTED -> ACKNOWLEDGED. Docs only:\nno event type, dataschema or payload changes.\n\nADR 0015 records the additive contract corrections and the two design\nnotes deliberately left undecided (acknowledgement event timing,\nCycleTimeP95). docs/ddd pages that listed these as gaps or hotspots are\nupdated; Mermaid validated.\n\n* docs: fix stale comments and descriptions found by the docs audit\n\n- shared.NetworkOrderShipmentConfirmed: ConfirmNetworkOrderShipment\n  (ADR 0014) now calls ConfirmShipment; document that.\n- shared.NetworkOrderAcknowledged: document the SUBMITTED publication\n  timing; RejectionReason: four reasons, not three.\n- mcp.Deps cited ADR 0009 for the shipment-confirmation endpoint; it is\n  ADR 0014.\n- list_network_orders description and the operating prompt now mention\n  SUBMITTED and SUBMISSION_FAILED.\n- migrations/0001 idx_network_orders_local_order comment: comment-only\n  edit (golang-migrate stores versions, not checksums) stating that no\n  code queries the index yet and why (ADR 0014).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxQckCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAM20QALF4kFP82WD0fECZ3s09muUn\nbgjlK4u7NmkP7iUrHRxjoweHOP8u2UkA+cAHWryuMWOussr9uY0Am1/syZ1yrixB\nOSwnzyvg/1LHx2NAW72i85fLHfeCeOSZ1cQfc0dEBveqsWq3RJl15AyIeuSJoXfZ\nNb9Sjj08+XiB0QFI1LmDs8VYo2n0d7MAkcWbPMVqdBzi0T0F6BbKqcwARFKl2RyJ\ntg/nN5kn6qbBWrgk+EmasdZArme5nhFPDWWeU1wVgWYCKIY0J+xaqi3dbeujSWVf\nPDWNmbdfJFiDGv9sPTcrPOGnphUdy6NzhDGPS8iJn/m+KKn+CJ1FL6XCUauI2AGA\nqpoxiGD/a8+jOrhU1TkT58F4a4T9lmleoMFaOvXLSJLRqytWlJ7rNC3kMyeg17uA\n+tCN13uVaiydtl4JoJ4wpBcLtbetdE5z+npmFhlBCg7GI5VMPFn3pHbFIofYOXuZ\n5k3Y4/aO25uFW2LLKjkNyqCGIIdNswgwHn2H6Kb0JE0kSJfiUolvJ0eHgsjRvaQw\nQ+Ip4ZmD38AupH4M7vUsmhHQWC98AAaHb4J1/fxdG5jLr+w38F6v6DLlW4vVciLm\nKFhwnDmxZYP+8Fe17StkqfO7Pbn4ahhMuJhuXCKMQQL8TcVQLBRUHUpZzswwatHf\n1MacKOH+HKKBkz6HLiGL\n=uzCl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T14:35:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","use