rl":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/8ac9c2de9f187f627e145b84a4de94037c472516/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:45:55Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T10:45:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: validate persisted status/state strings in repository scans (#48)\n\n* fix(networkorder): validate persisted state via ParseState instead of unchecked cast\n\nscanOrder cast the stored state string to networkorder.State, so a corrupt value became an invalid aggregate. Add ParseState/ErrUnknownState and return a wrapped rehydrate error from the repo.\n\n* fix(capabilityoffer): validate persisted basis via ParseBasis and wrap rehydrate errors\n\nThe repo cast Basis(raw) and relied on New to reject it with an unwrapped error. Add ParseBasis (New now uses it), wrap the read-path error with rehydrate context, and add integration tests that insert corrupt rows for both repos.","tree":{"sha":"fbe2da3d8354ad4f15112883e6758c4d020fec1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/fbe2da3d8354ad4f15112883e6758c4d020fec1d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/8ac9c2de9f187f627e145b84a4de94037c472516","verification":{"payload":"tree fbe2da3d8354ad4f15112883e6758c4d020fec1d\nparent 3ffeae07f9cc58fb5b0ba5d68497b9141795ddbd\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791283555 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791283555 -0300\n\nfix: validate persisted status/state strings in repository scans (#48)\n\n* fix(networkorder): validate persisted state via ParseState instead of unchecked cast\n\nscanOrder cast the stored state string to networkorder.State, so a corrupt value became an invalid aggregate. Add ParseState/ErrUnknownState and return a wrapped rehydrate error from the repo.\n\n* fix(capabilityoffer): validate persisted basis via ParseBasis and wrap rehydrate errors\n\nThe repo cast Basis(raw) and relied on New to reject it with an unwrapped error. Add ParseBasis (New now uses it), wrap the read-path error with rehydrate context, and add integration tests that insert corrupt rows for both repos.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxNFjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACv0QAE/lpiEm543ILiCoCk39minp\nd29FGkMq7EOK9kbbGp4qrotKg+rxO3zx5Rlf+hPCSYDES8QaHFEmNYeHj6nWj3zR\n6XUIuox0Z3+8cmZjAsK/ibMyVgt9ewVSc9VankVOmMjP1hhuxmuzXUUSaosFfB/+\nT1HI0enMi1sN8GSvgmLq1W/sPZOx5d5q1Kybau0/Wj0pa+A4lCf/UFVtSUBSbGBt\n25u1vYgMH3olLTvRp72rmOr1x9ArOO0Uv3CZnnzd10lOeFCARHSoEugcMVQOCrQe\nhtxEu0KfKRTXwre2DJCFvVIDDuqbVPuAKnifb8HY6x4todUnzobEzSFCvhyChhnE\nnu14JLsW1BTyhl269Y6J9a7U9DQRbZny1s0Racnn69uWXdxiu/AcSRntCsRhZVzL\nEwr+3yNmCZH/5f7gmvLQ3C9CcZ9CXlwvsE6LKhmSJIFADgSd7N2aPp4lfaDyYiYn\n/XCPhUE20tbjnherJNWprPeVjeFt80ibN7GLlPWpm5/bcIUL0lWzwg12On4kQSTp\nHlBo76mVcDTsFlxiH7mgNMHFOydQiO6EU+ujJjjaJDjfbJJ/aaVPaJTthOzymbYM\nl1IEZXj4ay6mjlBwTMqZV0vIsl4mNqk5ObLie5MOJN2zgbwBaYwkUErQn8YlPaZT\nDc7+BFawxmFt+Nrqv7WP\n=rcKI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-06T10:45:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/8ac9c2de9f187f627e145b84a4de94037c472516","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDhhYzljMmRlOWYxODdmNjI3ZTE0NWI4NGE0ZGU5NDAzN2M0NzI1MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/3ffeae07f9cc58fb5b0ba5d68497b9141795ddbd","sha":"3ffeae07f9cc58fb5b0ba5d68497b9141795ddbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/3ffeae07f9cc58fb5b0ba5d68497b9141795ddbd"}],"sha":"8ac9c2de9f187f627e145b84a4de94037c472516","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/8ac9c2de9f187f627e145b84a4de94037c472516"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/3ffeae07f9cc58fb5b0ba5d68497b9141795ddbd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:12:09Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:12:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#46)\n\n* docs: refresh README and operations notes against develop; add ADR index\n\nREADME: SUBMITTED state, CapabilityOffer, reconcile/reject-overdue/\nshipment-confirmation/recompute use cases, full REST/MCP/analytics\nsurface, every env var per binary, releases on main, PII rule per\nADR 0009, CI job list. operations-notes: ghcr.io/iqvo image and chart\nregistry, ADR 0014 write route, tickers, two aggregates. New\ndocs/adr/README.md lists every ADR with the Status its body states.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): add strategic ddd-crew pages under docs/ddd\n\nIndex (README.md + ddd-artifacts.md), Core Domain Chart (Supporting,\nquadrant 3, evolution note), Bounded Context Canvas v5 with every\ninbound/outbound message mapped to a route, MCP tool, port or topic,\nContext Map slice with U/D, patterns, technology and evidence, and the\nUbiquitous Language mapped to code identifiers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): add aggregate design canvas, eventstorming and domain events\n\nAggregate Design Canvas v1.1 for NetworkOrder and CapabilityOffer (state\ndiagrams from the real State/Basis constants, every invariant tied to its\nErr value), design-level EventStorming for four processes with hotspots\ntaken from ADRs and code, and a domain-events catalogue (full CloudEvents\ntypes, topics, keys, payloads, producers, consumers) with the AsyncAPI\ndiscrepancies found.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(ddd): add message flow, class, ER and sequence diagrams\n\nDomain Message Flow (4 scenarios, cmd/evt/qry-prefixed, autonumbered),\nUML class diagrams for both aggregates and the domain events plus a\nhexagonal ports/adapters map, ER diagrams of the OLTP and analytical\nschemas (FK lines only where a FOREIGN KEY exists, table-to-aggregate\nmap), and sequence diagrams for every command use case plus the outbox\nrelay and analytics projection. Validator: 25/25 diagrams render.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(agents): CapabilityOffer is built, capability caches consume PPM and WP events, Kafka testcontainers\n\nAGENTS.md is the real file here (CLAUDE.md is the symlink).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"910a9ee9ab72569334d762915ee873cb5baf8ff5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/910a9ee9ab72569334d762915ee873cb5baf8ff5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/3ffeae07f9cc58fb5b0ba5d68497b9141795ddbd","verification":{"payload":"tree 910a9ee9ab72569334d762915ee873cb5baf8ff5\nparent fdceb0df1f3b65f739bf88d502613646ea0e16fd\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791270729 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791270729 -0300\n\ndocs: refresh product docs and add ddd-crew DDD artifact pack (#46)\n\n* docs: refresh README and operations notes against develop; add ADR index\n\nREADME: SUBMITTED state, CapabilityOffer, reconcile/reject-overdue/\nshipment-confirmation/recompute use cases, full REST/MCP/analytics\nsurface, every env var per binary, releases on main, PII rule per\nADR 0009, CI job list. operations-notes: ghcr.io/iqvo image and chart\nregistry, ADR 0014 write route, tickers, two aggregates. New\ndocs/adr/README.md lists ever