//api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/c134a8b51d479e6c2fd3c0e0385c0c29f2848a06","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKGMxMzRhOGI1MWQ0NzllNmMyZmQzYzBlMDM4NWMwYzI5ZjI4NDhhMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7","sha":"6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7"}],"sha":"c134a8b51d479e6c2fd3c0e0385c0c29f2848a06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/c134a8b51d479e6c2fd3c0e0385c0c29f2848a06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:19:55Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T12:19:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: CapabilityOffer aggregate, Kafka caches, read surface, shipment confirmation (ADR 0001 §8) (#42)\n\n* feat: CapabilityOffer aggregate, Kafka caches, Postgres repo, tests\n\nADR 0001 §8: the CapabilityOffer domain model built by a prior pass on\nthis branch, now with full test coverage and a fix for the hexagonal\narch-fitness test:\n\n- internal/domain/capabilityoffer: aggregate + Compute() (unit tests)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/processpathcache: CPTScheduleChanged /\n  ProcessPathCreated|Updated|Deactivated cache, per-process unique\n  consumer group + FirstOffset replay + WaitReady gate (unit tests with\n  a fake Reader; NextCutoff split into smaller helpers to satisfy\n  gocognit)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/pathcapacitycache: PathCapacityChanged\n  cache, same pattern (unit tests)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/inventoryclient: REST client to\n  inventory-storage''s usable-inventory read model -- the documented,\n  deliberate deviation from a third Kafka cache (unit tests)\n- internal/application/usecases/recompute_capability_offers.go: the\n  recompute pass (unit tests with fakes for every port)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/memory + postgres: CapabilityOfferRepo for\n  both backends (unit + testcontainers integration tests)\n- migrations/0003_capability_offers: schema for the above\n- ports.go fix: NextCutoff/EligiblePath were structs declared directly\n  in ports.go, violating ''ports package only contains interfaces''\n  (caught by internal/architecture''s own fitness test, which was not\n  green before this commit). Moved to internal/application/contract,\n  alongside this context''s other port DTOs (HeldOrderRequest etc).\n\nmake check-all: 94.4% coverage (gate 90%), all arch-fitness tests green\nincluding the one this commit fixes. go test -tags=integration ./...\ngreen against real Postgres containers.\n\n* feat: CapabilityOffer read surface + explicit shipment confirmation\n\n- GET /capability-offers (REST) and list_capability_offers (MCP tool),\n  registered only when Offers is wired (nil means not registered, same\n  convention as MetricsRegistry/Reports).\n- item 4: NetworkOrderShipmentConfirmed is now actually raised.\n  ConfirmNetworkOrderShipment is an explicit use case taking a\n  NetworkRef directly rather than correlating fulfillment-execution''s\n  PackageManifested event, because no persisted NetworkRef<->WorkUnitId\n  mapping exists and ADR 0001 Hard rule 4 (''Correlation is a persisted\n  mapping, never a string convention'') forbids inventing one. Exposed\n  as this context''s one write endpoint:\n  POST /network-orders/{networkRef}/shipment-confirmation (204, empty\n  body), idempotent on an already-CONFIRMED order.\n- docs/adr/0009-explicit-shipment-confirmation-endpoint.md: amends ADR\n  0001 Rollout step 6 and narrows Hard rule 9 (''no write endpoint\n  without a new ADR'') for this one case, with the full reasoning.\n- Unit tests for the use case (publish ordering, idempotency, gateway\n  submission, failure paths) and both new HTTP handlers.\n\n* feat: wire CapabilityOffer pipeline + shipment confirmation into cmd/\n\ncmd/netfulfil/main.go:\n- CAPABILITY_OFFER_ENABLED=true (default false) gates the whole\n  pipeline so the service''s zero-config, no-broker-required boot\n  (ADR 0001 section 4) is unaffected for every deployment that has not\n  opted in -- mirrors the existing EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka convention.\n- When enabled: dials both Kafka caches through the existing boot\n  retry() (Istio first-dial reset, ADR 0011), starts their Run\n  goroutines, and BLOCKS boot on both WaitReady gates before accepting\n  traffic -- an empty, not-yet-replayed cache must never silently\n  advertise an under-counted figure.\n- Wires INVENTORY_STORAGE_URL (default http://localhost:8080,\n  matching ORDER_MANAGEMENT_URL own default), the CapabilityOfferRepo\n  (memory or postgres, matching wireOrders own choice), and a ticker\n  (RECOMPUTE_INTERVAL, default 1m) driving RecomputeCapabilityOffers\n  alongside the existing sweep ticker.\n- Graceful shutdown waits (bounded) for both cache consumer goroutines\n  to actually stop, same pattern as the poller/outbox relay.\n- api.Offers and api.ConfirmShipment wired on the HTTP server (nil\n  when the feature is disabled, matching the nil-means-not-registered\n  convention).\n- Capability offer wiring''s fatal error path is placed BEFORE the\n  closeOrders/closeEventPublisher defers are registered, so an\n  os.Exit on failure cannot skip a cleanup defer (gocritic\n  exitAfterDefer); make check''s golangci-lint run is clean.\n\ncmd/mcp/main.go: wires the SAME CapabilityOfferRepo backend choice\n(memory or postgres, sharing buildOrders own pool) for\nlist_capability_offers.\n\nmake check-all, go vet/test -tags=integration, helm lint+template all\ngreen (see PR body).\n\n* docs: renumber ADR 0009 to 0014 (collision with develop''s new 0009-0013)\n\n* fix: renumber capability_offers migration 0003 -> 0004 (collision with develop''s 0003_submitted_state)","tree":{"sha":"ec11bea6ae1225999a4aeb4578971e8733fd65ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/ec11bea6ae1225999a4aeb4578971e8733fd65ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7","verification":{"payload":"tree ec11bea6ae1225999a4aeb4578971e8733fd65ec\nparent a336ae3d115cc3d07c700c060ae7a5e6a39c6b83\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791202795 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791202795 -0300\n\nfeat: CapabilityOffer aggregate, Kafka caches, read surface, shipment confirmation (ADR 0001 §8) (#42)\n\n* feat: CapabilityOffer aggregate, Kafka caches, Postgres repo, tests\n\nADR 0001 §8: the CapabilityOffer domain model built by a prior pass on\nthis branch, now with full test coverage and a fix for the hexagonal\narch-fitness test:\n\n- internal/domain/capabilityoffer: aggregate + Compute() (unit tests)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/processpathcache: CPTScheduleChanged /\n  ProcessPathCreated|Updated|Deactivated cache, per-process unique\n  consumer group + FirstOffset replay + WaitReady gate (unit tests with\n  a fake Reader; NextCutoff split into smaller helpers to satisfy\n  gocognit)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/pathcapacitycache: PathCapacityChanged\n  cache, same pattern (unit tests)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/inventoryclient: REST client to\n  inventory-storage''s usable-inventory read model -- the documented,\n  deliberate deviation from a third Kafka cache (unit tests)\n- internal/application/usecases/recompute_capability_offers.go: the\n  recompute pass (unit tests with fakes for every port)\n- internal/adapters/outbound/memory + postgres: CapabilityOfferRepo for\n  both backends (unit + testcontainers integration tests)\n- migrations/0003_capability_offers: schema for the above\n- ports.go fix: NextCutoff/EligiblePath were structs declared directly\n  in ports.go, violating ''ports package only contains interfaces''\n  (caught by internal/architecture''s own fitness test, which was not\n  green before this commit). Moved to internal/application/contract,\n  alongside this context''s other port DTOs (HeldOrderRequest etc).\n\nmake check-all: 94.4% coverage (gate 90%), all arch-fitness tests green\nincluding the one this commit fixes. go test -tags=integration ./...\ngreen against real Postgres containers.\n\n* feat: CapabilityOffer read surface + explicit shipment confirmation\n\n- GET /capability-offers (REST) and list_capability_offers (MCP tool),\n  registered only when Offers is wired (nil means not registered, same\n  convention as MetricsRegistry/Reports).\n- item 4: NetworkOrderShipmentConfirmed is now actually raised.\n  ConfirmNetworkOrderShipment is an explicit use case taking a\n  NetworkRef directly rather than correlating fulfillment-execution''s\n  PackageManifested event, because no persisted NetworkRef<->WorkUnitId\n  mapping exists and ADR 0001 Hard rule 4 (''Correlation is a persisted\n  mapping, never a string convention'') forbids inventing one. Exposed\n  as this context''s one write endpoint:\n  POST /network-orders/{networkRef}/shipment-confirmation (204, empty\n  body), idempotent on an already-CONFIRMED order.\n- docs/adr/0009-explicit-shipment-confirmation-endpoint.md: amends ADR\n  0001 Rollout step 6 and narrows Hard rule 9 (''no write endpoint\n  without a new ADR'') for this one case, with the full reasoning.\n- Unit tests for the use case (publish ordering, idempotency, gateway\n  submission, failure paths) and both new HTTP handlers.\n\n* feat: wire CapabilityOffer pipeline + shipment confirmation into cmd/\n\ncmd/netfulfil/main.go:\n- CAPABILITY_OFFER_ENABLED=true (default false) gates the whole\n  pipeline so the service''s zero-config, no-broker-required boot\n  (ADR 0001 section 4) is unaffected for every deployment that has not\n  opted in -- mirrors the existing EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka convention.\n- When enabled: dials both Kafka caches through the existing boot\n  retry() (Istio first-dial reset, ADR 0011), starts their Run\n  goroutines, and BLOCKS boot on both WaitReady gates before accepting\n  traffic -- an empty, not-yet-replayed cache must never silently\n  advertise an under-counted figure.\n- Wires INVENTORY_STORAGE_URL (default http://localhost:8080,\n  matching ORDER_MANAGEMENT_URL own default), the CapabilityOfferRepo\n  (memory or postgres, matching wireOrders own choice), and a ticker\n  (RECOMPUTE_INTERVAL, default 1m) driving RecomputeCapabilityOffers\n  alongside the existing sweep ticker.\n- Graceful shutdown waits (bounded) for both cache consumer goroutines\n  to actually stop, same pattern as the poller/outbox relay.\n- api.Offers and api.ConfirmShipment wired on the HTTP server (nil\n  when the feature is disabled, matching the nil-means-not-registered\n  convention).\n- Capability offer wiring''s fatal error path is placed BEFORE the\n  closeOrders/closeEventPublisher defers are registered, so an\n  os.Exit on failure cannot skip a cleanup defer (gocritic\n  exitAfterDefer); make check''s golangci-lint run is clean.\n\ncmd/mcp/main.go: wires the SAME CapabilityOfferRepo backend choice\n(memory or postgres, sharing buildOrders own pool) for\nlist_capability_offers.\n\nmake check-all, go vet/test -tags=integration, helm lint+template all\ngreen (see PR body).\n\n* docs: renumber ADR 0009 to 0014 (collision with develop''s new 0009-0013)\n\n* fix: renumber capability_offers migration 0003 -> 0004 (collision with develop''s 0003_submitted_state)","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw5XrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHOgQAJ4++CQx3brxh85D2tTYjV2z\nwfAidw14wP1SJ0A9M+XIRresohUwiKl9MxjIFeGZMYbnblsK3+KdGiBIuPBNJ+9a\ng5ciRT7ukpiNM/yXEXV7ex9dLoIQv3V4eELXTlEE2+pg5RewKDI/nCKYQGRj5Fjf\n/cqG++VvZWLZHAmg/MN4nyfejxPdEU1AujwOOG2Yo8dUYoAVaLWliCS79QLXK6ZY\nmgP5qHIkt+JRYUmjL2FBBzNLe+Uc0wgRoybkmAJtprLnFV8afeW13uZSFE2KqYGg\nYSThKIetsKLQoRAXSSD8G6Ilegp/dSdljq21mbwxFazpPoxMDZ63XJKrY4wJ0eL9\n+5JQ6umMmxDdZEIKF5GYvPkVstot64ECvDQuZXSYKnmkiShGtEfZdwJ0wgzfXVfs\npuBvoQ/xi4Wo7knwwmAO4rX7cORh6gdfiYD/cCcFWR8jCmyOcZuqDLCbrN5jES0m\nWKtgX2uWwj1LwaZwb2237l0UXcvuKAhxDZNJNrB4rHv5wa10JjYA2r7IFzHalJjz\nTOdpUmtKi8k0B7m3BsoQ6MZjvZVA+GCgd5Yg3PztvbwULOpGrAhlEnKa9TyF9COW\nBEGXR7178MUO34xDYLSDz1ZJwvo3oAU1JCBjvsHsuYba1245cO3IAP9lCVKwvO1n\nuPSVYunuqH08BzIDO83t\n=e5yc\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T12:19:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDZkNzViOGFiMDA1ZjM2ZDk2MDliNmI3MTY1M2I2NGFjNGEyZTQ1ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/a336ae3d115cc3d07c700c060ae7a5e6a39c6b83","sha":"a336ae3d115cc3d07c700c060ae7a5e6a39c6b83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/a336ae3d115cc3d07c700c060ae7a5e6a39c6b83"}],"sha":"6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/6d75b8ab005f36d9609b6b71653b64ac4a2e45e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/a336ae3d115cc3d07c700c060ae7a5e6a39c6b83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:56:19Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T11:56:19Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: ADR conformance gaps (CapabilityOffer, sweep bug, reconciliation, sandbox removal) (#41)\n\n* docs: renumber duplicate ADR-0002 (retail-network) to ADR-0009\n\nThis repo had two ADRs numbered 0002: 0002-mcp-and-analytics-data-product.md\n(keeps 0002) and 0002-retail-network-not-amazon-counterpart.md (moved to\n0009, the next free number). Updates frontmatter id/slug/title/sidebar\nand cross-references in docs/planning. AGENTS.md also references the old\nnumber in several places but is a protected agent-instruction file this\nrun is blocked from editing; flagged in the PR body.\n\n* fix: add SUBMITTED state + submission reconciliation (ADR 0001 §5)\n\nItem 3: NetworkOrder gains a SUBMITTED state between NEW and\nACKNOWLEDGED. ReceiveNetworkDemand now stops at SUBMITTED and no\nlonger releases the held order optimistically right after telling the\nnetwork — that was the real bug: a submit response (accepted-for-\nprocessing) was being treated as a completed commitment. A new\nReconcileSubmittedOrders use case polls NetworkGateway.SubmissionStatus\nand only then settles the order to ACKNOWLEDGED (releasing the hold) or\nREJECTED (cancelling it, reason SUBMISSION_FAILED). Wired into\ncmd/netfulfil on its own ticker (reuses POLL_INTERVAL).\n\nItem 5 (partial): NetworkGateway port gains SubmitAvailability,\nDeclareCapability, RequestLabel and SubmissionStatus (stub\nimplementations; CapabilityOffer''s own PR will be the first real\ncaller). NETWORK_MODE sandbox removed from the Go gateway (ParseMode/\nNewGateway/Mode consts); NETWORK_BASE_URL now wired into\ncmd/netfulfil''s wireGateway (fails closed if live mode has no base\nURL). Chart/docs/test sandbox removal is a separate commit.\n\nAcknowledge() stays as a one-shot Submit+ConfirmAcknowledgement\nconvenience so every test fixture that only needs a settled order\n(http, mcp, postgres integration tests) is unaffected.\n\n* fix: sweep never mutates the aggregate (ADR 0001 §6)\n\nItem 2: SweepAcknowledgementDeadlines mutated the aggregate (called\no.Reject() and published NetworkOrderRejected) contradicting ADR\n0001 §6''s documented design. Split into two independent use cases:\n\n- SweepAcknowledgementDeadlines: now a pure reporter. No Planner, no\n  UnitOfWork, no Save. Publishes the new AcknowledgementDeadlineAtRisk\n  CloudEvent (re-fires every pass, by design) and nothing else.\n- RejectOverdueOrders (new): the separate path that performs the actual\n  rejection -- cancels the held order, transitions to REJECTED, and\n  publishes NetworkOrderRejected (reason=ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_DEADLINE_MISSED)\n  in one atomic (outbox) scope. Wired on its own ticker in cmd/netfulfil,\n  independent of the sweep''s.\n\nAdded AcknowledgementDeadlineAtRisk to apis/asyncapi.yaml (message +\nschemas + golden CloudEvents JSON test on both streams) and to ADR\n0008''s type catalogue (internal/architecture''s fitness test enforces\nevery published type is listed there). Also fixed NetworkOrderState\nenums (openapi.yaml, web/src/types.ts, MCP list filter) and the\nNetworkOrderRejected reason enum to include the new SUBMITTED state\nand SUBMISSION_FAILED reason from the previous commit.\n\nRewrote every sweep test that asserted the old mutating behaviour,\nmoved the rejection-behaviour tests to RejectOverdueOrders, and added\na new test proving the sweep leaves state and the held order untouched.\n\n* fix: finish sandbox removal, readinessProbe /readyz, ADR back-links\n\nItem 5 (rest): removed NETWORK_MODE=sandbox from the chart\n(values.yaml, configmap.yaml, NOTES.txt, deployment.yaml comments),\napis/openapi.yaml''s gateway-mode enum, web/src/types.ts, and\ntest_credential_wiring.py''s live-only mode list. Wired\nconfig.networkBaseUrl into the chart (ConfigMap NETWORK_BASE_URL,\nrendered only when set) matching cmd/netfulfil''s new wireGateway.\n\nItem 7: charts/network-fulfillment/values.yaml readinessProbe now\ntargets /readyz instead of /healthz -- the route and the ADR 0004\nreadiness-flip-first shutdown sequence already exist in\ncmd/netfulfil/main.go; only the chart was stale.\n\nItem 6: ADR-0001''s Status section gets the ''(amended by ADR-0009)''\nback-link. ADR-0004''s stale ''NETWORK_MODE=stub/sandbox/live'' and\n''sandbox/live client'' text fixed to stub/live, pointing at ADR 0009 §4.\n\nhelm lint, helm template (stub + live+creds), and both chart python\ntest suites verified green.\n\n* fix: analytics integration test uses testcontainers (item 8)\n\ninternal/adapters/outbound/analyticsstore/postgres_integration_test.go\nwas the one holdout still gated on an external ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL\nwith a skip -- the OLTP postgres package''s own integration tests\nalready use testcontainers-go. Converted it to the same pattern: boots\nits own postgres:16-alpine container per test run, runs the analytics\nmigrations against it, no env var, no skip. Verified actually green\nagainst a real container (not just compiling): go test -tags=integration\n./internal/adapters/outbound/analyticsstore/... -v.\n\nAlso fixes outbox_integration_test.go''s stubGateway, which predates\nthe NetworkGateway interface extension from an earlier commit and only\nsurfaces under -tags=integration (go vet/test without the tag never\ncompiles this file) -- go vet -tags=integration ./... now passes too.\n\nAdds migration 0003_submitted_state: the SUBMITTED value added to the\nGo-side networkorder.State enum two commits ago was never added to\nnetwork_orders'' CHECK constraints, so linking a local order at SUBMITTED\ntime (ReceiveNetworkDemand.acknowledge) violated\nnetwork_orders_state_check / local_order_requires_answer in any run\nagainst real Postgres. go test -tags=integration ./... was the only\nway this surfaced -- plain go test never touches the schema.\n\n* docs: fix placeholder ADR NNNN refs to ADR 0003 (item 8)\n\nreceive_network_demand.go:32 and coverage_gap_test.go:140 both cited\nthe transactional outbox as ''ADR NNNN'' -- a placeholder left over from\nbefore that ADR was numbered. It''s docs/adr/0003-transactional-outbox.md.\n\n* fix: resolve guide-lint stale ADR-0002 cross-refs (item 9)\n\n- docs/adr/0002-retail-network-not-amazon-counterpart.md is restored as a\n  small redirect stub to ADR 0009, because CLAUDE.md:11 still cites the\n  old path verbatim and CLAUDE.md is a protected agent-instruction file\n  this automation is blocked from editing (write refused by the vault/\n  protection layer). This is the minimal fix that keeps guide-lint''s\n  ''cites X which does not exist'' check honest without touching the\n  protected file; a human maintainer can delete the stub once CLAUDE.md\n  is updated directly.\n- fix stale 0002 cross-ref in .claude/skills/how-to-write-an-adr/SKILL.md\n  to point at 0009.\n\nguide-lint now passes locally (0 errors, 0 warnings).","tree":{"sha":"72f552af5871706a9bb5469b07dbf6982527597e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/72f552af5871706a9bb5469b07dbf6982527597e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/a336ae3d115cc3d07c700c060ae7a5e6a39c6b83","verification":{"payload":"tree 72f552af5871706a9bb5469b07dbf6982527597e\nparent 411a92511227dfaecc40aefa2987df262c39300c\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1791201379 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791201379 -0300\n\nfix: ADR conformance gaps (CapabilityOffer, sweep bug, reconciliation, sandbox removal) (#41)\n\n* docs: renumber duplicate ADR-0002 (retail-network) to ADR-0009\n\nThis repo had two ADRs numbered 0002: 0002-mcp-and-analytics-data-product.md\n(keeps 0002) and 0002-retail-network-not-amazon-counterpart.md (moved to\n0009, the next free number). Updates frontmatter id/slug/title/sidebar\nand cross-references in docs/planning. AGENTS.md also references the old\nnumber in several places but is a protected agent-instruction file this\nrun is blocked from editing; flagged in the PR body.\n\n* fix: add SUBMITTED state + submission reconciliation (ADR 0001 §5)\n\nItem 3: NetworkOrder gains a SUBMITTED state between NEW and\nACKNOWLEDGED. ReceiveNetworkDemand now stops at SUBMITTED and no\nlonger releases the held order optimistically right after telling the\nnetwork — that was the real bug: a submit response (accepted-for-\nprocessing) was being treated as a completed commitment. A new\nReconcileSubmittedOrders use case polls NetworkGateway.SubmissionStatus\nand only then settles the order to ACKNOWLEDGED (releasing the hold) or\nREJECTED (cancelling it, reason SUBMISSION_FAILED). Wired into\ncmd/netfulfil on its own ticker (reuses POLL_INTERVAL).\n\nItem 5 (partial): NetworkGateway port gains SubmitAvailability,\nDeclareCapability, RequestLabel and SubmissionStatus (stub\nimplementations; CapabilityOffer''s own PR will be the first real\ncaller). NETWORK_MODE sandbox removed from the Go gateway (ParseMode/\nNewGateway/Mode consts); NETWORK_BASE_URL now wired into\ncmd/netfulfil''s wireGateway (fails closed if live mode has no base\nURL). Chart/docs/test sandbox removal is a separate commit.\n\nAcknowledge() stays as a one-shot Submit+ConfirmAcknowledgement\nconvenience so every test fixture that only needs a settled order\n(http, mcp, postgres integration tests) is unaffected.\n\n* fix: sweep never mutates the aggregate (ADR 0001 §6)\n\nItem 2: SweepAcknowledgementDeadlines mutated the aggregate (called\no.Reject() and published NetworkOrderRejected) contradicting ADR\n0001 §6''s documented design. Split into two independent use cases:\n\n- SweepAcknowledgementDeadlines: now a pure reporter. No Planner, no\n  UnitOfWork, no Save. Publishes the new AcknowledgementDeadlineAtRisk\n  CloudEvent (re-fires every pass, by design) and nothing else.\n- RejectOverdueOrders (new): the separate path that performs the actual\n  rejection -- cancels the held order, transitions to REJECTED, and\n  publishes NetworkOrderRejected (reason=ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_DEADLINE_MISSED)\n  in one atomic (outbox) scope. Wired on its own ticker in cmd/netfulfil,\n  independent of the sweep''s.\n\nAdded AcknowledgementDeadlineAtRisk to apis/asyncapi.yaml (message +\nschemas + golden CloudEvents JSON test on both streams) and to ADR\n0008''s type catalogue (internal/architecture''s fitness test enforces\nevery published type is listed there). Also fixed NetworkOrderState\nenums (openapi.yaml, web/src/types.ts, MCP list filter) and the\nNetworkOrderRejected reason enum to include the new SUBMITTED state\nand SUBMISSION_FAILED reason from the previous commit.\n\nRewrote every sweep test that asserted the old mutating behaviour,\nmoved the rejection-behaviour tests to RejectOverdueOrders, and added\na new test proving the sweep leaves state and the held order untouched.\n\n* fix: finish sandbox removal, readinessProbe /readyz, ADR back-links\n\nItem 5 (rest): removed NETWORK_MODE=sandbox from the chart\n(values.yaml, configmap.yaml, NOTES.txt, deployment.yaml comments),\napis/openapi.yaml''s gateway-mode enum, web/src/types.ts, and\ntest_credential_wiring.py''s live-only mode list. Wired\nconfig.networkBaseUrl into the chart (ConfigMap NETWORK_BASE_URL,\nrendered only when set) matching cmd/netfulfil''s new wireGateway.\n\nItem 7: charts/network-fulfillment/values.yaml readinessProbe now\ntargets /readyz instead of /healthz -- the route and the ADR 0004\nreadiness-flip-first shutdown sequence already exist in\ncmd/netfulfil/main.go; only the chart was stale.\n\nItem 6: ADR-0001''s Status section gets the ''(amended by ADR-0009)''\nback-link. ADR-0004''s stale ''NETWORK_MODE=stub/sandbox/live'' and\n''sandbox/live client'' text fixed to stub/live, pointing at ADR 0009 §4.\n\nhelm lint, helm template (stub + live+creds), and both chart python\ntest suites verified green.\n\n* fix: analytics integration test uses testcontainers (item 8)\n\ninternal/adapters/outbound/analyticsstore/postgres_integration_test.go\nwas the one holdout still gated on an external ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL\nwith a skip -- the OLTP postgres package''s own integration tests\nalready use testcontainers-go. Converted it to the same pattern: boots\nits own postgres:16-alpine container per test run, runs the analytics\nmigrations against it, no env var, no skip. Verified actually green\nagainst a real container (not just compiling): go test -tags=integration\n./internal/adapters/outbound/analyticsstore/... -v.\n\nAlso fixes outbox_integration_test.go''s stubGateway, which predates\nthe NetworkGateway interface extension from an earlier commit and only\nsurfaces under -tags=integration (go vet/test without the tag never\ncompiles this file) -- go vet -tags=integration ./... now passes too.\n\nAdds migration 0003_submitted_state: the SUBMITTED value added to the\nGo-side networkorder.State enum two commits ago was never added to\nnetwork_orders'' CHECK constraints, so linking a local order at SUBMITTED\ntime (ReceiveNetworkDemand.acknowledge) violated\nnetwork_orders_state_check / local_order_requires_answer in any run\nagainst real Postgres. go test -tags=integration ./... was the only\nway this surfaced -- plain go test never touches the schema.\n\n* docs: fix placeholder ADR NNNN refs to ADR 0003 (item 8)\n\nreceive_network_demand.go:32 and coverage_gap_test.go:140 both cited\nthe transactional outbox as ''ADR NNNN'' -- a placeholder left over from\nbefore that ADR was numbered. It''s docs/adr/0003-transactional-outbox.md.\n\n* fix: resolve guide-lint stale ADR-0002 cross-refs (item 9)\n\n- docs/adr/0002-retail-network-not-amazon-counterpart.md is restored as a\n  small redirect stub to ADR 0009, because CLAUDE.md:11 still cites the\n  old path verbatim and CLAUDE.md is a protected agent-instruction file\n  this automation is blocked from editing (write refused by the vault/\n  protection layer). This is the minimal fix that keeps guide-lint''s\n  ''cites X which does not exist'' check honest without touching the\n  protected file; a human maintainer can delete the stub once CLAUDE.md\n  is updated directly.\n- fix stale 0002 cross-ref in .claude/skills/how-to-write-an-adr/SKILL.md\n  to point at 0009.\n\nguide-lint now passes locally (0 errors, 0 warnings).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw5BjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANrAQABta9bHd+AMAR3WBFtMHpyfW\nOMI5GpJqKjR2eChTMSOw41aUsAPHLemgqjxrlo2KDbGtz8xT49WTxd3RxMRln7XI\nM2ZQoxYCP/sKDWkzVbBjNJWF/U65F1F7lXcRsszU/IISKfD7C96s4N/xjA8OjznJ\nz4E0ygfOGN13rx6XkqJGYbE4Nae+UemBVyv7Ch1o9vv0wVfcZarfSDd01GsIsyL/\n2kQuw/H1R5zeEn2D7rgS4Xvqi/MWGJOhK3Zvlq4Ga7QouCbzwTjTP2MpPIRgRhSA\n6dAqdTmpa1uez0BVSLpK09EE+QrAPrnAk35OM8e8+TIM5tKBlTp1p9q5KRnm37d1\n6mEoJGiBhcTl1MGIAQOnUvJNMDZYVi1OslRFdTfaKwCauht8mpidobGvJf1+kapA\n2sEHfHB4D0o71hxwIpcg9y1OYlPRce+EElm/tud2z523YnKjjL957RArlnWjKiSJ\nzOkXcHh+1//XPJMF4KNdbmV8E3rt5jRFE83OjfESRkHYGv1PRF61asKnsjRTFaBB\neqBor/z4564JORKn+au2H7UkvF82RW0Cdt+HpY+M4B5QBE4aIN9L8l8LaP2Tot5t\n0qNTYmzmC6mp8l/xVE1NdCQx19BBpbz4NQ+vq3NzenfGeNEI4z8ci9b8JRBfOUWI\nkm4XrkMnewA/pb9MdlMB\n=1Dcr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T11:56:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","no