ork-fulfillment/commit/a30252cb42520bf78659d368106d060874393fa3","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKGEzMDI1MmNiNDI1MjBiZjc4NjU5ZDM2ODEwNmQwNjA4NzQzOTNmYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f","sha":"3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/1279a31e0f1c71857af84de8b433eb12f2cdc71c","sha":"1279a31e0f1c71857af84de8b433eb12f2cdc71c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/1279a31e0f1c71857af84de8b433eb12f2cdc71c"}],"sha":"a30252cb42520bf78659d368106d060874393fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/a30252cb42520bf78659d368106d060874393fa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:29Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T13:22:29Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#25)\n\n## Problem\n\nFleet-wide bug, found and fixed first in order-management (PR #115,\nADR-0029), ported here. golang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a\nsession-scoped `pg_advisory_lock` to serialize concurrent migration runs\nat boot. `DATABASE_URL` (warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer rollout)\npoints this service at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode, which does\nnot preserve session state across statements. Two or more replicas of\ncmd/netfulfil or cmd/mcp starting concurrently (an HPA scale-out, or an\nordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1) crash-loop with `pq: unnamed\nprepared statement does not exist` for ~1-2 minutes until one wins the\nadvisory-lock race.\n\n## Fix\n\n`cmd/netfulfil/main.go`''s wireOrders and `cmd/mcp/main.go`''s buildOrders\n(both run migrations at startup) now read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nenv var for the migration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when\nunset. The pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\nDATABASE_URL unchanged — every request keeps going through PgBouncer.\n\nnetfulfil-projector/netfulfil-reports are unaffected: ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL\nwas never routed through PgBouncer.\n\n`charts/network-fulfillment`: new `database.migrationsExistingSecretKey`\nvalue (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders the env var in both\nthe api and mcp Deployments, sourced from the same existingSecret, with\n`optional: true` on the secretKeyRef so a secret predating this key\nstill starts the pod.\n\nVerified directly against the live cluster (not assumed from\nwarehouse-infra PR #44''s summary, since this service''s Terraform wiring\nis a standalone kubernetes_secret.network_fulfillment_db resource, not\nthe shared kubernetes_secret.service_db[each.key] pattern):\n\n  $ kubectl get secret network-fulfillment-db -n warehouse-systems \\\n      -o jsonpath=''{.data}'' | jq keys\n  [\"DATABASE_URL\", \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\"]\n\nBoth keys decode to network_fulfillment DSNs with identical\nuser/password/dbname; DATABASE_URL still points at\npgbouncer.warehouse-data.svc.cluster.local:6432, MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nis new and points at postgres-postgresql.warehouse-data.svc.cluster.local:5432.\n\n## Tests added\n\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback — the env-var fallback both\n  directions.\n- TestWireOrders_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations —\n  proves wireOrders itself threads MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, not\n  DATABASE_URL, into the migration step.\n\n## ADR\n\ndocs/adr/0007-migrations-direct-postgres-connection.md — mirrors\norder-management''s ADR-0029, cross-references warehouse-infra PR #43/#44\nand this repo''s own standalone Terraform wiring.\n\n## Quality gate\n\nmake check, make check-all (coverage 95.7%, gate 90%; arch-test green),\nmake integration (testcontainers Postgres/Kafka), helm lint + chart\nwiring tests (test_credential_wiring.py, test_data_files.py) — all pass.\n\nDoes not touch warehouse-infra: its secret provisioning (PR #44) already\ncovers this service.","tree":{"sha":"79d75e8bd2651812e403c46cd633f6fa7a709bbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/79d75e8bd2651812e403c46cd633f6fa7a709bbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f","verification":{"payload":"tree 79d75e8bd2651812e403c46cd633f6fa7a709bbd\nparent d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790601749 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790601749 -0300\n\nfix(migrations): run golang-migrate over a direct Postgres connection (#25)\n\n## Problem\n\nFleet-wide bug, found and fixed first in order-management (PR #115,\nADR-0029), ported here. golang-migrate''s postgres driver takes a\nsession-scoped `pg_advisory_lock` to serialize concurrent migration runs\nat boot. `DATABASE_URL` (warehouse-infra PR #43, PgBouncer rollout)\npoints this service at PgBouncer in transaction-pooling mode, which does\nnot preserve session state across statements. Two or more replicas of\ncmd/netfulfil or cmd/mcp starting concurrently (an HPA scale-out, or an\nordinary rolling deploy with replicas>1) crash-loop with `pq: unnamed\nprepared statement does not exist` for ~1-2 minutes until one wins the\nadvisory-lock race.\n\n## Fix\n\n`cmd/netfulfil/main.go`''s wireOrders and `cmd/mcp/main.go`''s buildOrders\n(both run migrations at startup) now read a new MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nenv var for the migration step only, falling back to DATABASE_URL when\nunset. The pgxpool built right after migrations complete still uses\nDATABASE_URL unchanged — every request keeps going through PgBouncer.\n\nnetfulfil-projector/netfulfil-reports are unaffected: ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL\nwas never routed through PgBouncer.\n\n`charts/network-fulfillment`: new `database.migrationsExistingSecretKey`\nvalue (default \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\") renders the env var in both\nthe api and mcp Deployments, sourced from the same existingSecret, with\n`optional: true` on the secretKeyRef so a secret predating this key\nstill starts the pod.\n\nVerified directly against the live cluster (not assumed from\nwarehouse-infra PR #44''s summary, since this service''s Terraform wiring\nis a standalone kubernetes_secret.network_fulfillment_db resource, not\nthe shared kubernetes_secret.service_db[each.key] pattern):\n\n  $ kubectl get secret network-fulfillment-db -n warehouse-systems \\\n      -o jsonpath=''{.data}'' | jq keys\n  [\"DATABASE_URL\", \"MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\"]\n\nBoth keys decode to network_fulfillment DSNs with identical\nuser/password/dbname; DATABASE_URL still points at\npgbouncer.warehouse-data.svc.cluster.local:6432, MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL\nis new and points at postgres-postgresql.warehouse-data.svc.cluster.local:5432.\n\n## Tests added\n\n- TestMigrationsDatabaseURLFallback — the env-var fallback both\n  directions.\n- TestWireOrders_UsesMigrationsDatabaseURLNotDatabaseURLForMigrations —\n  proves wireOrders itself threads MIGRATIONS_DATABASE_URL, not\n  DATABASE_URL, into the migration step.\n\n## ADR\n\ndocs/adr/0007-migrations-direct-postgres-connection.md — mirrors\norder-management''s ADR-0029, cross-references warehouse-infra PR #43/#44\nand this repo''s own standalone Terraform wiring.\n\n## Quality gate\n\nmake check, make check-all (coverage 95.7%, gate 90%; arch-test green),\nmake integration (testcontainers Postgres/Kafka), helm lint + chart\nwiring tests (test_credential_wiring.py, test_data_files.py) — all pass.\n\nDoes not touch warehouse-infra: its secret provisioning (PR #44) already\ncovers this service.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqumoVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA42wQAF8OFOpEP8RaKpXZWoNG/OaM\nxaBTQ1kuhJhv2fMCVqJJEpcV8ejWvnA66VeXi4dSyejDm+SxkqLbUojH0sfT/PMe\ncBU2qRgnYqNwHyyJ0wmMeo/QEunyk9qg/RPKjKS7nAv5c2GyQo0AhsE2ZpukaGjC\nRbbOl2F2J1tlvTAye4vMSZmzbLuRpGyJYNjjD7c40S2Yk/YHHE+LK3UMnaann31o\neptleGhpO2OQRyFXPOsH9bMw1I4J9lLp9DIVzl4KOQ1MLcEurrkIYTgyAQ3bBlxA\nCU5RhwdYu/tlVQx/iJxulAOMHB/OVHkKJEc5Zp/hRpXIZXKbnHDA/wUZhagAzLpw\nX/ttGSamgueBhdYIS5LtEr3gptFch/juG0KHjlO5DW4cBiY5/8ZMwgEYh03hYNI1\nB2AIZTtm8mkkjO135kKvtd/ccA0czDqD2bz2c8r35rMycD6kxoTLNqn146DvxLCq\nTfedG+t1g90c8bmf+WZ8LrNg90dX5wDefShyJYkqrl9TmWMR+jcEswWpBWReHL7g\nzm5goKWXmCYJsMDL+M/IuNnRWwqZygH4BNLsQAZpqF4r5wO2h6aaWQ4pKn4YrZ2L\npMQ8p/DlT7nAdZ1mqAGbAxEDL33McMHa/46crjjjctVMgay6tSHa7gGFLubJmS0z\njs8PuO/xmR1q4aH2Rk//\n=PhaU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T13:22:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDNlMzdjYWE4ZDgxMDQzYWRiOTljOTA4NTg3ZjY3MDEyMmUwZjhlNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d","sha":"d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d"}],"sha":"3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/3e37caa8d81043adb99c908587f670122e0f8e6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:01:59Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T10:01:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(network): stub gateway must retry unacknowledged demand, not drop it (#14)\n\nStubGateway.PollDemand unconditionally cleared pending on every call,\nregardless of whether ReceiveNetworkDemand.Execute succeeded for each\nunit. This silently violated the poller''s own documented contract\n(poller.go: \"a pass where any demand failed leaves it where it was, so\nthe next poll re-fetches that demand and tries again\") -- a demand unit\nthat failed on its first poll (e.g. a transient error calling\norder-management) was gone forever instead of being retried on the next\ntick.\n\nFound via a real e2e run against the live fleet: order-management''s\nfirst POST /orders after a cold start returned 500 (Kafka topic/producer\nwarm-up), the poller correctly left its watermark unadvanced for a\nretry, but the stub gateway had already discarded the seeded unit on the\nfirst PollDemand call, so it silently vanished instead of being\nre-delivered.\n\nFix: PollDemand now returns pending without clearing it. Retirement\nmoves to SubmitAcknowledgement, which is the point ReceiveNetworkDemand\nhas actually finished with an order (both its reject and acknowledge\npaths call it last-but-one, before the one irreversible step) --\nmirroring how a real network''s own cursor only advances once we have\ntold it something, not once we have merely asked.\n\nUpdated TestStubGateway_PollClearsSeededDemand (renamed to\nTestStubGateway_PollDemandRePresentsUnacknowledgedUnits) to assert the\ncorrected contract: an un-acked unit is repeated on the next poll, and\nacknowledging it is what retires it.\n\nFull suite (including architecture fitness tests) green: go test ./...","tree":{"sha":"d33e03109e11012276fa42540b1b7ca25221c646","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/d33e03109e11012276fa42540b1b7ca25221c646"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d","verification":{"payload":"tree d33e03109e11012276fa42540b1b7ca25221c646\nparent 746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790589719 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790589719 -0300\n\nfix(network): stub gateway must retry unacknowledged demand, not drop it (#14)\n\nStubGateway.PollDemand unconditionally cleared pending on every call,\nregardless of whether ReceiveNetworkDemand.Execute succeeded for each\nunit. This silently violated the poller''s own documented contract\n(poller.go: \"a pass where any demand failed leaves it where it was, so\nthe next poll re-fetches that demand and tries again\") -- a demand unit\nthat failed on its first poll (e.g. a transient error calling\norder-management) was gone forever instead of being retried on the next\ntick.\n\nFound via a real e2e run against the live fleet: order-management''s\nfirst POST /orders after a cold start returned 500 (Kafka topic/producer\nwarm-up), the poller correctly left its watermark unadvanced for a\nretry, but the stub gateway had already discarded the seeded unit on the\nfirst PollDemand call, so it silently vanished instead of being\nre-delivered.\n\nFix: PollDemand now returns pending without clearing it. Retirement\nmoves to SubmitAcknowledgement, which is the point ReceiveNetworkDemand\nhas actually finished with an order (both its reject and acknowledge\npaths call it last-but-one, before the one irreversible step) --\nmirroring how a real network''s own cursor only advances once we have\ntold it something, not once we have merely asked.\n\nUpdated TestStubGateway_PollClearsSeededDemand (renamed to\nTestStubGateway_PollDemandRePresentsUnacknowledgedUnits) to assert the\ncorrected contract: an un-acked unit is repeated on the next poll, and\nacknowledging it is what retires it.\n\nFull suite (including architecture fitness tests) green: go test ./...","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqujsXCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHgQQACXnaxVAI8Yi8WM+ttx/hR65\nTn1kvAsa/coUPUIhejrh3vFIwUHjfAj3w8qmV/6fpfhJUBtnONfVUBIG/n6DDa+s\n9Ld5zIzTpArznQheOtdio8SRdi0JFsU2tSLDFPOvNrzkF6cw8tjY6JL6gbV45q2U\nyN39yiY23ZLnPA0t5f3DBzBIhj3Vo/B7cME8lqLQP8KDSSZqYYcOf3MMwHWtlS35\nHpijJvE97qc4c5DyIxwSF6EXxkSbAAtZrYi+IP3heCNhF2m2xzEYVW81R8EnDOX9\nOWM6tSWlwCgikp2I7uv/RWRyj5ZPC06+XxVGzEmBVAUx16vOz7pgaqDoBk85GMYP\nBQ9LMU5HlC83FhMSeJ1/yrtTZXPQIGiyqqmEjxhRhFCdftu60p2REWL73oyEbema\nBHXqvCicH2HOx2mabOu5i4VOtZ4qe2IxM2fikHwK5V0E+pwMJ8OE7SZzuDS9gl92\n6bel627VQkLFdwsiq5KP03X6legvkvYB/gaNgPKsAeKY8hFuPUb3nUPHrRMzAYNh\ntyr09lX3GEl1Qzq4f4lJisVDoVEib3JWQ0HeYHQND9TRFJ5oDoBTvo3AA+PRaHa9\nw0/BUjlDXDyNDP7SnlEgzChBLo3hOEHgiWHUNXCEzKS+/t2RHPJhewpukAhyDvZh\nhzdhR5jh1zuQT8UnCXFV\n=zEyP\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T10:02:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKGQ0ZGYzYjc5MjRkMDFjOGFmYjk2MGFmNTE5MGY5NzM2MjFiMWQ1MWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1","sha":"746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1"}],"sha":"d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/d4df3b7924d01c8afb960af5190f973621b1d51d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:00:05Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T04:00:05Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (#24)\n\nPort order-management''s Phase 3 scalability reference (PR #110, ADR\n0026) to network-fulfillment, adapted to this repo''s own chart shape,\nfive-binary set, and Kafka consumer-group convention -- and folded in\nwarehouse-infra PR #43 (PgBouncer in front of the shared Postgres\ninstance), which had not yet landed when ADR 0026 was written.\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed workload,\ndefault-disabled in values.yaml so this PR changes no production\nreplica counts on merge:\n\n- api (cmd/netfulfil): min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP HTTP\n  plus an inbound poller and ack-deadline sweep, both driven by this\n  process''s own ticker; no inbound Kafka consumer at all, so no\n  consumer-group question exists for this Deployment.\n- analytics-reports (cmd/netfulfil-reports): min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU.\n  Stateless read-only REST reader over its own read-only pgxpool.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving.\n- analytics-projector: deliberately EXCLUDED (no autoscaling block at\n  all, not just disabled). Its Kafka consumer group id is minted fresh\n  per process instance and replays from the earliest offset on every\n  start -- the opposite convention from order-management''s stable\n  shared group. N>1 replicas would each independently replay the\n  entire analytics topic and double/triple-project every historical\n  event.\n- mcp: deliberately EXCLUDED, same reason as order-management''s mcp --\n  in-memory per-process MCP session state, no sessionAffinity on the\n  Service.\n\nEach HPA-eligible Deployment template now guards its own `replicas:`\nfield with `{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so the HPA\ncontroller is the sole owner of .spec.replicas once enabled, instead of\nfighting a hardcoded value on every reconcile. Verified with helm\ntemplate: 0 HPAs / all replicas fields present by default; exactly 3\nHPAs render with all three enabled; enabling only one HPA drops only\nthat Deployment''s replicas field, leaving the others untouched.\n\npgxpool tuning, MaxConns + statement_timeout via AfterConnect on every\npool (OLTP, analytics writer, analytics reader), matching\norder-management''s values with one documented deviation: the OLTP\npool''s MaxConns=10 is now a client-side concurrency bound behind\nPgBouncer (transaction-pooling mode) rather than a literal reserved\nslice of the shared instance''s max_connections=100, since every\nservice''s OLTP DATABASE_URL already points at PgBouncer per\nwarehouse-infra PR #43. The two analytics pools stay direct against\nPostgres (mirroring PR #43''s own OLTP/analytics split), so their\nMaxConns=5 each keeps the same literal-connection accounting ADR 0026\nused.\n\nNew test: pool_limits_integration_test.go, testcontainers-backed\n(-tags=integration), proving statement_timeout actually gets applied\nto every new connection (a real Postgres cancels a pg_sleep past the\nconfigured timeout, SQLSTATE 57014) and MaxConns is a real enforced\nceiling (a further Acquire past the limit blocks until context\ndeadline), ported from order-management''s identically-shaped test.\n\nNew ADR: docs/adr/0006-horizontal-autoscaling-and-pgxpool-tuning.md,\ndocumenting the per-workload HPA table, the two exclusions and why,\nthe pgxpool numbers, and the PgBouncer-driven deviation from ADR\n0026''s connection-budget accounting.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt -l (clean),\nmake check (fmt-check/vet/build/lint/test -race), make arch-test,\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (real Postgres via\ntestcontainers), make coverage (95.7%, gate 90%), helm lint, helm\ntemplate (default and all-enabled/mixed-enabled scenarios), and the\nchart''s existing Python wiring tests (test_credential_wiring.py,\ntest_data_files.py).\n\nRefs: order-management PR #110 / ADR 0026, warehouse-infra PR #43,\nADR 0004, ADR 0005.","tree":{"sha":"b6f71572cc91b0d798f9a968a24b3916e2ccaf65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/b6f71572cc91b0d798f9a968a24b3916e2ccaf65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1","verification":{"payload":"tree b6f71572cc91b0d798f9a968a24b3916e2ccaf65\nparent 18589710390854e440b9263bb234cb19e21f5bdb\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790568005 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790568005 -0300\n\nfeat(scalability): per-workload HPA + pgxpool MaxConns/statement_timeout tuning (#24)\n\nPort order-management''s Phase 3 scalability reference (PR #110, ADR\n0026) to network-fulfillment, adapted to this repo''s own chart shape,\nfive-binary set, and Kafka consumer-group convention -- and folded in\nwarehouse-infra PR #43 (PgBouncer in front of the shared Postgres\ninstance), which had not yet landed when ADR 0026 was written.\n\nHPA (autoscaling/v2), one per independently-assessed workload,\ndefault-disabled in values.yaml so this PR changes no production\nreplica counts on merge:\n\n- api (cmd/netfulfil): min 1 / max 4 / 70% CPU. Stateless OLTP HTTP\n  plus an inbound poller and ack-deadline sweep, both driven by this\n  process''s own ticker; no inbound Kafka consumer at all, so no\n  consumer-group question exists for this Deployment.\n- analytics-reports (cmd/netfulfil-reports): min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU.\n  Stateless read-only REST reader over its own read-only pgxpool.\n- frontend: min 1 / max 3 / 70% CPU. Pure static-asset serving.\n- analytics-projector: deliberately EXCLUDED (no autoscaling block at\n  all, not just disabled). Its Kafka consumer group id is minted fresh\n  per process instance and replays from the earliest offset on every\n  start -- the opposite convention from order-management''s stable\n  shared group. N>1 replicas would each independently replay the\n  entire analytics topic and double/triple-project every historical\n  event.\n- mcp: deliberately EXCLUDED, same reason as order-management''s mcp --\n  in-memory per-process MCP session state, no sessionAffinity on the\n  Service.\n\nEach HPA-eligible Deployment template now guards its own `replicas:`\nfield with `{{- if not .Values.autoscaling.<x>.enabled }}` so the HPA\ncontroller is the sole owner of .spec.replicas once enabled, instead of\nfighting a hardcoded value on every reconcile. Verified with helm\ntemplate: 0 HPAs / all replicas fields present by default; exactly 3\nHPAs render with all three enabled; enabling only one HPA drops only\nthat Deployment''s replicas field, leaving the others untouched.\n\npgxpool tuning, MaxConns + statement_timeout via AfterConnect on every\npool (OLTP, analytics writer, analytics reader), matching\norder-management''s values with one documented deviation: the OLTP\npool''s MaxConns=10 is now a client-side concurrency bound behind\nPgBouncer (transaction-pooling mode) rather than a literal reserved\nslice of the shared instance''s max_connections=100, since every\nservice''s OLTP DATABASE_URL already points at PgBouncer per\nwarehouse-infra PR #43. The two analytics pools stay direct against\nPostgres (mirroring PR #43''s own OLTP/analytics split), so their\nMaxConns=5 each keeps the same literal-connection accounting ADR 0026\nused.\n\nNew test: pool_limits_integration_test.go, testcontainers-backed\n(-tags=integration), proving statement_timeout actually gets applied\nto every new connection (a real Postgres cancels a pg_sleep past the\nconfigured timeout, SQLSTATE 57014) and MaxConns is a real enforced\nceiling (a further Acquire past the limit blocks until context\ndeadline), ported from order-management''s identically-shaped test.\n\nNew ADR: docs/adr/0006-horizontal-autoscaling-and-pgxpool-tuning.md,\ndocumenting the per-workload HPA table, the two exclusions and why,\nthe pgxpool numbers, and the PgBouncer-driven deviation from ADR\n0026''s connection-budget accounting.\n\nVerified: go build/vet (plain + -tags=integration), gofmt -l (clean),\nmake check (fmt-check/vet/build/lint/test -race), make arch-test,\ngo test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (real Postgres via\ntestcontainers), make coverage (95.7%, gate 90%), helm lint, helm\ntemplate (default and all-enabled/mixed-enabled scenarios), and the\nchart''s existing Python wiring tests (test_credential_wiring.py,\ntest_data_files.py).\n\nRefs: order-management PR #110 / ADR 0026, warehouse-infra PR #43,\nADR 0004, ADR 0005.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueZFCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAdD4QAG+E/cM2Zymyvq8wyBVfnyWB\nb/DiO4UqJlaO2r4KnekFBnrWWcEnPnIDschPSbUpcfuiGA/50m9Gq1AebRDaDKUn\nwASW6fhrIPPhhCd/6LO6ocTM4c699wIYY61dn+KT+e/sq7W3XSqWYoTr6nsqvQGR\n43Sj7E+k0HErq0Y3t5OM6l0RI16NpvVTcLv5mHfjMZT6fzEWR9EbGc931tl510TF\nBI7IW4ToqrCprafCadmZ0fFMgiA3Ip6XfvPJChHamGFDG86O9Ysx/MiwIRQixQmL\nkHhy/6GQLh0fJVxXSi99OrHhd0Aiehkm7m86XEzhYac9N7Uiwd5iTMZVWQAgR9oe\nxBiB9C1uExz7A02f6Bs7JIE2dcymvDJ4fIF2xRkORgtQQ03JyIThceH805O83uB+\nKVtKeAkhEqDt8ESF8oZarORef6iibot2W0nGDq8vl/veraFxUhKvAYDvsguf8d3T\n7cM7xfKFIuWb6283SckDh0gLTBc09CKcKFwuLQvMzwelb2Il5H5D08pZoteUTO0X\n7F88T7iigTRJEgNnSYEBj/uGL1LfTy9fFUuFpMJ/i6/JTY27ADaA38IPJ8oSp2O0\nQzmanM2G6kuXpKaAbcWgcPHhNYkkvRzWiqgpg0YERCW3Nw4zd+wU7+mUsSucoWgR\n8vMDwAefuo2L9RVxpNbm\n=OS2F\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-28T04:00:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDc0NjI3NzA4NGY0ODhjMmY5Y2Y0MmI5ZmRkMjQ2Y2U3MjYxZDViZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/18589710390854e440b9263bb234cb19e21f5bdb","sha":"18589710390854e440b9263bb234cb19e21f5bdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/18589710390854e440b9263bb234cb19e21f5bdb"}],"sha":"746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/746277084f488c2f9cf42b9fdd246ce7261d5bd1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/18589710390854e440b9263bb234cb19e21f5bdb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:35:01Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T03:35:01Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(kafka): switch outbound writers to Hash balancer for partition affinity (ADR 0005) (#23)\n\nEvery kafkago.Writer in internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/ used\n&kafkago.LeastBytes{}, which ignores Message.Key entirely when choosing\na partition (it only reads len(Key)+len(Value) to track cumulative\nbytes written). Publisher.Encode and AnalyticsPublisher.Encode already\nset Message.Key correctly (aggregateKey returns the event''s NetworkRef)\n-- so on paper every event for one NetworkRef looked like it should\nland on one partition, but LeastBytes never actually used that key for\nrouting. This was invisible while both topics ran at 1 partition;\nwarehouse-infra PR #42 scaled every business topic (including both of\nthis repo''s) from 1 to 8 partitions, which can now let a consumer\nobserve events for the same NetworkRef out of relative order.\n\nMirrors order-management''s identical fix (PR #111, ADR 0027) and the\nsame bug independently found and fixed in inventory-storage (PR #102)\nand workforce-management (PR #106).\n\nFix:\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher.go: NewPublisher''s writer\n  Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}.\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/analytics_publisher.go:\n  NewAnalyticsPublisher''s writer Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/analytics_consumer.go:\n  AnalyticsConsumer''s dlqWriter had no explicit Balancer at all\n  (kafka-go defaults that to RoundRobin, which also ignores Key) ->\n  explicit &kafkago.Hash{}, so a poison aggregate''s dead-lettered\n  events stay grouped on one DLQ partition for a future replay tool.\n  Documented the reasoning (DLQ ordering isn''t itself a live-consumer\n  correctness requirement, but consistency + the replay-tool benefit\n  make Hash the better default) in both the code comment and ADR 0005.\n\nNo Message.Key-setting logic changed anywhere -- aggregateKey and the\nDLQ path''s key-forwarding were already correct per the fleet audit.\n\nTests:\n- New internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher_integration_test.go\n  (build tag `integration`), TestPublisherKeysMessagesForSameNetworkRefOntoTheSamePartition:\n  starts a real confluentinc/confluent-local broker via Testcontainers,\n  creates an 8-partition topic, publishes 3 events for one NetworkRef\n  plus 1 for a different NetworkRef, and asserts all 3 land on the same\n  partition while the other NetworkRef''s event is independent. Verified\n  by hand that this test FAILS under the old &kafkago.LeastBytes{}\n  balancer (1 of 3 same-key messages landed on the expected partition)\n  and PASSES under &kafkago.Hash{} (3 of 3) -- proving a fake-writer\n  unit test alone would not catch this bug class.\n\nAdds ADR 0005 (docs/adr/0005-kafka-hash-balancer-for-partition-affinity.md)\nreferencing order-management PR #111 and warehouse-infra PR #42.\n\nVerified: go build ./..., go vet ./..., gofmt (clean), make check,\nmake arch-test, go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all\npass, including the new real-broker test), make coverage (95.7%, gate\n90%).","tree":{"sha":"27ed3fffc9db5b826b1a6ea46603942298012cff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/27ed3fffc9db5b826b1a6ea46603942298012cff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/18589710390854e440b9263bb234cb19e21f5bdb","verification":{"payload":"tree 27ed3fffc9db5b826b1a6ea46603942298012cff\nparent 6437e13675407cb8b54fd4909b3c727a397a5865\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790566501 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790566501 -0300\n\nfix(kafka): switch outbound writers to Hash balancer for partition affinity (ADR 0005) (#23)\n\nEvery kafkago.Writer in internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/ used\n&kafkago.LeastBytes{}, which ignores Message.Key entirely when choosing\na partition (it only reads len(Key)+len(Value) to track cumulative\nbytes written). Publisher.Encode and AnalyticsPublisher.Encode already\nset Message.Key correctly (aggregateKey returns the event''s NetworkRef)\n-- so on paper every event for one NetworkRef looked like it should\nland on one partition, but LeastBytes never actually used that key for\nrouting. This was invisible while both topics ran at 1 partition;\nwarehouse-infra PR #42 scaled every business topic (including both of\nthis repo''s) from 1 to 8 partitions, which can now let a consumer\nobserve events for the same NetworkRef out of relative order.\n\nMirrors order-management''s identical fix (PR #111, ADR 0027) and the\nsame bug independently found and fixed in inventory-storage (PR #102)\nand workforce-management (PR #106).\n\nFix:\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher.go: NewPublisher''s writer\n  Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}.\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/analytics_publisher.go:\n  NewAnalyticsPublisher''s writer Balancer -> &kafkago.Hash{}.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka/analytics_consumer.go:\n  AnalyticsConsumer''s dlqWriter had no explicit Balancer at all\n  (kafka-go defaults that to RoundRobin, which also ignores Key) ->\n  explicit &kafkago.Hash{}, so a poison aggregate''s dead-lettered\n  events stay grouped on one DLQ partition for a future replay tool.\n  Documented the reasoning (DLQ ordering isn''t itself a live-consumer\n  correctness requirement, but consistency + the replay-tool benefit\n  make Hash the better default) in both the code comment and ADR 0005.\n\nNo Message.Key-setting logic changed anywhere -- aggregateKey and the\nDLQ path''s key-forwarding were already correct per the fleet audit.\n\nTests:\n- New internal/adapters/outbound/kafka/publisher_integration_test.go\n  (build tag `integration`), TestPublisherKeysMessagesForSameNetworkRefOntoTheSamePartition:\n  starts a real confluentinc/confluent-local broker via Testcontainers,\n  creates an 8-partition topic, publishes 3 events for one NetworkRef\n  plus 1 for a different NetworkRef, and asserts all 3 land on the same\n  partition while the other NetworkRef''s event is independent. Verified\n  by hand that this test FAILS under the old &kafkago.LeastBytes{}\n  balancer (1 of 3 same-key messages landed on the expected partition)\n  and PASSES under &kafkago.Hash{} (3 of 3) -- proving a fake-writer\n  unit test alone would not catch this bug class.\n\nAdds ADR 0005 (docs/adr/0005-kafka-hash-balancer-for-partition-affinity.md)\nreferencing order-management PR #111 and warehouse-infra PR #42.\n\nVerified: go build ./..., go vet ./..., gofmt (clean), make check,\nmake arch-test, go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1 (all\npass, including the new real-broker test), make coverage (95.7%, gate\n90%).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqueBlCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmpAQACtRjJbfkdlygWGvvg+aa32v\nOoSEkJoscEGOTJSRhPAWHdh0bePXtLfxvkRiduX+bK0mNWHbjklHq4ec0LmhnjWi\n0Y8LIBuR6QQeuI7RvUYPOUXQ2AZDYbev4a+6GETiOl8AaPEjsnDm+qRLL0tcQ7jx\nDyI0Q3yqRVw9T7XaS0Wf9zoe/xplxJ8A0KxoGhzGHLS694wC2BjEa7GVB5iA4Ts7\nbwtQ9VBvqJXBvnAlB+j7U+jwEE22mQK9hPCcMAb29ktA6CK4MMbtIUCtXCFLpWDB\nJgEbzBVY43sJFNtlv3Gh/fpvZzvsOIzv1ljnCGuOo6XlfS87N9EOrqDRElDDaogj\n0Wd6soyN3VdUkpa5K8lL70kF2zF874soQ+zfhVFYfkjKiSYfJNEg0FftrbQ4gcCE\nh6f1c9jueB2Ccb1I3SrwkwwNf8Q3o41Xay8ij7Oe/vAm/zbLA0aGEPfnNrtMQrpq\nkfCQLn3Es4uJ/ZYDCf7vN9FgoCluke