a397a5865"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/c32e5ecafe0f74db1594648393536ae9f5370b42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T22:55:58Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T22:55:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resilience): circuit breaker, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (ADR 0004) (#107 port) (#21)\n\nPorts order-management PR #107 / ADR 0025 to network-fulfillment,\nscoped to this repo''s actual shape (verified by reading the code, not\nassumed):\n\n- internal/resilience: shared circuit-breaker tuning (ReadyToTrip,\n  DefaultMaxRequests/Interval/Timeout) and CallTimeout deadline\n  propagation, copied verbatim from order-management''s package of the\n  same name.\n\n- ordermanagement.BreakerClient wraps Planner (the one real sync\n  cross-context HTTP client in this repo) with a single\n  sony/gobreaker/v2 breaker guarding all three methods\n  (RaiseHeldOrder/ReleaseHeldOrder/CancelHeldOrder). Planner has no\n  permissive/fail-open fallback to reuse (confirmed by reading\n  planner.go/client.go), so the OPEN-state path returns a new\n  ErrCircuitOpen rather than inventing soft-fallback semantics that\n  did not exist before. No retry added: all three calls are mutating,\n  with no idempotency-key contract to make blind retry safe.\n\n- telemetry.CircuitBreakerMetrics exposes circuit_breaker_state via a\n  dedicated Prometheus registry served at GET /metrics. This repo has\n  no OTel wiring (unlike order-management), so this goes straight to\n  prometheus/client_golang instead of re-exporting an OTel gauge.\n\n- AnalyticsConsumer (the one Kafka consumer in this repo) gets a dead-\n  letter topic (<topic>.dlq): MarkProcessed and the projection-apply\n  step are retried INDEPENDENTLY (not as one unit like\n  RepromiseConsumer) because this consumer''s dedupe gate is a separate\n  call from the state change it guards, not one atomic operation --\n  retrying the whole handler after a partial success would silently\n  skip the apply step. Exhausting a phase''s retries dead-letters the\n  raw payload with x-dlq-* headers and commits the offset, so one\n  poison event can never block its partition. Verified end to end with\n  a real testcontainers Kafka\n  (TestAnalyticsConsumer_PoisonMessage_GoesToDeadLetterTopicWithoutBlockingPartition).\n\n- GET /readyz + Readiness gate, flipped as the first step of graceful\n  shutdown in cmd/netfulfil/main.go, before the HTTP server stops and\n  before the poller/outbox relay are given a bounded wait to finish\n  in-flight work. /healthz is untouched (liveness only).\n\n- apis/openapi.yaml documents the new /readyz and /metrics routes;\n  spectral lint passes.\n\nDeliberately deferred (documented in ADR 0004, not silently skipped):\n- internal/adapters/outbound/network/gateway.go (NETWORK_MODE=\n  stub/sandbox/live): no real sandbox/live client exists yet, so there\n  is nothing to wrap in a breaker.\n- No dedicated backoff wrapper on the poller: its existing\n  ticker-paced retry is already bounded backpressure, not blind\n  retry-forever; its real cross-context risk (Planner) is already\n  covered by the breaker above.\n\nVerification:\n- go build/vet, plain and -tags=integration: clean.\n- gofmt -l .: clean.\n- make check (fmt-check vet build lint test): clean, 0 lint issues.\n- make arch-test: all hexagonal fitness tests pass, including\n  TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers.\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: clean, including the\n  new DLQ integration test against a real Kafka container.\n- make coverage: 95.7% before and after (unchanged; this change adds\n  no domain/application code), gate is 90%.\n- helm lint charts/network-fulfillment: clean (charts untouched).\n- spectral lint apis/openapi.yaml: clean.\n\nNew direct dependencies: sony/gobreaker/v2 v2.4.0 (matches\norder-management), github.com/prometheus/client_golang (new to this\nrepo), github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-go/modules/kafka\nv0.44.0 (test-only, matches this repo''s existing testcontainers\nversion). cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted from indirect to direct.","tree":{"sha":"c774396bc5ee24823b9802ba1e2da4b9cd844bd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/c774396bc5ee24823b9802ba1e2da4b9cd844bd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/c32e5ecafe0f74db1594648393536ae9f5370b42","verification":{"payload":"tree c774396bc5ee24823b9802ba1e2da4b9cd844bd5\nparent 4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790549758 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790549758 -0300\n\nfeat(resilience): circuit breaker, Kafka DLQ, graceful shutdown (ADR 0004) (#107 port) (#21)\n\nPorts order-management PR #107 / ADR 0025 to network-fulfillment,\nscoped to this repo''s actual shape (verified by reading the code, not\nassumed):\n\n- internal/resilience: shared circuit-breaker tuning (ReadyToTrip,\n  DefaultMaxRequests/Interval/Timeout) and CallTimeout deadline\n  propagation, copied verbatim from order-management''s package of the\n  same name.\n\n- ordermanagement.BreakerClient wraps Planner (the one real sync\n  cross-context HTTP client in this repo) with a single\n  sony/gobreaker/v2 breaker guarding all three methods\n  (RaiseHeldOrder/ReleaseHeldOrder/CancelHeldOrder). Planner has no\n  permissive/fail-open fallback to reuse (confirmed by reading\n  planner.go/client.go), so the OPEN-state path returns a new\n  ErrCircuitOpen rather than inventing soft-fallback semantics that\n  did not exist before. No retry added: all three calls are mutating,\n  with no idempotency-key contract to make blind retry safe.\n\n- telemetry.CircuitBreakerMetrics exposes circuit_breaker_state via a\n  dedicated Prometheus registry served at GET /metrics. This repo has\n  no OTel wiring (unlike order-management), so this goes straight to\n  prometheus/client_golang instead of re-exporting an OTel gauge.\n\n- AnalyticsConsumer (the one Kafka consumer in this repo) gets a dead-\n  letter topic (<topic>.dlq): MarkProcessed and the projection-apply\n  step are retried INDEPENDENTLY (not as one unit like\n  RepromiseConsumer) because this consumer''s dedupe gate is a separate\n  call from the state change it guards, not one atomic operation --\n  retrying the whole handler after a partial success would silently\n  skip the apply step. Exhausting a phase''s retries dead-letters the\n  raw payload with x-dlq-* headers and commits the offset, so one\n  poison event can never block its partition. Verified end to end with\n  a real testcontainers Kafka\n  (TestAnalyticsConsumer_PoisonMessage_GoesToDeadLetterTopicWithoutBlockingPartition).\n\n- GET /readyz + Readiness gate, flipped as the first step of graceful\n  shutdown in cmd/netfulfil/main.go, before the HTTP server stops and\n  before the poller/outbox relay are given a bounded wait to finish\n  in-flight work. /healthz is untouched (liveness only).\n\n- apis/openapi.yaml documents the new /readyz and /metrics routes;\n  spectral lint passes.\n\nDeliberately deferred (documented in ADR 0004, not silently skipped):\n- internal/adapters/outbound/network/gateway.go (NETWORK_MODE=\n  stub/sandbox/live): no real sandbox/live client exists yet, so there\n  is nothing to wrap in a breaker.\n- No dedicated backoff wrapper on the poller: its existing\n  ticker-paced retry is already bounded backpressure, not blind\n  retry-forever; its real cross-context risk (Planner) is already\n  covered by the breaker above.\n\nVerification:\n- go build/vet, plain and -tags=integration: clean.\n- gofmt -l .: clean.\n- make check (fmt-check vet build lint test): clean, 0 lint issues.\n- make arch-test: all hexagonal fitness tests pass, including\n  TestKafkaIntegrationTestsUseTestcontainers.\n- go test -tags=integration ./... -race -count=1: clean, including the\n  new DLQ integration test against a real Kafka container.\n- make coverage: 95.7% before and after (unchanged; this change adds\n  no domain/application code), gate is 90%.\n- helm lint charts/network-fulfillment: clean (charts untouched).\n- spectral lint apis/openapi.yaml: clean.\n\nNew direct dependencies: sony/gobreaker/v2 v2.4.0 (matches\norder-management), github.com/prometheus/client_golang (new to this\nrepo), github.com/testcontainers/testcontainers-go/modules/kafka\nv0.44.0 (test-only, matches this repo''s existing testcontainers\nversion). cenkalti/backoff/v4 promoted from indirect to direct.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquZ7+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAADkgQAJcflhcWSNK+/him1x2mLgA6\nQxW5yuey1eOttHyXL83/iSy+N9fg8tOGleI3vBgTtWiEjlilIh+GtD/1sIpFMkeN\n60I0Jl4uWRyNXFHIAJu23fUCRf2r5ok8jznD1TMhr2t/hvI6CjkttU6UVLRC4jjR\nD1mp7FzqMRtuGNk6VI9G7Et5lmfiWGg1NSSLk+fIC5uXd6bYPIH+brr+w7J/0l1e\nHBVkjcHtqLy9diKX0xD7Wck3Ua59yQ+1AgP/bSAeqEVBnqNefr3Z0V5woTG+N/+O\nw4yaaJHPhSkKx+I5nQqIsapgWVpjs+UKCu4G7fsXSCg4IwKP24l5a5o2PQ/3pC4Y\n0fm4SYitE5LmKb8mb9UADciZ1QzWDdRzKOZIQWDhamHoUInDXzHg27p21RF0oMsT\n+iatuJLgE5saiRy2SE6sl62i7xE/b5rosRl3fjDDCKdr1n21z05WiDwqM1lBfYvj\nxRAaGkEjZRqthLTBjcX/tm0sstPjXN58SEnEKtfkpfTbPGRboqWk8oeLHYgx/Ha7\nY3X0GDB9fFak+wYJDdG69BIqIy6PRPOdjQqsegzxWSxlWPcJumw07sJ5arAqDicV\nrKrQt9+x2iSNLwYUs8EAI7jWWf7Lmtq7ytm6jFm5BMjQqg7OyjiPITVckudlXKZX\nn6Y3AWl/3WFSQdcexIBm\n=YrKX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T22:55:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/c32e5ecafe0f74db1594648393536ae9f5370b42","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKGMzMmU1ZWNhZmUwZjc0ZGIxNTk0NjQ4MzkzNTM2YWU5ZjUzNzBiNDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db","sha":"4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db"}],"sha":"c32e5ecafe0f74db1594648393536ae9f5370b42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/c32e5ecafe0f74db1594648393536ae9f5370b42"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T01:24:40Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T01:24:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(outbox): transactional outbox + relay for the Kafka publish path (ADR 0003) (#20)\n\nSave a NetworkOrder and publish its domain event(s) to both the\nintegration and analytics Kafka topics in one Postgres transaction,\ndraining an outbox_events table with a background relay, activated only\nwhen DATABASE_URL is configured (mirrors the existing in-memory/stub\nmode matrix otherwise).\n\n- ports.UnitOfWork (Execute(ctx, fn) error), optional; nil = run\n  Save+Publish back to back as before.\n- usecases.atomically helper; ReceiveNetworkDemand and\n  SweepAcknowledgementDeadlines wrap every Save+Publish pair.\n- postgres.UnitOfWork, querierFrom/beginOrJoin, NetworkOrderRepo.Save\n  joins an outer transaction when one is bound to the context.\n- postgres.OutboxPublisher (ports.EventPublisher over outbox_events) and\n  postgres.OutboxRelay (SKIP LOCKED, stops at a failed row, per-aggregate\n  ordering preserved, retries on the next pass).\n- kafka.Publisher/AnalyticsPublisher split Encode from Send so the relay\n  can forward already-encoded messages without re-deriving envelopes.\n- migrations/0002_outbox.{up,down}.sql.\n- cmd/netfulfil/main.go: DATABASE_URL + EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka now wires\n  the outbox publisher and starts the relay goroutine with graceful\n  shutdown; every other combination in the existing matrix is unchanged.\n- docs/adr/0003-transactional-outbox.md; README env var table.\n\nTests: usecases/unit_of_work_test.go (unit), postgres/outbox_integration_test.go\n(testcontainers Postgres, no external DATABASE_URL, no t.Skip). Full\nsuite, arch-test and integration suite pass locally (see PR body for\ncommands and coverage numbers).","tree":{"sha":"0832e012f855006866d478cc9cc36d0d161d9155","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/0832e012f855006866d478cc9cc36d0d161d9155"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db","verification":{"payload":"tree 0832e012f855006866d478cc9cc36d0d161d9155\nparent 0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790472280 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790472280 -0300\n\nfeat(outbox): transactional outbox + relay for the Kafka publish path (ADR 0003) (#20)\n\nSave a NetworkOrder and publish its domain event(s) to both the\nintegration and analytics Kafka topics in one Postgres transaction,\ndraining an outbox_events table with a background relay, activated only\nwhen DATABASE_URL is configured (mirrors the existing in-memory/stub\nmode matrix otherwise).\n\n- ports.UnitOfWork (Execute(ctx, fn) error), optional; nil = run\n  Save+Publish back to back as before.\n- usecases.atomically helper; ReceiveNetworkDemand and\n  SweepAcknowledgementDeadlines wrap every Save+Publish pair.\n- postgres.UnitOfWork, querierFrom/beginOrJoin, NetworkOrderRepo.Save\n  joins an outer transaction when one is bound to the context.\n- postgres.OutboxPublisher (ports.EventPublisher over outbox_events) and\n  postgres.OutboxRelay (SKIP LOCKED, stops at a failed row, per-aggregate\n  ordering preserved, retries on the next pass).\n- kafka.Publisher/AnalyticsPublisher split Encode from Send so the relay\n  can forward already-encoded messages without re-deriving envelopes.\n- migrations/0002_outbox.{up,down}.sql.\n- cmd/netfulfil/main.go: DATABASE_URL + EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka now wires\n  the outbox publisher and starts the relay goroutine with graceful\n  shutdown; every other combination in the existing matrix is unchanged.\n- docs/adr/0003-transactional-outbox.md; README env var table.\n\nTests: usecases/unit_of_work_test.go (unit), postgres/outbox_integration_test.go\n(testcontainers Postgres, no external DATABASE_URL, no t.Skip). Full\nsuite, arch-test and integration suite pass locally (see PR body for\ncommands and coverage numbers).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquHBYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAntEQAD7VGY49fNpCNxBzBG9e7hI7\nnxqze8hO86Ji27eJBifDUA1ESLE6pZZrJK633ijUKNcXbJx7/HUchKFETjs0lIQ8\nr/gbD+y6PGW7i/SXllYg62OpV4CduqKSRTLp6LfOy3IdmGLxmmNxcvdGVrDX35aq\nLlnsTFyi8dRZvlkbJO8v5p2CTS74CTPz3cSyuDfY6SJc/+B+iqPyoDPJmiOsDVG2\nfL0efAMkVrdMuyt9ktHqFOX/aaqC3O4yeYuuaO7yPQW68dhR2OBJncgV7r151Z1j\n97PKpFWtFwJsxsrWIp6pETqDSLYI3WlSUj5oF9KWifCJSr7w5rlpxBpk78uJSEeG\n2ukAX4l/FUgII+T0pRjQ4Ew8/U+Vqd1qhDSXH9muIcVhivr66qQ/rk/GXno0Jgzd\nkvhbcfJyLloNiDst/mVyEIj50BLYznPHQyQWgMC0VjAg8tqbP0lnaYyFHdznb7YQ\nzJUD3Ik2GhMwAnjdYy6fUOXMlH71tvZB/L3MVeVUHnOz7+ul4QsMQKgv5irYiWJl\nKG4urgXVT6BEnpwukrfZxiEgaZp4SpmGcq3o7I8REZGwEWE3QKJ+1OawPvYalh/0\nOFP2phvyodwUV5IDIVMDS3UsIE+CfPcJEPbzMzdNN0bz5MnOz8yQCfx/x557dWnO\n6601PRGKbbnapsGAcSG2\n=esOr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T01:24:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDRlZmJiNDRkZjE5NWZiZmI5YTRkZDA3NWE0YmIwYzRkMTM5NjcyZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7","sha":"0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7"}],"sha":"4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/4efbb44df195fbfb9a4dd075a4bb0c4d139672db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:27:51Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:27:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: MCP server + analytics data product (ADR 0002, fleet parity) (#18)\n\n* feat(domain): add NetworkOrder domain events and wire use cases\n\nAdds NetworkOrderReceived, NetworkOrderAcknowledged, NetworkOrderRejected\n(with a RejectionReason distinguishing untranslatable-SKU vs infeasible\ndeadline vs missed acknowledgement window), and NetworkOrderShipmentConfirmed\nto internal/domain/shared, mirroring the fleet''s lightweight DomainEvent\nconvention (EventName/OccurredAt). Wires ReceiveNetworkDemand and\nSweepAcknowledgementDeadlines to emit them via the existing EventPublisher\nport. Full table-driven test coverage for emission order, payload fields,\nand publish-failure propagation.\n\n* feat(events): add Kafka integration+analytics publishers, analytics data model\n\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka: Publisher (warehouse.network-fulfillment.events)\n  and AnalyticsPublisher (warehouse.network-fulfillment.analytics), both trace-free.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka: AnalyticsConsumer, idempotent on event_id via\n  ProcessedEvents, unique-per-instance consumer group helper (NewUniqueConsumerGroup).\n- internal/analytics/report: pure read-model catalogue (Row/AcknowledgementReport/\n  ReportQuery) + ports (ProjectionStore/ReportStore), no domain/application imports.\n- internal/adapters/outbound/analyticsstore: MemoryStore (tests), PostgresProjection\n  (sole writer, idempotent via analytics_processed_events claim), PostgresReport\n  (read-only reader + FreshnessLag), ConsumedEventsRepo (consumer dedupe gate).\n- migrations/analytics/0001_report.{up,down}.sql: acknowledgement_rollup +\n  analytics_processed_events + analytics_consumed_events.\n- cmd/netfulfil/main.go: EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka now fans out to both topics via\n  fanOutPublisher; unset keeps the existing log publisher (outbound/events package).\n- internal/architecture: arch-go rules for the new analytics region (self-contained,\n  and the OLTP domain/application layers must not import it or its store).\n\nAll new code has table-driven unit tests; go build/vet/test pass.\n\n* feat(analytics): add projector/reports binaries and reports HTTP handler\n\n- cmd/netfulfil-projector: sole analytics-DB writer, unique consumer group\n  per instance, runs analytics migrations on start.\n- cmd/netfulfil-reports: read-only reports server over a read-only pgxpool.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/reports_handler.go: GET /reports/acknowledgement\n  and /reports/acknowledgement/freshness, RFC 7807 problem+json errors,\n  chi router (NewReportsRouter), mirroring facility-layout''s template.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/logging.go: chi RequestLogger, used only by\n  the reports router (the OLTP server stays a plain net/http mux).\n\ngo build/vet/test pass; full reports_handler_test.go table-driven suite added.\n\n* feat(mcp): add read-only MCP server (3 tools, resource, prompt)\n\ncmd/mcp/main.go is a new independent deployable exposing 3 read-only\nMCP tools over Streamable HTTP: get_network_order, list_network_orders,\nget_acknowledgement_report (wraps the reports REST service). Follows\nfacility-layout''s internal/adapters/inbound/mcp structural template\n(server.go, tools.go, report_tool.go, resources.go, prompts.go),\nadapted to this repo''s domain and its no-OTel convention (AGENTS.md).\n\nEvery tool is ReadOnlyHint:true; no write tool is registered, matching\nthis context''s read-only ADR-0001 stance. Adds ports.NetworkOrderRepo.\nListAll (memory + postgres implementations) to back list_network_orders\nwithout widening ListUnanswered''s semantics.\n\nFull unit test coverage: tools_test.go, report_tool_test.go,\nserver_test.go.\n\n* feat(docker): build and ship all 4 binaries (netfulfil, netfulfil-projector, netfulfil-reports, mcp)\n\nVerified with a real docker build: all 4 binaries present in the\nruntime image at /app, plus both migrations/ (OLTP) and\nmigrations/analytics/ (analytics) trees. This closes the exact gap\nthat bit process-path-management PR#26 and PR#28 (docker-publish never\nruns on non-main PRs, so a missing binary is only caught at live\ndeploy).\n\n* feat(deploy): multi-binary Dockerfile + MCP/analytics chart templates\n\nAdds Helm templates for the three new workloads (mcp, netfulfil-projector,\nnetfulfil-reports) alongside the existing OLTP deployment:\n\n- _helpers.tpl: name helpers for mcp/projector/reports/analytics-secret.\n- deployment.yaml/service.yaml: app.kubernetes.io/component: api label,\n  so the OLTP Service''s selector cannot widen to catch the new pods\n  (this fleet''s proven recurring Service-selector-collision bug).\n- mcp-deployment.yaml/mcp-service.yaml: the read-only MCP server,\n  component: mcp, HTTP_ADDR default :8090 (cmd/mcp/main.go).\n- projector-deployment.yaml: the analytics writer, component:\n  analytics-projector, no Service (nothing calls it over HTTP).\n- reports-deployment.yaml (with an embedded Service): the read-only\n  reports reader, component: analytics-reports, HTTP_ADDR default :8092\n  (cmd/netfulfil-reports/main.go).\n- analytics-secret.yaml: holds ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL, gated on\n  analytics.enabled and skipped when analytics.database.existingSecret\n  is set — the existingSecret/url pattern the OLTP database.* block\n  already uses in this same chart.\n- values.yaml: mcp:/analytics:/kafka: blocks (all opt-in, enabled:\n  false by default) plus config.eventPublisher (log|kafka) wired into\n  the OLTP deployment''s env so EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka fans domain events\n  out onto both the integration and analytics topics from one flag.\n\nVerified with a real docker build + docker run ... ls /app showing all\nfour binaries (netfulfil, netfulfil-projector, netfulfil-reports, mcp)\npresent in the image.\n\n* test(coverage): close remaining error-propagation branches + document measured mutation baseline\n\n- coverage_gap_test.go: exercises non-ErrUnknownProduct translation\n  failures, domain-construction failures, and the reject/acknowledge\n  gateway-submit + second-publish failure paths that only fire once\n  the first publish already succeeded.\n- network_order_test.go: pins AcknowledgementWindow''s literal value\n  (24h) instead of deriving the test''s expectation from the same\n  constant under test, so mutating the constant is actually caught.\n- report_tool.go: simplify a query-struct passthrough.\n- .gremlins.yaml: document the real gremlins unleash ./internal/domain/networkorder\n  measurement this repo''s thresholds are set below (100% efficacy,\n  93.33% mutant coverage; 14 killed / 0 lived / 1 not-coverable const).\n- go.mod/go.sum: chi bumped 5.2.1 -> 5.2.2 (go mod tidy).","tree":{"sha":"715e570a1bb56dfed91c819acd34eebbf9e5f154","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/715e570a1bb56dfed91c819acd34eebbf9e5f154"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7","verification":{"payload":"tree 715e570a1bb56dfed91c819acd34eebbf9e5f154\nparent 9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790461671 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790461671 -0300\n\nfeat: MCP server + analytics data product (ADR 0002, fleet parity) (#18)\n\n* feat(domain): add NetworkOrder domain events and wire use cases\n\nAdds NetworkOrderReceived, NetworkOrderAcknowledged, NetworkOrderRejected\n(with a RejectionReason distinguishing untranslatable-SKU vs infeasible\ndeadline vs missed acknowledgement window), and NetworkOrderShipmentConfirmed\nto internal/domain/shared, mirroring the fleet''s lightweight DomainEvent\nconvention (EventName/OccurredAt). Wires ReceiveNetworkDemand and\nSweepAcknowledgementDeadlines to emit them via the existing EventPublisher\nport. Full table-driven test coverage for emission order, payload fields,\nand publish-failure propagation.\n\n* feat(events): add Kafka integration+analytics publishers, analytics data model\n\n- internal/adapters/outbound/kafka: Publisher (warehouse.network-fulfillment.events)\n  and AnalyticsPublisher (warehouse.network-fulfillment.analytics), both trace-free.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/kafka: AnalyticsConsumer, idempotent on event_id via\n  ProcessedEvents, unique-per-instance consumer group helper (NewUniqueConsumerGroup).\n- internal/analytics/report: pure read-model catalogue (Row/AcknowledgementReport/\n  ReportQuery) + ports (ProjectionStore/ReportStore), no domain/application imports.\n- internal/adapters/outbound/analyticsstore: MemoryStore (tests), PostgresProjection\n  (sole writer, idempotent via analytics_processed_events claim), PostgresReport\n  (read-only reader + FreshnessLag), ConsumedEventsRepo (consumer dedupe gate).\n- migrations/analytics/0001_report.{up,down}.sql: acknowledgement_rollup +\n  analytics_processed_events + analytics_consumed_events.\n- cmd/netfulfil/main.go: EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka now fans out to both topics via\n  fanOutPublisher; unset keeps the existing log publisher (outbound/events package).\n- internal/architecture: arch-go rules for the new analytics region (self-contained,\n  and the OLTP domain/application layers must not import it or its store).\n\nAll new code has table-driven unit tests; go build/vet/test pass.\n\n* feat(analytics): add projector/reports binaries and reports HTTP handler\n\n- cmd/netfulfil-projector: sole analytics-DB writer, unique consumer group\n  per instance, runs analytics migrations on start.\n- cmd/netfulfil-reports: read-only reports server over a read-only pgxpool.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/reports_handler.go: GET /reports/acknowledgement\n  and /reports/acknowledgement/freshness, RFC 7807 problem+json errors,\n  chi router (NewReportsRouter), mirroring facility-layout''s template.\n- internal/adapters/inbound/http/logging.go: chi RequestLogger, used only by\n  the reports router (the OLTP server stays a plain net/http mux).\n\ngo build/vet/test pass; full reports_handler_test.go table-driven suite added.\n\n* feat(mcp): add read-only MCP server (3 tools, resource, prompt)\n\ncmd/mcp/main.go is a new independent deployable exposing 3 read-only\nMCP tools over Streamable HTTP: get_network_order, list_network_orders,\nget_acknowledgement_report (wraps the reports REST service). Follows\nfacility-layout''s internal/adapters/inbound/mcp structural template\n(server.go, tools.go, report_tool.go, resources.go, prompts.go),\nadapted to this repo''s domain and its no-OTel convention (AGENTS.md).\n\nEvery tool is ReadOnlyHint:true; no write tool is registered, matching\nthis context''s read-only ADR-0001 stance. Adds ports.NetworkOrderRepo.\nListAll (memory + postgres implementations) to back list_network_orders\nwithout widening ListUnanswered''s semantics.\n\nFull unit test coverage: tools_test.go, report_tool_test.go,\nserver_test.go.\n\n* feat(docker): build and ship all 4 binaries (netfulfil, netfulfil-projector, netfulfil-reports, mcp)\n\nVerified with a real docker build: all 4 binaries present in the\nruntime image at /app, plus both migrations/ (OLTP) and\nmigrations/analytics/ (analytics) trees. This closes the exact gap\nthat bit process-path-management PR#26 and PR#28 (docker-publish never\nruns on non-main PRs, so a missing binary is only caught at live\ndeploy).\n\n* feat(deploy): multi-binary Dockerfile + MCP/analytics chart templates\n\nAdds Helm templates for the three new workloads (mcp, netfulfil-projector,\nnetfulfil-reports) alongside the existing OLTP deployment:\n\n- _helpers.tpl: name helpers for mcp/projector/reports/analytics-secret.\n- deployment.yaml/service.yaml: app.kubernetes.io/component: api label,\n  so the OLTP Service''s selector cannot widen to catch the new pods\n  (this fleet''s proven recurring Service-selector-collision bug).\n- mcp-deployment.yaml/mcp-service.yaml: the read-only MCP server,\n  component: mcp, HTTP_ADDR default :8090 (cmd/mcp/main.go).\n- projector-deployment.yaml: the analytics writer, component:\n  analytics-projector, no Service (nothing calls it over HTTP).\n- reports-deployment.yaml (with an embedded Service): the read-only\n  reports reader, component: analytics-reports, HTTP_ADDR default :8092\n  (cmd/netfulfil-reports/main.go).\n- analytics-secret.yaml: holds ANALYTICS_DATABASE_URL, gated on\n  analytics.enabled and skipped when analytics.database.existingSecret\n  is set — the existingSecret/url pattern the OLTP database.* block\n  already uses in this same chart.\n- values.yaml: mcp:/analytics:/kafka: blocks (all opt-in, enabled:\n  false by default) plus config.eventPublisher (log|kafka) wired into\n  the OLTP deployment''s env so EVENT_PUBLISHER=kafka fans domain events\n  out onto both the integration and analytics topics from one flag.\n\nVerified with a real docker build + docker run ... ls /app showing all\nfour binaries (netfulfil, netfulfil-projector, netfulfil-reports, mcp)\npresent in the image.\n\n* test(coverage): close remaining error-propagation branches + document measured mutation baseline\n\n- coverage_gap_test.go: exercises non-ErrUnknownProduct translation\n  failures, domain-construction failures, and the reject/acknowledge\n  gateway-submit + second-publish failure paths that only fire once\n  the first publish already succeeded.\n- network_order_test.go: pins AcknowledgementWindow''s literal value\n  (24h) instead of deriving the test''s expectation from the same\n  constant under test, so mutating the constant is actually caught.\n- report_tool.go: simplify a query-struct passthrough.\n- .gremlins.yaml: document the real gremlins unleash ./internal/domain/networkorder\n  measurement this repo''s thresholds are set below (100% efficacy,\n  93.33% mutant coverage; 14 killed / 0 lived / 1 not-coverable const).\n- go.mod/go.sum: chi bumped 5.2.1 -> 5.2.2 (go mod tidy).","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquEbnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA56IQAABS8FK/yuBQTpQHTsYGKOW7\nJGsOUbthnY3KE/BpifKqTnK4MR3t63zGMEaLYrM+XNh0J382XdneVWrMNHmocTHc\n0sMqSPgrqRAb9RkI84PKMRp6g8sZ3mqe6UCj2BJzz3XPFgV+eAIfl3/+7EX3tz5U\n2MUAHPA180EyxHNYW8bYo+i8vWQURCzbEML2ZMr87uB/R2jjT9G+K1vw+3TYWgTZ\nLnBZhlEW39hjHnxjuOfW/tXm6+tQ9atwMgUb1nc27hfWldYa1oRkiMeJ6AWimcyV\nEt8Qnjre2BIMwmeDD6fvXCLfPgPtQYPlp84v69stQDA9IH7kPuJQnwtnlLg4lzzv\n4FfSMZQuAnM2/uvwK8DVuxTd8AXk4hxWAg9CnNtlGG6Kc7fwsa6hTjnCOlYoQm1H\nOmqqR2NtxIUYBSHTBym0P82ilS1eaian5g4i7tHylKcmheMrLrUyiLVFxs3YBmgn\nFxWw1r1pRYiUxs6L+nUg+OcNeomKYw9EEsF0pC4rOeHpbIlYyMuXYnHhnzN2jY7F\ndyZIuo8ypnleWHTj9VOjCYRDBaJU6tKgDNoIIpqwqWP2rXnXvIrKyGc1k556CC2j\ndIXlKoQbt4vG9xc9t/QVdiGnz2g4Bf88UxEh1wBbAjEi5HxgvD0YFmbiftBmrxfj\nQYTXtev6p92GRaGxByW5\n=VcqL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:27:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDBiNWZhMGY3YTlhZThmNDAwYjBkODUxYTQ1N2QyZThkNGE3MTdiZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2","sha":"9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2"}],"sha":"0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/0b5fa0f7a9ae8f400b0d851a457d2e8d4a717bf7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:17:50Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:17:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(web): scaffold netfulfil_mfe Module Federation remote (#16)\n\nAdds the web/ Module Federation micro-frontend remote for\nnetwork-fulfillment, matching every sibling bounded-context repo''s\nexisting scaffold shape.\n\n- package.json: netfulfil-mfe, dev port 5188 (fleet''s last unreserved\n  slot; 5181-5187 and 5189 are taken by the other 8 remotes), same\n  dependency versions as every sibling.\n- vite.config.ts: object-form defineConfig (never the callback form,\n  which breaks vitest.config.ts''s mergeConfig), base\n  /mfes/network-fulfillment/ at build time via process.argv, federation\n  name netfulfil_mfe exposing ./App, shared singletons react/react-dom/\n  react-router-dom/@warehouse/ui-kit.\n- src/api.ts: RFC 7807 ProblemDetails/ApiError, GET-only client -- this\n  context''s REST surface is genuinely read-only by design\n  (apis/openapi.yaml''s own description: demand arrives only by polling\n  the external network, never via HTTP intake), so there is no\n  apiPost/apiPut/apiDelete here, unlike the CRUD sibling remotes.\n- src/screens/NetworkFulfillmentScreen.tsx: DataTable of NetworkOrders\n  (networkRef, siteId, state, requiredShipBy, acknowledgeBy,\n  localOrderId) from GET /network-orders, plus a poller-health Card from\n  GET /inbound-status (polls/received/failed/unanswered/overdue, and a\n  \"never completed a pass\" indicator when `since` is absent) -- the\n  OpenAPI spec''s own rationale: a stalled poller is silent and an\n  outage is an SLA breach, not a delayed batch.\n- Component tests (Testing Library + MSW) cover loading, populated,\n  empty, poller-unhealthy (overdue>0), poller-never-succeeded (since\n  absent), and acknowledgement-overdue states, mocking the real\n  response shapes from apis/openapi.yaml.\n- Dockerfile/nginx.conf/.dockerignore copied verbatim from\n  fulfillment-execution''s remote (the simplest existing one), adjusted\n  only for repo/module names.\n\nBackend CORS wiring (internal/adapters/inbound/http/server.go):\nadds a corsMiddleware wrapping the existing read-only ServeMux, copying\nfacility-layout''s pattern (go-chi/cors, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS env\noverride, GET/OPTIONS only since this API has no writes). Reserves the\ndefault origin list as http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:5188 in\ncharts/network-fulfillment/values.yaml''s new config.corsAllowedOrigins\nkey, wired through configmap.yaml/deployment.yaml.\n\nHelm chart frontend support (charts/network-fulfillment/):\nadds templates/frontend-deployment.yaml + frontend-service.yaml (copied\nfrom facility-layout''s chart: nginx-unprivileged uid/gid 101,\nreadOnlyRootFilesystem, frontend.enabled: false by default). Both the\nexisting OLTP Deployment/Service and the new frontend workload now\ncarry a distinct app.kubernetes.io/component label (api vs frontend)\nso the OLTP Service''s selector cannot collide with the frontend\nService''s -- verified via a render assertion that each rendered Service\nselects exactly one Deployment with frontend.enabled=true.\n\nVerification (see PR description for full command output):\n- npm run build && npm run lint && npm test inside web/ -- all green\n  (10/10 tests passing).\n- npm run dev on :5188 in the background; curl / and /remoteEntry.js\n  both return 200.\n- helm lint charts/network-fulfillment and a template render with\n  --set frontend.enabled=true; rendered Service selectors each match\n  exactly one Deployment.\n- go build ./... / go test ./... across the whole repo still green\n  after the CORS middleware change.","tree":{"sha":"e085be9e1c4e048ae84e5b449b0d128d0736a7e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/e085be9e1c4e048ae84e5b449b0d128d0736a7e6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2","verification":{"payload":"tree e085be9e1c4e048ae84e5b449b0d128d0736a7e6\nparent cb3ed380a6976cf85f7f58e3b09c404831e3ca4f\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790461070 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790461070 -0300\n\nfeat(web): scaffold netfulfil_mfe Module Federation remote (#16)\n\nAdds the web/ Module Federation micro-frontend remote for\nnetwork-fulfillment, matching every sibling bounded-context repo''s\nexisting scaffold shape.\n\n- package.json: netfulfil-mfe, dev port 5188 (fleet''s last unreserved\n  slot; 5181-5187 and 5189 are taken by the other 8 remotes), same\n  dependency versions as every sibling.\n- vite.config.ts: object-form defineConfig (never the callback form,\n  which breaks vitest.config.ts''s mergeConfig), base\n  /mfes/network-fulfillment/ at build time via process.argv, federation\n  name netfulfil_mfe exposing ./App, shared singletons react/react-dom/\n  react-router-dom/@warehouse/ui-kit.\n- src/api.ts: RFC 7807 ProblemDetails/ApiError, GET-only client -- this\n  context''s REST surface is genuinely read-only by design\n  (apis/openapi.yaml''s own description: demand arrives only by polling\n  the external network, never via HTTP intake), so there is no\n  apiPost/apiPut/apiDelete here, unlike the CRUD sibling remotes.\n- src/screens/NetworkFulfillmentScreen.tsx: DataTable of NetworkOrders\n  (networkRef, siteId, state, requiredShipBy, acknowledgeBy,\n  localOrderId) from GET /network-orders, plus a poller-health Card from\n  GET /inbound-status (polls/received/failed/unanswered/overdue, and a\n  \"never completed a pass\" indicator when `since` is absent) -- the\n  OpenAPI spec''s own rationale: a stalled poller is silent and an\n  outage is an SLA breach, not a delayed batch.\n- Component tests (Testing Library + MSW) cover loading, populated,\n  empty, poller-unhealthy (overdue>0), poller-never-succeeded (since\n  absent), and acknowledgement-overdue states, mocking the real\n  response shapes from apis/openapi.yaml.\n- Dockerfile/nginx.conf/.dockerignore copied verbatim from\n  fulfillment-execution''s remote (the simplest existing one), adjusted\n  only for repo/module names.\n\nBackend CORS wiring (internal/adapters/inbound/http/server.go):\nadds a corsMiddleware wrapping the existing read-only ServeMux, copying\nfacility-layout''s pattern (go-chi/cors, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS env\noverride, GET/OPTIONS only since this API has no writes). Reserves the\ndefault origin list as http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:5188 in\ncharts/network-fulfillment/values.yaml''s new config.corsAllowedOrigins\nkey, wired through configmap.yaml/deployment.yaml.\n\nHelm chart frontend support (charts/network-fulfillment/):\nadds templates/frontend-deployment.yaml + frontend-service.yaml (copied\nfrom facility-layout''s chart: nginx-unprivileged uid/gid 101,\nreadOnlyRootFilesystem, frontend.enabled: false by default). Both the\nexisting OLTP Deployment/Service and the new frontend workload now\ncarry a distinct app.kubernetes.io/component label (api vs frontend)\nso the OLTP Service''s selector cannot collide with the frontend\nService''s -- verified via a render assertion that each rendered Service\nselects exactly one Deployment with frontend.enabled=true.\n\nVerification (see PR description for full command output):\n- npm run build && npm run lint && npm test inside web/ -- all green\n  (10/10 tests passing).\n- npm run dev on :5188 in the background; curl / and /remoteEntry.js\n  both return 200.\n- helm lint charts/network-fulfillment and a template render with\n  --set frontend.enabled=true; rendered Service selectors each match\n  exactly one Deployment.\n- go build ./... / go test ./... across the whole repo still green\n  after the CORS middleware change.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquESOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtgoQABhiIsmDdedknA+7NZssdph1\nd7gjyrU7I8Dji2LgGJxbinjfci91VS/EaVGmMMm3PvU/pkwVULFpOTV9LAIQThVN\n80Pu7YNFHNwusb1TdUR1rosHvfNJ+URp4m1oxqC3OKNrnYCCCvlJ/0vmmRApxmEh\npT+klRfvRq+XKQZcfS2vhuhGVtOIGiKSYPgtmChv/hAgsEfsQixPs9OTIBO7amW/\n60UQBu8GvdfcNsyTNaR5SX+7aSUE/3+BOfTVeCweUIgIXL61Jcv7D4YdbzjCdepU\nut48U5R2u2l74Qh8V1h7xRoh3i2XraE8wBGCk8dFnFkaUDTjWy8wWOX4x0AQHOu3\nusvw8DIU+2zOfrVKopIKyJ8ncQxw1XG3rxaGysTWUPetu+eqkySbiMo/duFMAzGd\ndRsI/9UDkKq2O7aQ6bRMHiFy8BNvcVIqLy+NWBXhJ7vIxeOmy2JC3v6wOTbfd6pp\nVhcrVkvN4HDzwE9V9cQJSxlEg2WKQYLNJ+0sFCwpVnw5OQEKVsr7Gu1xNBJqe3dt\nZM4SUN0k6gQiNM/yDWFXJ1p3mJ+/UscibADOIQFUKkE0puF5q41aTqN2SiGGjcB1\nrKzGdeKPxX+0B6uFx57p5/lIvfKRB+zpSLMhG1CZ5dqgzEpwheOvkG5qb4eRMWX5\nj4+7iug8MjtEI0pHcAXz\n=mK8L\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:17:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2","node_id":"C_kwDOUmckp9oAKDlmZDM4ZWUxYTQxOTRiYzVmMGQxMjNjNzkyZTQxN2ZiMmJjZjJjZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commit/cb3ed380a6976cf85f7f58e3b09c404831e3ca4f","sha":"cb3ed380a6976cf85f7f58e3b09c404831e3ca4f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/cb3ed380a6976cf85f7f58e3b09c404831e3ca4f"}],"sha":"9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/9fd38ee1a4194bc5f0d123c792e417fb2bcf2ce2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4073304?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claudioed","id":4073304,"login":"claudioed","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQwNzMzMDQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claudioed","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/commits/cb3ed380a6976cf85f7f58e3b09c404831e3ca4f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:54:08Z","email":"claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com","name":"Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:54:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: amend ADR 0001 with ADR 0002 -- counterpart is retail-network, not real SP-API (#19)\n\n* docs: amend ADR 0001 with ADR 0002 — counterpart is retail-network, not real SP-API\n\nRecords that the \"external retail fulfillment network\" network-fulfillment\nis Conformist to is retail-network, a new bounded context inside this same\nfleet''s orbit built to play that structural role -- not a real e-commerce\nretailer''s Selling Partner API. Companion to retail-network ADR 0001,\nstaged here (that repo does not exist yet, Phase 2) at\ndocs/planning/retail-network-adr-0001-DRAFT-for-new-repo.md pending its\ncreation.\n\n- docs/adr/0002-retail-network-not-amazon-counterpart.md (new, Proposed):\n  amends ADR 0001, renames the ACL adapter outbound/network/ ->\n  outbound/retailnetwork/ (Phase 3), tightens the PII rule to zero\n  ship-to data in this context at all (retail-network holds it instead),\n  drops the NETWORK_MODE sandbox value, keeps a real SP-API adapter as a\n  deferred (not dropped) future adapter swap behind the same\n  NetworkGateway port.\n- docs/planning/retail-network-adr-0001-DRAFT-for-new-repo.md (new): the\n  retail-network ADR 0001 draft, staged here temporarily with an explicit\n  header note to move it verbatim once that repo is scaffolded. Records\n  D1-D6 (one context; Direct-Fulfillment-like protocol fidelity in the\n  network''s own vocabulary; declared+measured capability; capacity share\n  proportional to physical stock; release on reconciled acceptance; no\n  auth).\n- AGENTS.md: updated rule 1 (adapter rename note) and rule 2 (no ship-to\n  PII reaches this context at all) to match ADR 0002''s decision, plus a\n  pointer to both new ADRs.\n\nPhase 1 (docs only) of 2026-09-25_231500-retail-network-in-ecosystem.md.\nPhase 0 (order-management boot-retry fix) already merged, PR #96.\n\nDo not merge -- Proposed status needs explicit user acceptance alongside\nthe companion retail-network ADR 0001.\n\n* docs: accept ADR-0002 and staged retail-network ADR-0001\n\nBoth accepted by owner review 2026-09-26. AGENTS.md''s informal status\nnote was left as-is (protected file, requires separate approval) but is\npurely descriptive and does not affect the accepted decision.","tree":{"sha":"9af1cba37bd438897c12fdd03771bd1774ab47b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/trees/9af1cba37bd438897c12fdd03771bd1774ab47b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/IQVO/network-fulfillment/git/commits/cb3ed380a6976cf85f7f58e3b09c404831e3ca4f","verification":{"payload":"tree 9af1cba37bd438897c12fdd03771bd1774ab47b0\nparent bb73f72456a68a04b1e38e5b0ccb2e4aa6611cb8\nauthor Claudio Eduardo de Oliveira <claudioed.oliveira@gmail.com> 1790456048 -0300\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790456048 -0300\n\ndocs: amend ADR 0001 with ADR 0002 -- counterpart is retail-network, not real SP-API (#19)\n\n* docs: amend ADR 0001 with ADR 0002 — counterpart is retail-network, not real SP-API\n\nRecords that the \"external retail fulfillment network\" network-fulfillment\nis Conformist to is retail-network, a new bounded context inside this same\nfleet''s orbit built to play that structural role -- not a real e-commerce\nretailer''s Selling Partner API. Companion to retail-network ADR 0001,\nstaged here (that repo does not exist yet, Phase 2) at\ndocs/planning/retail-network-adr-0001-DRAFT-for-new-repo.md pending its\ncreation.\n\n- docs/adr/0002-retail-network-not-amazon-counterpart.md (new, Proposed):\n  amends ADR 0001, renames the ACL adapter outbound/network/ ->\n  outbound/retailnetwork/ (Phase 3), tightens the PII rule to zero\n  ship-to data in this context at all (retail-network holds it instead),\n  drops the NETWORK_MODE sandbox value, keeps a real SP-API adapter as a\n  deferred (not dropped) future adapter swap behind the same\n  NetworkGateway port.\n- docs/planning/retail-network-adr-0001-DRAFT-for-new-repo.md (new): the\n  retail-network ADR 0001 draft, staged here temporarily with an explicit\n  header note to move it verbatim once that repo is scaffolded. Records\n  D1-D6 (one context; Direct-Fulfillment-like protocol fidelity in the\n  network''s own vocabulary; declared+measured capability; capacity share\n  proportional to physical stock; release on reconciled acceptance; no\n  auth).\n- AGENTS.md: updated rule 1 (adapter rename note) and rule 2 (no ship-to\n  PII reaches this context at all) to match ADR 0002''s decision, plus a\n  pointer to both new ADRs.\n\nPhase 1 (docs only) of 2026-09-25_231500-retail-network-in-ecosystem.md.\nPhase 0 (order-management boot-retry fix) already merged, PR #96.\n\nDo not merge -- Proposed status needs explicit user acceptance alongside\nthe companion retail-network ADR 0001.\n\n* docs: accept ADR-0002 and staged retail-network ADR-0001\n\nBoth accepted by owner review 2026-09-26. AGENTS.md''s informal status\nnote was left as-is (protected file, requires separate approval) but is\npurely descriptive and does not affect the accepted decision.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJquDDwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB7EQAA+wljxALDKnud5KY/sdx855\nrb0m7L0FzF1x5+au0r1T9mYvf/3y6nls7dcTjPg/eljtm4seHdONbVWPnwxJ8HDZ\nh2J8L0BLeNDWiItfg6A9QGZtvEjMxW8OGTeuBvcitYuob36KB0TROmhmdu9N0I4o\nIaX+7B1tmn5iA9/bV2FhJ5bN1vgqITPKUyes7zoC/UeVeDyejHT5WX6xhp5O1QjC\n8rdn78RyXcLcrBvU/n3n+bA79mk4S7svCsdBK7ZzVixiWwe8Gdz+YCagt80dT8Vs\neiv59IakO0KVwjYWwynKwZYhdxGIFQpAqpLxzI5rGUvxpF2zqm+L9XkTmYUg8yAl\nhR5u2CUYCfwtb1MI7EQNiZsRzcmIXG5ZRwuasVraBsUtXD1Tk/wHPO3eimb18L6G\nGI79J4oNrPrtP22gJijhwblNiTM1a51Ni8wXziQ1ikjV3bFkHSu9EigsVkoS75Nd\nuTZvWSPkigVDnBeqtKgy+KADk9BiZrPd3fKXr2v5gl9SzPZ0vK3xhzgkSWr6NHzn\nlqUnye2oeZ1/9GFBSskLDlXs5LcNzNgVNzw3f/KBh6e8B5w2IDe93MlvV6zIeesQ\nDhsEgY3y5431rp3uYQcjSYRL6xwUrsul6EiPMHvS15yAnlL9oi9l6CZUq+epCNlF\n2R4VGzjEOyFSnt8oTe/f\n=ZlFC\n-----EN