,"following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/971dfc2227f48d39af19bba6da54f5d5112bb1df","node_id":"C_kwDOUoGmVtoAKDk3MWRmYzIyMjdmNDhkMzlhZjE5YmJhNmRhNTRmNWQ1MTEyYmIxZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/1d2c64d3fc10b11afc57668a2533740c95dd4ca4","sha":"1d2c64d3fc10b11afc57668a2533740c95dd4ca4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/1d2c64d3fc10b11afc57668a2533740c95dd4ca4"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/770c42bc4014b9e7f95ef3745cc2645b9a19f2ef","sha":"770c42bc4014b9e7f95ef3745cc2645b9a19f2ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/770c42bc4014b9e7f95ef3745cc2645b9a19f2ef"}],"sha":"971dfc2227f48d39af19bba6da54f5d5112bb1df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/971dfc2227f48d39af19bba6da54f5d5112bb1df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10379680?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/f84a558f119bf5bbd13825532176fe145db21f5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:56:51Z","email":"bigbooooooom@gmail.com","name":"Oleh H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:56:51Z","email":"bigbooooooom@gmail.com","name":"Oleh H"},"message":"Check for unused and duplicated code before each commit, with lefthook\n\n`npm install` now installs git hooks (lefthook.yml; lefthook''s postinstall,\nskipped when CI is set). Before each commit, in parallel and only when a\nstaged file could change the answer:\n- unused code: `npm run lint:unused` (knip, as in CI);\n- duplicated code: `npm run lint:duplicates`, jscpd over src and scripts.\n\njscpd fails only on copies that aren''t in .jscpd-baseline.json: the 14 there\nwere when it came in (125 lines, 0.39%). The baseline holds fingerprints, not\npaths, and only shrinks: after removing a copy, --update-baseline drops it.\nCI runs the duplicates check too.\n\nThe two checks take about 3 s together; a commit of other files skips them.\nCLAUDE.md asks not to skip them with --no-verify, and gains a \"No copies\"\nrule; CONTRIBUTING.md and the PR template list the new check.","tree":{"sha":"f09dc728f431b9d473a66274dc2fbe7a9a28e9dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/git/trees/f09dc728f431b9d473a66274dc2fbe7a9a28e9dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/git/commits/f84a558f119bf5bbd13825532176fe145db21f5c","verification":{"payload":"tree f09dc728f431b9d473a66274dc2fbe7a9a28e9dc\nparent 9ac58f70ce5b5e85d27469b5fdfb221db9655529\nauthor Oleh H <bigbooooooom@gmail.com> 1790369811 +0000\ncommitter Oleh H <bigbooooooom@gmail.com> 1790369811 +0000\n\nCheck for unused and duplicated code before each commit, with lefthook\n\n`npm install` now installs git hooks (lefthook.yml; lefthook''s postinstall,\nskipped when CI is set). Before each commit, in parallel and only when a\nstaged file could change the answer:\n- unused code: `npm run lint:unused` (knip, as in CI);\n- duplicated code: `npm run lint:duplicates`, jscpd over src and scripts.\n\njscpd fails only on copies that aren''t in .jscpd-baseline.json: the 14 there\nwere when it came in (125 lines, 0.39%). The baseline holds fingerprints, not\npaths, and only shrinks: after removing a copy, --update-baseline drops it.\nCI runs the duplicates check too.\n\nThe two checks take about 3 s together; a commit of other files skips them.\nCLAUDE.md asks not to skip them with --no-verify, and gains a \"No copies\"\nrule; CONTRIBUTING.md and the PR template list the new check.\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBwW54mo\nWI4dbFRMlYDeq0GM0PK0R7a5FHpyWbLMWFaBfNsS9DyHT1A4JsO3HAy3A6IvmjWuooD5mxTGGbz3\nOgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10379680?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/f84a558f119bf5bbd13825532176fe145db21f5c","node_id":"C_kwDOUoGmVtoAKGY4NGE1NThmMTE5YmY1YmJkMTM4MjU1MzIxNzZmZTE0NWRiMjFmNWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/9ac58f70ce5b5e85d27469b5fdfb221db9655529","sha":"9ac58f70ce5b5e85d27469b5fdfb221db9655529","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/9ac58f70ce5b5e85d27469b5fdfb221db9655529"}],"sha":"f84a558f119bf5bbd13825532176fe145db21f5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/f84a558f119bf5bbd13825532176fe145db21f5c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10379680?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/5aa7a4113dd490b56dbdbda43161a03451de13e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:47:44Z","email":"bigbooooooom@gmail.com","name":"Oleh H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:47:44Z","email":"bigbooooooom@gmail.com","name":"Oleh H"},"message":"Read Angular, Vue 2 and web components; load source maps from files\n\nPicking an element now also finds the Angular component that rendered it\n(development builds through window.ng, production builds through Angular''s\nprivate view registry, labelled as such), a Vue 2 component, or a web\ncomponent such as Lit''s: props, state (signals, data and Lit state can be\nset), the chain and a Components tree for each. The Component page lists\nevery listener on the picked element with the function it runs, which is all\nthere is on a plain page. A bundle whose site doesn''t publish its source map\ncan be given one from a file, kept with the workspace until forgotten.\n\n- main: adapters for Vue 2, Angular and custom elements with shared DOM\n  helpers; the Angular registry found with Runtime.queryObjects only when a\n  production Angular page is read, and handed to the adapter; listeners from\n  DOMDebugger.getEventListeners (Vue 3 invokers unwrapped); a per-workspace\n  SourceMapFileStore, a file dialog and file maps served before the site''s;\n  the source-map channels in their own module; engine constants as a folder\n- renderer: listeners on the Component page and for plain elements, the\n  Angular internals label, Load a source map / Forget on the source card and\n  in the Explorer, places traced again when a bundle''s map changes\n- tests: Angular, Vue 2 and Lit carts bundled from dev dependencies, unit,\n  renderer, integration in real Chromium and e2e\n- docs: SPEC 6.8 and 6.11, CHANGELOG, README, research doc","tree":{"sha":"a5d5563376e7445c56dbc5f645ac6743f9f1bc5b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/git/trees/a5d5563376e7445c56dbc5f645ac6743f9f1bc5b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/git/commits/5aa7a4113dd490b56dbdbda43161a03451de13e1","verification":{"payload":"tree a5d5563376e7445c56dbc5f645ac6743f9f1bc5b\nparent a681a7a5d762a50f9e50bd66f673fd866851ba92\nauthor Oleh H <bigbooooooom@gmail.com> 1790369264 +0000\ncommitter Oleh H <bigbooooooom@gmail.com> 1790369264 +0000\n\nRead Angular, Vue 2 and web components; load source maps from files\n\nPicking an element now also finds the Angular component that rendered it\n(development builds through window.ng, production builds through Angular''s\nprivate view registry, labelled as such), a Vue 2 component, or a web\ncomponent such as Lit''s: props, state (signals, data and Lit state can be\nset), the chain and a Components tree for each. The Component page lists\nevery listener on the picked element with the function it runs, which is all\nthere is on a plain page. A bundle whose site doesn''t publish its source map\ncan be given one from a file, kept with the workspace until forgotten.\n\n- main: adapters for Vue 2, Angular and custom elements with shared DOM\n  helpers; the Angular registry found with Runtime.queryObjects only when a\n  production Angular page is read, and handed to the adapter; listeners from\n  DOMDebugger.getEventListeners (Vue 3 invokers unwrapped); a per-workspace\n  SourceMapFileStore, a file dialog and file maps served before the site''s;\n  the source-map channels in their own module; engine constants as a folder\n- renderer: listeners on the Component page and for plain elements, the\n  Angular internals label, Load a source map / Forget on the source card and\n  in the Explorer, places traced again when a bundle''s map changes\n- tests: Angular, Vue 2 and Lit carts bundled from dev dependencies, unit,\n  renderer, integration in real Chromium and e2e\n- docs: SPEC 6.8 and 6.11, CHANGELOG, README, research doc\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQDR0Vg94\nCgYZj+5949iUmOtk4smAmuBXu6uAYF91P4XA2AyHeT7ymb2G/39I9vcRbbtPaObnhB3Gno7OP5Pb\npQc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10379680?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/5aa7a4113dd490b56dbdbda43161a03451de13e1","node_id":"C_kwDOUoGmVtoAKDVhYTdhNDExM2RkNDkwYjU2ZGJkYmRhNDMxNjFhMDM0NTFkZTEzZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/a681a7a5d762a50f9e50bd66f673fd866851ba92","sha":"a681a7a5d762a50f9e50bd66f673fd866851ba92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/a681a7a5d762a50f9e50bd66f673fd866851ba92"}],"sha":"5aa7a4113dd490b56dbdbda43161a03451de13e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/5aa7a4113dd490b56dbdbda43161a03451de13e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10379680?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/bab043740206a9d47add0c4734f823913b9e1b97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:34:03Z","email":"bigbooooooom@gmail.com","name":"Oleh H"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T20:34:03Z","email":"bigbooooooom@gmail.com","name":"Oleh H"},"message":"Click \"Put back\" without racing the window it closes, in the page-window tests\n\nThe website window''s \"Put back in the editor window\" closes the window it is\nin, as soon as the main process hears of it. Playwright''s click waits on its\npage after the press, so it failed with \"Target page, context or browser has\nbeen closed\" whenever the window went first: 3 of 10 runs of this file on\nmain, in three tests (goes back from its toolbar''s button, keeps the site''s\npop-ups open, copes with being put back while its window still loads). An\nevaluate that clicks has the same race, as the click''s message to main can\novertake the evaluate''s answer.\n\nclickClosing schedules the click once its evaluate has answered, and the test\nwaits for the window to go as before. Waits for a window to open or close now\ntake WINDOW_TIMEOUT (10 s) rather than expect.poll''s default second, which a\nbusy machine can exceed.\n\nThe file passes 20 runs in a row, and 3 of 3 with every core busy. The\nActions-window tests never click a control that closes its own window.","tree":{"sha":"9fe083275eac0323cefe9cc386b24a5c4765caa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/git/trees/9fe083275eac0323cefe9cc386b24a5c4765caa0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/git/commits/bab043740206a9d47add0c4734f823913b9e1b97","verification":{"payload":"tree 9fe083275eac0323cefe9cc386b24a5c4765caa0\nparent d1eea364ffa0bca60f53fe43266b1a586aecec8b\nauthor Oleh H <bigbooooooom@gmail.com> 1790368443 +0000\ncommitter Oleh H <bigbooooooom@gmail.com> 1790368443 +0000\n\nClick \"Put back\" without racing the window it closes, in the page-window tests\n\nThe website window''s \"Put back in the editor window\" closes the window it is\nin, as soon as the main process hears of it. Playwright''s click waits on its\npage after the press, so it failed with \"Target page, context or browser has\nbeen closed\" whenever the window went first: 3 of 10 runs of this file on\nmain, in three tests (goes back from its toolbar''s button, keeps the site''s\npop-ups open, copes with being put back while its window still loads). An\nevaluate that clicks has the same race, as the click''s message to main can\novertake the evaluate''s answer.\n\nclickClosing schedules the click once its evaluate has answered, and the test\nwaits for the window to go as before. Waits for a window to open or close now\ntake WINDOW_TIMEOUT (10 s) rather than expect.poll''s default second, which a\nbusy machine can exceed.\n\nThe file passes 20 runs in a row, and 3 of 3 with every core busy. The\nActions-window tests never click a control that closes its own window.\n","reason":"unknown_key","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAyRfvKA\nH/ohRvZIqOV41t0UBtizSRMldF4uvL1mg7dKfVBTIQEBgDFbjlh41e+VkGjYwMwgaVFSXQt6x27q\n2A0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10379680?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev","id":10379680,"login":"olehwebdev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzc5Njgw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/olehwebdev","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/bab043740206a9d47add0c4734f823913b9e1b97","node_id":"C_kwDOUoGmVtoAKGJhYjA0Mzc0MDIwNmE5ZDQ3YWRkMGM0NzM0ZjgyMzkxM2I5ZTFiOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/olehwebdev/console-editor/commit/d1eea364ffa0bca60f53fe43266b1a586aecec8b","sha":"d1eea364ffa0bca60f53fe43266b1a586aecec8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/olehwebdev/console-editor/commits/d1eea364ffa0bca60f53fe43266b1a586aecec8b"}],"sha":"bab043740206a9d47add0c