login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:48:11.042Z","repositoryId":1384251324,"sha":"c0176075e37c66fea662df19cfefc883b7b85be3"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:48:11.042Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/984a7c784df5d2fcb0cdbf553828150e0eb79e89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T18:54:22Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T18:54:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"2.3 Build-time prerendering for the host (THE-500) (#18)\n\n* Prerender host routes at build time with Playwright (THE-500)\n\nWhy: issue 2.3. The host is a client-rendered SPA, so crawlers and\nno-JavaScript visitors would see an empty page. The site is hosted as\nstatic files on S3 + CloudFront (no server), so the HTML for each route is\ngenerated at build time and saved next to the build output.\n\nWhat changed (apps/portfolio-web):\n- prerender.mjs and a `prerender` Nx target (depends on `build`): serves the\n  production build, opens each route in headless Chromium, and saves the\n  rendered HTML to dist/index.html and dist/portfolio/firefly/index.html.\n  Routes are listed in the script with the h1 and title each must contain.\n  Outputs are written only after every route is captured, because the\n  preview server falls back to dist/index.html and it must stay the pristine\n  shell until the last route is rendered.\n- The script checks its own output and fails the build if a route has the\n  wrong h1, not exactly one <title>, or console errors. A second pass serves\n  the saved files the way production hosting will (/x -> /x/index.html),\n  loads each page, and checks the client render equals the prerendered HTML,\n  with one <title> and one description and no console errors.\n- src/Seo.tsx: per-route <title> and <meta name=\"description\"> using React\n  19''s built-in hoisting into <head>. The static <title> was removed from\n  index.html, since React does not replace it and it duplicated the tag.\n- Home and Firefly routes set their own title and description. Firefly also\n  renders a host-owned h1 and summary; the federated remote is wrapped in a\n  new ClientOnly component, so the remote''s content renders in the browser\n  only. The script sets window.__PRERENDER__ so it never mounts during\n  capture.\n- src/bootstrap.tsx: awaits router.load(), and when #root already has\n  prerendered content, renders over it with createRoot (see below) after\n  removing the prerendered <title>/description, which React re-creates.\n  App sets window.__APP_READY__ so the script knows the client render\n  committed. The brand link now matches exactly, so it isn''t marked active on\n  every page.\n\nFinding, and a deviation from the issue: it asked for hydrateRoot. The\nprerendered HTML is captured from a client render, so it has none of the\nSuspense markers React needs to hydrate it, and TanStack Router always\nrenders a Suspense boundary (its root Outlet). hydrateRoot logged React\nerror #418 (hydration mismatch) on every route. Rendering over the\nprerendered markup with createRoot avoids that, and the second-pass check\nproves the client output is identical to the saved HTML, which is what the\nrequirement was for.\n\nVerification:\n- `nx prerender @theory/portfolio-web` passes (both routes, all checks), and\n  `nx run-many -t lint test build` and `nx format:check --all` pass.\n- With JavaScript disabled, both routes show their own title, h1 and\n  description from the saved files.\n- Lighthouse SEO: 91 on / and on /portfolio/firefly. The only failed audit is\n  robots.txt, which is issue 4.5.\n- Playwright dev e2e: the 5 existing tests still pass.\n- Not covered here: hosting must map /portfolio/firefly to\n  /portfolio/firefly/index.html (CloudFront, issue 2.4), and prerendering\n  other pages happens by adding them to the script''s route list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Run prerender in CI and document it (THE-500)\n\nWhy: the prerender script fails when a route''s saved HTML is wrong, so CI\nshould run it; otherwise a change that breaks prerendering only shows up at\ndeploy time.\n\nWhat changed:\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: after the lint/test/build step, install\n  Playwright''s Chromium (`npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`) and\n  run `nx affected -t prerender` against the same base and head.\n- README: the `nx prerender portfolio-web` command in Getting started, and\n  the SEO line in the stack list.\n\nVerification: `nx format:check --all` passes. The workflow change gets its\nfirst GitHub run on the PR for this branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Rename the root convenience scripts (owner''s edit)\n\nWhy: hand edit by the repo owner, grouped into this branch as requested (see\nthe \"Branches and pull requests\" notes: manual changes go on the current\nbranch). Not part of the prerender work.\n\nWhat changed (package.json): the three scripts portfolio-web-serve,\nportfolio-web-prod-build and portfolio-web-prod-serve are renamed to\nportfolio-serve, portfolio-prod-build and portfolio-prod-serve, and\nfirefly-portfolio-serve (`nx dev portfolio-firefly`) is added.\n\nVerification: package.json is valid JSON and `nx format:check --all` passes.\nThe scripts only wrap existing nx targets and were not run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"693d6dd555d7de566413a292fb3f72506b94f7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/693d6dd555d7de566413a292fb3f72506b94f7ae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/984a7c784df5d2fcb0cdbf553828150e0eb79e89","verification":{"payload":"tree 693d6dd555d7de566413a292fb3f72506b94f7ae\nparent 8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790362462 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790362462 -0400\n\n2.3 Build-time prerendering for the host (THE-500) (#18)\n\n* Prerender host routes at build time with Playwright (THE-500)\n\nWhy: issue 2.3. The host is a client-rendered SPA, so crawlers and\nno-JavaScript visitors would see an empty page. The site is hosted as\nstatic files on S3 + CloudFront (no server), so the HTML for each route is\ngenerated at build time and saved next to the build output.\n\nWhat changed (apps/portfolio-web):\n- prerender.mjs and a `prerender` Nx target (depends on `build`): serves the\n  production build, opens each route in headless Chromium, and saves the\n  rendered HTML to dist/index.html and dist/portfolio/firefly/index.html.\n  Routes are listed in the script with the h1 and title each must contain.\n  Outputs are written only after every route is captured, because the\n  preview server falls back to dist/index.html and it must stay the pristine\n  shell until the last route is rendered.\n- The script checks its own output and fails the build if a route has the\n  wrong h1, not exactly one <title>, or console errors. A second pass serves\n  the saved files the way production hosting will (/x -> /x/index.html),\n  loads each page, and checks the client render equals the prerendered HTML,\n  with one <title> and one description and no console errors.\n- src/Seo.tsx: per-route <title> and <meta name=\"description\"> using React\n  19''s built-in hoisting into <head>. The static <title> was removed from\n  index.html, since React does not replace it and it duplicated the tag.\n- Home and Firefly routes set their own title and description. Firefly also\n  renders a host-owned h1 and summary; the federated remote is wrapped in a\n  new ClientOnly component, so the remote''s content renders in the browser\n  only. The script sets window.__PRERENDER__ so it never mounts during\n  capture.\n- src/bootstrap.tsx: awaits router.load(), and when #root already has\n  prerendered content, renders over it with createRoot (see below) after\n  removing the prerendered <title>/description, which React re-creates.\n  App sets window.__APP_READY__ so the script knows the client render\n  committed. The brand link now matches exactly, so it isn''t marked active on\n  every page.\n\nFinding, and a deviation from the issue: it asked for hydrateRoot. The\nprerendered HTML is captured from a client render, so it has none of the\nSuspense markers React needs to hydrate it, and TanStack Router always\nrenders a Suspense boundary (its root Outlet). hydrateRoot logged React\nerror #418 (hydration mismatch) on every route. Rendering over the\nprerendered markup with createRoot avoids that, and the second-pass check\nproves the client output is identical to the saved HTML, which is what the\nrequirement was for.\n\nVerification:\n- `nx prerender @theory/portfolio-web` passes (both routes, all checks), and\n  `nx run-many -t lint test build` and `nx format:check --all` pass.\n- With JavaScript disabled, both routes show their own title, h1 and\n  description from the saved files.\n- Lighthouse SEO: 91 on / and on /portfolio/firefly. The only failed audit is\n  robots.txt, which is issue 4.5.\n- Playwright dev e2e: the 5 existing tests still pass.\n- Not covered here: hosting must map /portfolio/firefly to\n  /portfolio/firefly/index.html (CloudFront, issue 2.4), and prerendering\n  other pages happens by adding them to the script''s route list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Run prerender in CI and document it (THE-500)\n\nWhy: the prerender script fails when a route''s saved HTML is wrong, so CI\nshould run it; otherwise a change that breaks prerendering only shows up at\ndeploy time.\n\nWhat changed:\n- .github/workflows/ci.yml: after the lint/test/build step, install\n  Playwright''s Chromium (`npx playwright install --with-deps chromium`) and\n  run `nx affected -t prerender` against the same base and head.\n- README: the `nx prerender portfolio-web` command in Getting started, and\n  the SEO line in the stack list.\n\nVerification: `nx format:check --all` passes. The workflow change gets its\nfirst GitHub run on the PR for this branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Rename the root convenience scripts (owner''s edit)\n\nWhy: hand edit by the repo owner, grouped into this branch as requested (see\nthe \"Branches and pull requests\" notes: manual changes go on the current\nbranch). Not part of the prerender work.\n\nWhat changed (package.json): the three scripts portfolio-web-serve,\nportfolio-web-prod-build and portfolio-web-prod-serve are renamed to\nportfolio-serve, portfolio-prod-build and portfolio-prod-serve, and\nfirefly-portfolio-serve (`nx dev portfolio-firefly`) is added.\n\nVerification: package.json is valid JSON and `nx format:check --all` passes.\nThe scripts only wrap existing nx targets and were not run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtsNeCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5V8QALFtZtS7tragSmSxrIALQl0s\na5OERTcuID+bRNcmgcQ3p8NtRUrZZ/7tDh31nR3UTwxP36z4ERknfARM0DQ32cpi\n70JRssb5kcELG5XHwx3oF0K1RjV59ongUEAImFDPrz811QFfceIKycOuvS6D7IDy\n6PLiXg7hJbP0JZLShVKdasxsL8lcYLDaRVhwnx5ArP+oBPvJw4nGg74qptds8vfa\n3L4Z8q0YfCb/72ia9WIT03NvuOmbcay71jyuiCrhAS86jG+edziZJExDdpYAjW+x\nw6IXduFzokpxrik8pV7CS3hCOs1kFi8aPFpnFmJIwzXwq5pKv90LRP+rwsWT+AQW\nWkbIo9WnmhUXSe52gK7zb6lEzfQzUHkgiLKNoz7874ZTzpZj8UGPnUm09ck7r0zp\n+sKjRzq5/8o/hNS2nTEmF91vDPpG56YRIA3dRlgfiwFgT/QtmTe6qS0xk8Er10qh\nVKi0JHE9HhRPgxsMcCewKr6mk/oFP4WqyaxIeDYoUpMErlzZIJ/+k0edHmpxdWtQ\nLvXj6PlBGbQtoOs8QkVv/6JwZ8zKRHHNN04vF61sidSJe9LvsUrR+Y1EP1hIFYJ0\ntNRnSsoUwC11H9/A9F593k8k9PuURw93+u6p8zkMWSeYcIkt6ECz3X+gxRr0emCY\nS9HBN/l3ofY1t3aZ0X0D\n=otiI\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T18:54:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/984a7c784df5d2fcb0cdbf553828150e0eb79e89","node_id":"C_kwDOUoH_vNoAKDk4NGE3Yzc4NGRmNWQyZmNiMGNkYmY1NTM4MjgxNTBlMGViNzllODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c","sha":"8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c"}],"sha":"984a7c784df5d2fcb0cdbf553828150e0eb79e89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/984a7c784df5d2fcb0cdbf553828150e0eb79e89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:51:31Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:51:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Document preferring Nx generators over hand-written config (#17)\n\nWhy: the owner has twice steered toward \"use the Nx generators and\ntemplates\" (the Nx module federation template for the host, then\n@nx/react:provider for the Firefly remote, after a hand-configured Angular\nremote failed). That is a reusable pattern, flagged under the \"Capturing\ntechnology decision patterns\" rule and approved for recording.\n\nWhat changed (CLAUDE.md only): a new \"Prefer generators\" section before the\ndecision-patterns section. Prefer Nx generators and templates (for example\n@nx/react:provider, or the ones @aws/nx-plugin offers) over hand-written\nconfig. Hand-write or adapt config only when no generator does the job, and\nnote afterwards what was changed from the generated output (such as a\nrenamed target or a scoped project name) so it''s clear what to redo if the\ngenerator is rerun.\n\nVerification: docs-only change; `prettier --check CLAUDE.md` passes. The same\nsection was added to the other repo.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"71d2addc980bbe1c272a7f0e7b47ecc5c4f75884","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/71d2addc980bbe1c272a7f0e7b47ecc5c4f75884"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c","verification":{"payload":"tree 71d2addc980bbe1c272a7f0e7b47ecc5c4f75884\nparent bbeb113c318c1e54b8f53ea06eff9c4a66d0be89\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790358691 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790358691 -0400\n\nDocument preferring Nx generators over hand-written config (#17)\n\nWhy: the owner has twice steered toward \"use the Nx generators and\ntemplates\" (the Nx module federation template for the host, then\n@nx/react:provider for the Firefly remote, after a hand-configured Angular\nremote failed). That is a reusable pattern, flagged under the \"Capturing\ntechnology decision patterns\" rule and approved for recording.\n\nWhat changed (CLAUDE.md only): a new \"Prefer generators\" section before the\ndecision-patterns section. Prefer Nx generators and templates (for example\n@nx/react:provider, or the ones @aws/nx-plugin offers) over hand-written\nconfig. Hand-write or adapt config only when no generator does the job, and\nnote afterwards what was changed from the generated output (such as a\nrenamed target or a scoped project name) so it''s clear what to redo if the\ngenerator is rerun.\n\nVerification: docs-only change; `prettier --check CLAUDE.md` passes. The same\nsection was added to the other repo.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtrSjCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAChgQAF2Y8AJfrt3mYVoUPC+RjXxH\nHC5uSU93rfDyKZiRg+hxrWNZ+CGmQ7aPfBRzhS1YwqCpdOqW3yOcBDQdLoEqYJs5\nBy9B6OuChpEVKWLaxYftnI9WFOhtffAwaO/UD2wmV769YDO7oFfcrkZJdXOLsLox\nm32IGo+CfaQmfkxuMoB7nQnRZbUyKRmcTC5MtTnNAgLKbkkalpdK3BkT/gqokBG6\nXYoYfFgJqww+Dml8eOBGuF2cwT2wZa86Fu4QuzJJwLQr1ZW2TyEToHQ5NsO/X3j3\npSUKwVdTIb4Q3X/mWOp9y5d6OU9XuKrxvDlmQfZTpXoslbtz5aJ5IKbnsO6rXhBa\nvmLcN83sOpD12RudzzMCFoa7TJ3A3ZAY46K8TEKTJE/kxaTUxi4+J4EN8wADbaRF\naRXnLjW3hCsJU/0vG73QBHOLuqJz8jTGv9TqdYZz2OP7XpF9JgFeLnzRjdCH+cDK\nrGQsJfpJ5d9nxnTt+Zg0qS+Ej3kaKjLInLi1GLGxFH7/KIlvQk9HUN1sRkuz2nGJ\nng2Q0knesq9iTG5TOETOUkXd+Hj6bkTRPyPM/kmbx7Tljj/iGFlb4pXok1Mjxtp9\n97eXO7DbhUDoj+cvYi/XxF1EJVCBaSOtCHV8nn789JRoACqDUtzkANdylcV1468D\nw5OvektG8Krg0bHbLPcP\n=6sY1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T17:51:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c","node_id":"C_kwDOUoH_vNoAKDgxODdmMmFjYjk5Y2FkMjc5ODViZmJkZGE2NzQ0NzcwZWQ3ODJkNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/bbeb113c318c1e54b8f53ea06eff9c4a66d0be89","sha":"bbeb113c318c1e54b8f53ea06eff9c4a66d0be89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/bbeb113c318c1e54b8f53ea06eff9c4a66d0be89"}],"sha":"8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/8187f2acb99cad27985bfbdda6744770ed782d4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/bbeb113c318c1e54b8f53ea06eff9c4a66d0be89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:32:26Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T17:32:26Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"2.2 Firefly React remote loaded into the host (THE-499) (#16)\n\n* Generate the Firefly React remote with @nx/react:provider (THE-499)\n\nWhy: issue 2.2 was changed from an Angular remote to a React remote. The\nAngular route ran into a compatibility wall: @nx/angular-rspack 23.2.1\ndidn''t work with the Angular 22.2 that npm resolved (a DataCloneError,\nthen \"Hash utility must be initialized\"), Rspack 2 crashed Node 24 on\nload, and it also needed a Vite host to load an Rspack-built remote. The\nFirefly page is now ported to React on the same Vite + Module Federation\nstack as the host, using Nx''s generator. The Angular attempt was discarded\nand this branch started clean.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Ran `nx g @nx/react:provider --directory=apps/portfolio-firefly\n  --bundler=vite --consumer=portfolio-web --exposeName=FireflyPage\n  --port=4201`. It creates a Vite + @module-federation/vite provider that\n  exposes ./FireflyPage (a hello-world component with a data-testid), plus\n  a standalone bootstrap so it also runs on its own at :4201.\n- The generated project.json was adjusted to this workspace: the project\n  and package are named @theory/portfolio-firefly (like the host), the\n  serve target is renamed `dev`, and it depends on\n  @theory/portfolio-web:dev so `nx dev portfolio-firefly` also starts the\n  host. The generator''s dependsOn used the unscoped name\n  (portfolio-web:serve), which Nx silently ignored here, so the host never\n  started; using the scoped project name fixed it.\n- .gitignore: `@mf-types`, the type stubs the federation plugin writes.\n- package-lock.json for the new workspace package.\n\nVerification: `nx dev portfolio-firefly` brings up the host on :4200 and\nthe remote on :4201 (both return 200). `nx run-many -t lint test build`\npasses for all four projects. Loading the remote in the host is the next\ncommit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Load the Firefly remote in the host at /portfolio/firefly (THE-499)\n\nWhy: the second half of issue 2.2: the host loads the remote through the\nModule Federation runtime, with a fallback when it fails to load, and it\nworks in both dev and production builds.\n\nWhat changed:\n- src/mf.ts: registers the remote (alias portfolio-firefly, federation\n  name portfolio_firefly). The entry is http://127.0.0.1:4201/remoteEntry.js\n  in dev and /remotes/firefly/remoteEntry.js in a production build (where\n  the infrastructure issue 2.4 will serve it), overridable with\n  VITE_FIREFLY_ENTRY, which is how a production build was pointed at a\n  locally served remote for testing. `type: ''module''` stays: the remote is\n  Vite-built ESM. Comments updated (no longer \"revisit for Angular\").\n- src/pages.tsx and router.tsx: a /portfolio/firefly route rendering the\n  lazily loaded FireflyPage inside the existing ProviderBoundary, which shows\n  an alert fallback if the remote can''t be fetched while the rest of the\n  site keeps working.\n- Layout.tsx: a temporary \"Firefly\" nav link (real nav is issue 3.5/4.1).\n- e2e/firefly.spec.ts: three Playwright tests: the remote renders at\n  /portfolio/firefly; navigating Home <-> Firefly three times never leaves\n  more than one instance and none on Home; and with the remote''s\n  remoteEntry/manifest requests aborted, the page shows the fallback alert\n  and the site chrome still renders.\n- playwright.config.mts: the web server is now `nx dev portfolio-firefly`\n  (which also starts the host), waiting on the remote''s remoteEntry.js.\n- README: Firefly is described as a React remote ported from the old\n  Angular app.\n\nVerification:\n- `nx run-many -t lint test build --skip-nx-cache` passes for the four\n  projects and `nx format:check --all` passes.\n- Playwright (Chromium): 5 tests pass against the dev servers.\n- Production: built the host with VITE_FIREFLY_ENTRY pointing at :4201 and\n  the remote, served both with `vite preview`, and the same 5 tests pass;\n  a screenshot of /portfolio/firefly from the production build shows the\n  remote''s content inside the host chrome with no console errors.\n- The fallback test logs a Federation Runtime RUNTIME-008 error, which is\n  the expected failure being exercised.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6dd5594c6a3b18b4638e9e5904700cc49e3f24e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/6dd5594c6a3b18b4638e9e5904700cc49e3f24e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/bbeb113c318c1e54b8f53ea06eff9c4a66d0be89","verification":{"payload":"tree 6dd5594c6a3b18b4638e9e5904700cc49e3f24e7\nparent 533c9bb705e21f781006f4f1a974544441001dad\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790357546 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790357546 -0400\n\n2.2 Firefly React remote loaded into the host (THE-499) (#16)\n\n* Generate the Firefly React remote with @nx/react:provider (THE-499)\n\nWhy: issue 2.2 was changed from an Angular remote to a React remote. The\nAngular route ran into a compatibility wall: @nx/angular-rspack 23.2.1\ndidn''t work with the Angular 22.2 that npm resolved (a DataCloneError,\nthen \"Hash utility must be initialized\"), Rspack 2 crashed Node 24 on\nload, and it also needed a Vite host to load an Rspack-built remote. The\nFirefly page is now ported to React on the same Vite + Module Federation\nstack as the host, using Nx''s generator. The Angular attempt was discarded\nand this branch started clean.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Ran `nx g @nx/react:provider --directory=apps/portfolio-firefly\n  --bundler=vite --consumer=portfolio-web --exposeName=FireflyPage\n  --port=4201`. It creates a Vite + @module-federation/vite provider that\n  exposes ./FireflyPage (a hello-world component with a data-testid), plus\n  a standalone bootstrap so it also runs on its own at :4201.\n- The generated project.json was adjusted to this workspace: the project\n  and package are named @theory/portfolio-firefly (like the host), the\n  serve target is renamed `dev`, and it depends on\n  @theory/portfolio-web:dev so `nx dev portfolio-firefly` also starts the\n  host. The generator''s dependsOn used the unscoped name\n  (portfolio-web:serve), which Nx silently ignored here, so the host never\n  started; using the scoped project name fixed it.\n- .gitignore: `@mf-types`, the type stubs the federation plugin writes.\n- package-lock.json for the new workspace package.\n\nVerification: `nx dev portfolio-firefly` brings up the host on :4200 and\nthe remote on :4201 (both return 200). `nx run-many -t lint test build`\npasses for all four projects. Loading the remote in the host is the next\ncommit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Load the Firefly remote in the host at /portfolio/firefly (THE-499)\n\nWhy: the second half of issue 2.2: the host loads the remote through the\nModule Federation runtime, with a fallback when it fails to load, and it\nworks in both dev and production builds.\n\nWhat changed:\n- src/mf.ts: registers the remote (alias portfolio-firefly, federation\n  name portfolio_firefly). The entry is http://127.0.0.1:4201/remoteEntry.js\n  in dev and /remotes/firefly/remoteEntry.js in a production build (where\n  the infrastructure issue 2.4 will serve it), overridable with\n  VITE_FIREFLY_ENTRY, which is how a production build was pointed at a\n  locally served remote for testing. `type: ''module''` stays: the remote is\n  Vite-built ESM. Comments updated (no longer \"revisit for Angular\").\n- src/pages.tsx and router.tsx: a /portfolio/firefly route rendering the\n  lazily loaded FireflyPage inside the existing ProviderBoundary, which shows\n  an alert fallback if the remote can''t be fetched while the rest of the\n  site keeps working.\n- Layout.tsx: a temporary \"Firefly\" nav link (real nav is issue 3.5/4.1).\n- e2e/firefly.spec.ts: three Playwright tests: the remote renders at\n  /portfolio/firefly; navigating Home <-> Firefly three times never leaves\n  more than one instance and none on Home; and with the remote''s\n  remoteEntry/manifest requests aborted, the page shows the fallback alert\n  and the site chrome still renders.\n- playwright.config.mts: the web server is now `nx dev portfolio-firefly`\n  (which also starts the host), waiting on the remote''s remoteEntry.js.\n- README: Firefly is described as a React remote ported from the old\n  Angular app.\n\nVerification:\n- `nx run-many -t lint test build --skip-nx-cache` passes for the four\n  projects and `nx format:check --all` passes.\n- Playwright (Chromium): 5 tests pass against the dev servers.\n- Production: built the host with VITE_FIREFLY_ENTRY pointing at :4201 and\n  the remote, served both with `vite preview`, and the same 5 tests pass;\n  a screenshot of /portfolio/firefly from the production build shows the\n  remote''s content inside the host chrome with no console errors.\n- The fallback test logs a Federation Runtime RUNTIME-008 error, which is\n  the expected failure being exercised.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtrAqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKPkQAFxDTRkCfsJA8qfce6FiAApi\nZPG62VT7RJ1tV4H95/6HbL7w7UdTdHC0A3aodOJW1rlLc4c4lJytzC1+qJumIaOS\n3VJn0UD+vWlQYHX4cJWI5kIuXFoFmKN/nmJc3/CjDkf8P5ZnitPQPle7tr2IdEKx\nm5nHbD80dWeItEw4RtMwNtzqPt3+L4N