b00e3a0e7c98c1d5b82373b197ee5f40"}],"sha":"a73fc0ffee7354e37a88405c3746980cc261aa05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/a73fc0ffee7354e37a88405c3746980cc261aa05"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/8e52b267b00e3a0e7c98c1d5b82373b197ee5f40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:29:54Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:29:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Widen the local branch pruning rule to branches with no remote (#12)\n\nWhy: the first version of the rule only found local branches whose remote\nwas gone (`: gone]` in `git branch -vv`). In practice some merged branches\nnever had a remote tracked (for example branches created with\n`git branch -f`, or ones I pushed without -u), so they never show as gone\nand would pile up. Two such branches were cleaned up by hand.\n\nWhat changed (CLAUDE.md only): the \"Prune merged local branches\" bullet\nnow keys on the PR instead of the remote. A local branch is deletable when\n`gh pr list --state merged --head <branch> --json number,headRefOid`\nreturns a merged PR and the local tip equals that headRefOid (so nothing\nlocal is unpushed). That covers gone-remote branches and never-tracked\nbranches alike. Branches with an open or unmerged PR, no PR, or a tip that\ndiffers from the PR''s head are left and reported; current branch and main\nare never deleted. `git branch -D` is still required for squash and\nrebase merges.\n\nVerification: docs-only change. Checked the rule against the cleanup done\nearlier in theory-portfolio: each branch deleted that day had a merged PR\nwhose head matched its local tip. Applied the rule at branch creation here:\nboth repos had only main locally, so there was nothing left to prune.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d974fde746fc1f0edb361ed9c00222f3fc961e7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/d974fde746fc1f0edb361ed9c00222f3fc961e7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/8e52b267b00e3a0e7c98c1d5b82373b197ee5f40","verification":{"payload":"tree d974fde746fc1f0edb361ed9c00222f3fc961e7b\nparent c410a274fdfe177d7c84b11e93c9326df41e1cf1\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790314194 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790314194 -0400\n\nWiden the local branch pruning rule to branches with no remote (#12)\n\nWhy: the first version of the rule only found local branches whose remote\nwas gone (`: gone]` in `git branch -vv`). In practice some merged branches\nnever had a remote tracked (for example branches created with\n`git branch -f`, or ones I pushed without -u), so they never show as gone\nand would pile up. Two such branches were cleaned up by hand.\n\nWhat changed (CLAUDE.md only): the \"Prune merged local branches\" bullet\nnow keys on the PR instead of the remote. A local branch is deletable when\n`gh pr list --state merged --head <branch> --json number,headRefOid`\nreturns a merged PR and the local tip equals that headRefOid (so nothing\nlocal is unpushed). That covers gone-remote branches and never-tracked\nbranches alike. Branches with an open or unmerged PR, no PR, or a tip that\ndiffers from the PR''s head are left and reported; current branch and main\nare never deleted. `git branch -D` is still required for squash and\nrebase merges.\n\nVerification: docs-only change. Checked the rule against the cleanup done\nearlier in theory-portfolio: each branch deleted that day had a merged PR\nwhose head matched its local tip. Applied the rule at branch creation here:\nboth repos had only main locally, so there was nothing left to prune.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtgbSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAALYQQAFGJF3JL4fNYxeLtXdVNJMf0\nYRjMlO8cwhE8dsupeL+pD2W+Nz5tahVjGYXHNDAEXwguAU4z1tgMRyvoI+Pkmod0\nDofBLaZRPKsP3MjGyL/h2bdMLVN3KOcOQFaiXpyaTx36jzfUAf3MwIHmg0SeivrC\nY5UJBh3bDHMUxCQLEmwfL1TJZr+zpfgW55JMjfKx7aw/EMqmAogxvWcT7nrPlfo9\n4BZIhHvJLJhS9Kni7IBe6qGH4QX37j6lryrBWWjg7PWjV+aVOd5L+4l/OeUu+rM1\nfINCccPVU0jLHjhdHndoHGLnHPQhTfZzStMQsMn0/xc/ONtikCeG+9h4rNN+YhHJ\nKx4cV7xtdIbB1Gr1I8v4DtMhrciJ3uxn4dlfuLEzitJdv/7LAlr/LT08Ji6NovSG\nZMR74u9lVWVqF2aBNU9m4v80vnS7pAr9a+IG833bMkfGOtzqbY6YAPa/0QC2acSM\nRdFFy9/LxdtME7hvLZvN4SwJybhRKRc5aGDrJ9gY9mkVcgVQdUk/l1D11ZDedW4A\nU87acs87zxIrUuby1fjlsUClCXLySQwYNmgedSeGeEIkhpThS6MC3FgQo/qkvJlc\nIQ+04cdCMw1w9o2k0u7WUSvI+hpNgieAs721Y1tbdFWCHV+2UOWqojFHZb12WKJi\n+T+mqT5Juo5gz0djuz7K\n=lQDE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T05:29:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/8e52b267b00e3a0e7c98c1d5b82373b197ee5f40","node_id":"C_kwDOUoH_vNoAKDhlNTJiMjY3YjAwZTNhMGU3Yzk4YzFkNWI4MjM3M2IxOTdlZTVmNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/c410a274fdfe177d7c84b11e93c9326df41e1cf1","sha":"c410a274fdfe177d7c84b11e93c9326df41e1cf1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/c410a274fdfe177d7c84b11e93c9326df41e1cf1"}],"sha":"8e52b267b00e3a0e7c98c1d5b82373b197ee5f40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/8e52b267b00e3a0e7c98c1d5b82373b197ee5f40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/c410a274fdfe177d7c84b11e93c9326df41e1cf1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:22:22Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:22:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Document pruning merged local branches when creating a branch (#11)\n\nWhy: with squash and rebase merges, merged feature branches pile up\nlocally (GitHub deletes the remote branch, but the local one stays), and\n`git branch --merged` doesn''t recognise them because their commits were\nrewritten. Stale local branches make it easy to branch from or reuse the\nwrong thing.\n\nWhat changed (CLAUDE.md only): a new bullet in \"Branches and pull\nrequests\". When creating a new branch, first run `git fetch --prune`, then\nfind local branches whose remote is gone (`git branch -vv` shows\n`: gone]`), confirm each PR was merged (`gh pr list --state merged --head\n<branch>`), and delete them with `git branch -D` (needed because squash\nand rebase merges aren''t seen as merged). Branches with an open or\nunmerged PR, no PR, or unpushed commits are left alone and reported to the\nuser; the current branch and main are never deleted.\n\nVerification: docs-only change. The same rule was applied by hand to the\nlocal branches in this repo before committing, checking each PR''s merge\nstate first.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"590b5a08070b34c17af91758aae59c7c08a792a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/590b5a08070b34c17af91758aae59c7c08a792a7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/c410a274fdfe177d7c84b11e93c9326df41e1cf1","verification":{"payload":"tree 590b5a08070b34c17af91758aae59c7c08a792a7\nparent fda29baccf5162226cc40bf8cec94870ea6d3d22\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790313742 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790313742 -0400\n\nDocument pruning merged local branches when creating a branch (#11)\n\nWhy: with squash and rebase merges, merged feature branches pile up\nlocally (GitHub deletes the remote branch, but the local one stays), and\n`git branch --merged` doesn''t recognise them because their commits were\nrewritten. Stale local branches make it easy to branch from or reuse the\nwrong thing.\n\nWhat changed (CLAUDE.md only): a new bullet in \"Branches and pull\nrequests\". When creating a new branch, first run `git fetch --prune`, then\nfind local branches whose remote is gone (`git branch -vv` shows\n`: gone]`), confirm each PR was merged (`gh pr list --state merged --head\n<branch>`), and delete them with `git branch -D` (needed because squash\nand rebase merges aren''t seen as merged). Branches with an open or\nunmerged PR, no PR, or unpushed commits are left alone and reported to the\nuser; the current branch and main are never deleted.\n\nVerification: docs-only change. The same rule was applied by hand to the\nlocal branches in this repo before committing, checking each PR''s merge\nstate first.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtgUOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAmFMQAHUka7FDEuhYCLnXMN+cxGzi\nnRRh9Sge12x1b5qMNHAv9pESOC2+44/7+fj4DXsKlGXE3CH9QdADrYBmu3ocu3Gj\nZqzAPn3j2qo1RHXaEKW1H0SyTkAMgg9F/TO10tTu8y9gJ7snGVW/UOx6KiuzqDE7\nvbXrJuJLxMeRUcEtEA+dXC9K/rVWKXTxbqOFxovkAxJZbz4dS/wKqJny4f1WimkY\n00WkvIAow24QhJBGkxtUZQn9pBx0CyDwVOf8mZQZfqYQyWlIK+R2X6946Z7pM+oT\ngMsbzi7ELWfKQZgoEdV4vqzUZY5FdjAM4IXflCPoWGXfzh0i2MOWHq57fgenSu+c\nMN6KEkJNKitq5vz7/ZyR7VjxH