r":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/fda29baccf5162226cc40bf8cec94870ea6d3d22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:13:34Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:13:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Add a Vitest smoke test for the shared Badge so CI''s test step runs (THE-497) (#9)\n\nWhy: issue 1.4''s done-when is \"a failing test blocks merging\", but neither\nproject had any test files, so the `test` step in CI did nothing and there\nwas no real test that could fail. @theory/ui already had a Vitest target\n(jsdom, globals) with passWithNoTests, so this only needed a spec file.\n\nWhat changed:\n- packages/ui/src/lib/Badge.spec.tsx: two tests with Testing Library.\n  The Badge renders its label, and renders the count only when one is\n  given (absent without it, present after a rerender with count=2).\n\nNot changed: portfolio-web still has no Vitest config or tests; the host\nis a placeholder until the real pages land, so a test there would only\nassert placeholder copy.\n\nVerification: `nx test @theory/ui --skip-nx-cache` runs the spec and passes\n(1 file, 2 tests); `biome ci .` passes; `nx run-many -t lint test build`\npasses for both projects.\n\nNext for 1.4: use a throwaway branch that makes this test fail to confirm\nthe required `main` check blocks the merge (PR closed unmerged).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"70779ca5154417213da4de2dc8047b8704ac4c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/70779ca5154417213da4de2dc8047b8704ac4c4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/fda29baccf5162226cc40bf8cec94870ea6d3d22","verification":{"payload":"tree 70779ca5154417213da4de2dc8047b8704ac4c4a\nparent 48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790313214 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790313214 -0400\n\nAdd a Vitest smoke test for the shared Badge so CI''s test step runs (THE-497) (#9)\n\nWhy: issue 1.4''s done-when is \"a failing test blocks merging\", but neither\nproject had any test files, so the `test` step in CI did nothing and there\nwas no real test that could fail. @theory/ui already had a Vitest target\n(jsdom, globals) with passWithNoTests, so this only needed a spec file.\n\nWhat changed:\n- packages/ui/src/lib/Badge.spec.tsx: two tests with Testing Library.\n  The Badge renders its label, and renders the count only when one is\n  given (absent without it, present after a rerender with count=2).\n\nNot changed: portfolio-web still has no Vitest config or tests; the host\nis a placeholder until the real pages land, so a test there would only\nassert placeholder copy.\n\nVerification: `nx test @theory/ui --skip-nx-cache` runs the spec and passes\n(1 file, 2 tests); `biome ci .` passes; `nx run-many -t lint test build`\npasses for both projects.\n\nNext for 1.4: use a throwaway branch that makes this test fail to confirm\nthe required `main` check blocks the merge (PR closed unmerged).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtgL+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4dIQAJxHCYhftUIlLWFUcogJm0/t\nPtyOoSoxsZDIJ16nFqUZDbg4dF6iEpi4Sgpvdq5WAJ0bQ5s6I4qypn8v816gelB+\nzt3B4Cq+3k+cMNALB62ORAramFQbJITjynj248wnw2lABvOh2QXO2T+lbJhbW6b5\n3H5iPvTlee1IXqAjwKptLTwvpm2syBab553rFofbHOsmI/2Y8FVyHir3e34Cq4HP\nxLOgOymAR+1z26OGTXYNIY2O3F3U+1Xqj++j/mlig+to7F0/vFU2d52LTmFz9Foq\nD8KqS2yhjDy2aaq5VfiFYkWz4OFZP5SZYlQryz1Oim0fcfFP54seAjXrH2KjrsBO\nWJxpQ5RwoKDvxGT8UWNc4KJuIBMDvuwVn4+WcUmGSt/R4hr0wJoetzc4dOYhH/Ry\n2MEf+uapqARV8jVfy1Rzgg7lwPYJlKXt9yviW6w8/RnW2SXLNrqPp69iWlKY0iEE\nZbVTYMABgsKtn2iRlfe03LRr2NIbDKWTVKcNlL/jOEPAmE0LxOpHcs1R2GKxUMfi\ncORm903kvH+Mw6k2aqm/PW7xVuOfVXRUcbdOkcO2FMPS/4MFBWlbodUAKIts+9ej\nHeA4LcNcYQ5KKEOoEnSi264zkhSq76rv3ofsTqFBImVZiAi6ujoLNQVodZEfRK/E\nxg9Fbhc651gAXwyCpd92\n=woez\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T05:13:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/fda29baccf5162226cc40bf8cec94870ea6d3d22","node_id":"C_kwDOUoH_vNoAKGZkYTI5YmFjY2Y1MTYyMjI2Y2M0MGJmOGNlYzk0ODcwZWE2ZDNkMjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114","sha":"48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114"}],"sha":"fda29baccf5162226cc40bf8cec94870ea6d3d22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/fda29baccf5162226cc40bf8cec94870ea6d3d22"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:04:45Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T05:04:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Document branch and PR rules in CLAUDE.md; add web run scripts (#8)\n\nWhy: the one-branch-per-issue and squash-merge conventions, and the\nbranch naming, only lived in conversation, so a fresh session wouldn''t\nknow them. The same section was added to theory-apps. Separately, the\nweb app needed short commands to run and check it.\n\nWhat changed:\n- CLAUDE.md: new \"Branches and pull requests\" section after \"Commit\n  messages\":\n  - one branch and one PR per Linear issue; when told to start work,\n    create the branch right away from an up-to-date main, named\n    feature/<issue-id>-<short-description> for new work or\n    bug/<issue-id>-<short-description> for fixes (lowercase issue id);\n  - one-off tasks with no issue use chore/<short-description>, with their\n    own PR; if it turns out to be project scope, check with the user about\n    creating an issue;\n  - squash merge only (main requires a PR and linear history), PR title\n    carries the issue id and the body is built from the commit summaries;\n  - dependent issues are stacked and merged bottom-up, rebasing the next\n    branch onto main and retargeting its PR after each squash merge;\n  - branches are deleted after merge; don''t push, open a PR or merge\n    unless asked.\n- package.json (hand-written by the repo owner, grouped in here):\n  scripts portfolio-web-serve (nx dev), portfolio-web-prod-build (nx\n  build) and portfolio-web-prod-serve (nx preview) for portfolio-web.\n\nVerification: docs change plus three script aliases. package.json parses\nas valid JSON and `biome ci .` passes. The scripts just wrap the existing\nnx targets (dev, build, preview) and were not run separately here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0db5eaaf8cbfe63d48b8a2f02e5d8615f26a1c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/a0db5eaaf8cbfe63d48b8a2f02e5d8615f26a1c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114","verification":{"payload":"tree a0db5eaaf8cbfe63d48b8a2f02e5d8615f26a1c8\nparent 62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790312685 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790312685 -0400\n\nDocument branch and PR rules in CLAUDE.md; add web run scripts (#8)\n\nWhy: the one-branch-per-issue and squash-merge conventions, and the\nbranch naming, only lived in conversation, so a fresh session wouldn''t\nknow them. The same section was added to theory-apps. Separately, the\nweb app needed short commands to run and check it.\n\nWhat changed:\n- CLAUDE.md: new \"Branches and pull requests\" section after \"Commit\n  messages\":\n  - one branch and one PR per Linear issue; when told to start work,\n    create the branch right away from an up-to-date main, named\n    feature/<issue-id>-<short-description> for new work or\n    bug/<issue-id>-<short-description> for fixes (lowercase issue id);\n  - one-off tasks with no issue use chore/<short-description>, with their\n    own PR; if it turns out to be project scope, check with the user about\n    creating an issue;\n  - squash merge only (main requires a PR and linear history), PR title\n    carries the issue id and the body is built from the commit summaries;\n  - dependent issues are stacked and merged bottom-up, rebasing the next\n    branch onto main and retargeting its PR after each squash merge;\n  - branches are deleted after merge; don''t push, open a PR or merge\n    unless asked.\n- package.json (hand-written by the repo owner, grouped in here):\n  scripts portfolio-web-serve (nx dev), portfolio-web-prod-build (nx\n  build) and portfolio-web-prod-serve (nx preview) for portfolio-web.\n\nVerification: docs change plus three script aliases. package.json parses\nas valid JSON and `biome ci .` passes. The scripts just wrap the existing\nnx targets (dev, build, preview) and were not run separately here.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtgDtCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaWMQAKUAdHX3vnP3M2KH4vuMR8j2\ng7BqxSxWc6aAP1ot6hff3nIr9UTXTF2k6AW/o8sp4CPHbxFJe/pN1B4qoqwdaZTD\nERvJ1PR3ygT3QT8lHsKpZUeC2SiiAjeRLZitK0pdWv5kUHzJ+xKrOi7ieBp+5pYQ\nfAnff58Q8sJD3HIEKO2zJJAVuQT4YCQVt4R1YcvJsSwddFArQ1Ml9Ju8DJOMtM0l\nGpMOgsB/P9r9HEQy0YALRFEabmsdSHpKeECCil7lXTovqrvqOBLuBICba2xC8Dae\nn5E9DJYyTPfif0Vf3BqwKjCafiFUfhTkEyZMaeyFLwQP2rYK+opLaCt/OHwUh/KG\nGAKMAmmU3CBI5AdYOKXLsoG8g+40TwtqvtksAx1wa97p/PHZb8VvrKurZajfHd0n\nNC29jxaqTxPe2fnTVzYFkCOJMVd6gfJaqfPgH3781BwWV+6Znz1B27FI5Rq5AQTo\nkc5erWa7msbu4CUhlNn6DqjjqomDfgxwsIBjf4l5JDn1tNXZ1CM8ACmUa/2Ztxte\nDXE5beVxr//GEifmd6ZVKsvtwTXbjIQIvHYtr5Rg5bsCFXYyVun5II1sJCNnRJ2Z\nGyJn5URuv8PhbQk/2Q/KMR693C0lI3HU9d+Nui+VAw/hdpJhchRGiI+jgiftLWIE\nnNOtd/S6HFx0jc+hWVMC\n=eu6H\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T05:04:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114","node_id":"C_kwDOUoH_vNoAKDQ4ZWU3MjFhODYxMjA5OTMzOGE4NzNkZWM4YzNlNmUzMTA2YTAxMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/theory-network/portfolio/commit/62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95","sha":"62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95"}],"sha":"48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/48ee721a8612099338a873dec8c3e6e3106a0114"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T04:55:25Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T04:55:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Rewrite CI without Nx Cloud (THE-497) (#5)\n\nWhy: the workflow copied in from Nx''s React module federation template\ndepended on Nx Cloud (`start-ci-run` with distributed agents, `nx record`,\n`fix-ci`), which we don''t use (`neverConnectToCloud: true` in nx.json).\nIt also ran `nx format:check` (Prettier, while the repo''s formatter is\nBiome) and targets that don''t exist yet (typecheck, e2e). Issue 1.4 asks\nfor `nx affected -t lint test build` with caching on every PR.\n\nWhat changed (.github/workflows/ci.yml):\n- Full-history checkout (needed for `nx affected`), Node 24, `npm ci`.\n- Local Nx cache (.nx/cache) restored and saved with actions/cache.\n- `npx biome ci .` for formatting and import order.\n- `nx affected -t lint test build`, comparing against the PR base commit,\n  or the previous commit on pushes to main.\n- Concurrency group cancels superseded runs on the same ref; the job has\n  a 20 minute timeout; permissions reduced to contents: read.\n- E2E and deploys are left for later issues (2.4 adds deploys).\n\nAlso: one blank line added to CLAUDE.md before the \"Algorithm\" numbered\nlist, which Prettier''s markdown check wanted; no wording changed.\n\nVerification: `npx biome ci .` passes and\n`nx affected -t lint test build --base=HEAD~2` passes locally. The\nworkflow has not run on GitHub yet; that needs the push and a PR. Still\nopen on 1.4: make the check required in main''s ruleset once it has run,\nand prove a failing test blocks merging. Neither project has a `test`\ntarget yet, so `test` is a no-op until tests exist.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"95fce93e65e5868182ea2b94af7adf3268ce2756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/95fce93e65e5868182ea2b94af7adf3268ce2756"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95","verification":{"payload":"tree 95fce93e65e5868182ea2b94af7adf3268ce2756\nparent b4a0740c1992d19b708e0e13a57040b7099b5de7\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790312125 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790312125 -0400\n\nRewrite CI without Nx Cloud (THE-497) (#5)\n\nWhy: the workflow copied in from Nx''s React module federation template\ndepended on Nx Cloud (`start-ci-run` with distributed agents, `nx record`,\n`fix-ci`), which we don''t use (`neverConnectToCloud: true` in nx.json).\nIt also ran `nx format:check` (Prettier, while the repo''s formatter is\nBiome) and targets that don''t exist yet (typecheck, e2e). Issue 1.4 asks\nfor `nx affected -t lint test build` with caching on every PR.\n\nWhat changed (.github/workflows/ci.yml):\n- Full-history checkout (needed for `nx affected`), Node 24, `npm ci`.\n- Local Nx cache (.nx/cache) restored and saved with actions/cache.\n- `npx biome ci .` for formatting and import order.\n- `nx affected -t lint test build`, comparing against the PR base commit,\n  or the previous commit on pushes to main.\n- Concurrency group cancels superseded runs on the same ref; the job has\n  a 20 minute timeout; permissions reduced to contents: read.\n- E2E and deploys are left for later issues (2.4 adds deploys).\n\nAlso: one blank line added to CLAUDE.md before the \"Algorithm\" numbered\nlist, which Prettier''s markdown check wanted; no wording changed.\n\nVerification: `npx biome ci .` passes and\n`nx affected -t lint test build --base=HEAD~2` passes locally. The\nworkflow has not run on GitHub yet; that needs the push and a PR. Still\nopen on 1.4: make the check required in main''s ruleset once it has run,\nand prove a failing test blocks merging. Neither project has a `test`\ntarget yet, so `test` is a no-op until tests exist.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtf6+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMVgQAG2LkIeMgYt4hXIEYofgMkCq\npU8CK3EAz3py4tpHj/AtIQ3uVAe0NGO2yBSWTy3/OusTw1MignO+9ink/0lyXypO\ntCtF/Qfw33NvXUGbsyRfS4RI7N34MOUbCxdF7g3Utu95wXQ0nN3Mp/2o4C3O1UvL\n8b0RXvkC1ecqbISuRKeh5IGso/hijoj2++GPh4/0LlcIbLymJR2ATLtZKkhHzYP3\n6ap