5cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/62fc0005cb0ecbe359904621015eb47e69b5ac95"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1444536?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/andre-davcev","id":1444536,"login":"andre-davcev","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0NDQ1MzY=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/andre-davcev","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/commits/b4a0740c1992d19b708e0e13a57040b7099b5de7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T04:53:43Z","email":"andre.davcev@gmail.com","name":"Andre Davcev"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T04:53:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"1.3 Agent setup: CLAUDE.md with Nx guidance (THE-496) (#6)\n\n* Add CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md with Linear-driven \"what''s next\" rules (THE-496)\n\nWhy: this repo was recreated fresh (the previous theory-portfolio\ncontents were renamed to theory-apps), so it had no agent instructions.\nIssue 1.3 (Agent setup) plans to copy the \"what''s next\" and \"keeping\nLinear in sync\" rules from theory-apps/AGENTS.md, pointed at the\nPortfolio Linear project. This commit does that half of 1.3 now, so\n\"what''s next\" works from the first session.\n\nWhat changed:\n- CLAUDE.md: a single `@AGENTS.md` import, matching theory-apps.\n- AGENTS.md:\n  - \"what''s next\" points at the Linear Portfolio project (Theory Network\n    team) as the source of truth and says not to pull issues from the\n    Nexus project, which lives in theory-apps.\n  - Algorithm: finish an In Progress issue first; otherwise walk Epic 1\n    (Repo & Tooling) through Epic 7 (QA & Launch) in order and take the\n    lowest-numbered non-Done X.Y in the first epic with open work.\n    Un-parented issues are outside the walk.\n  - Notes that the epic order is also written in the Linear project''s\n    description, so both places need updating if it changes, plus the\n    numbering-integrity rule for gaps/duplicates/inserts.\n  - \"Keeping Linear in sync\" rules adapted from theory-apps, with the\n    Nexus-specific examples reworded for this repo.\n  - New \"Commit messages\" section: every commit body must carry the\n    AI-generated summary (what, why, how verified), the Linear issue id\n    goes in the subject, and messages are passed via `git commit -F`.\n\nDeliberately not included: Nx guidance. There is no Nx workspace yet\n(1.2), and 1.3 still needs to add the Nx guidance for agents once the\nworkspace exists, so 1.3 stays open after this commit.\n\nVerification: docs-only change. Ran the \"what''s next\" algorithm against\nthe Linear Portfolio project as a check: with nothing In Progress it\nresolved to 1.1 (Repo housekeeping, THE-494), the lowest-numbered open\nissue in Epic 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Move agent instructions into CLAUDE.md with the Nx guidance (THE-496)\n\nWhy: 1.3 (Agent setup) still lacked the Nx guidance for agents, now that\nthe Nx workspace exists. This repo is only worked on with Claude Code,\nand `nx configure-ai-agents` writes its rules block to CLAUDE.md for\nClaude, so keeping the rules in AGENTS.md behind an `@AGENTS.md` import\nwould have duplicated the block on the next Nx update. One file avoids\nthat and matches theory-apps.\n\nWhat changed:\n- CLAUDE.md now contains, in order: the Nx guidance block copied from\n  Nx''s React module federation template (with its start/end markers, so\n  Nx can keep it up to date), the Portfolio \"what''s next\" rules, the\n  \"Keeping Linear in sync\" rules and the \"Commit messages\" rule. The\n  rules text is unchanged from AGENTS.md.\n- AGENTS.md is deleted. It only ever held the rules now in CLAUDE.md.\n\nPolicy recorded with this: no home-grown skills; the Nx-provided skills\nare fine and Claude gets them from the Nx plugin.\n\nVerification: docs-only change. The file was assembled by script from the\nold AGENTS.md sections and the template''s Nx block (no hand retyping),\nand I checked that the Nx start/end markers each appear once and that\nthe section headings are all present.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Scaffold the Nx workspace and portfolio-web host with tooling (THE-495) (#7)\n\nWhy: issue 1.2 asks for the Nx workspace, the portfolio-web host and\nthe same tooling as theory-apps. The older `@nx/react:host` generator\nis deprecated in Nx 23 (removed in 24) and crashed with TypeScript 7\nhoisted, so the workspace was generated from Nx''s React module\nfederation template (nrwl/react-mfe-template) and copied in, with the\nscope renamed to @theory.\n\nWhat changed:\n- Workspace: Nx 23.2.1 with npm workspaces (apps/*, packages/*). nx and\n  every @nx/* package are pinned to 23.2.1 because @aws/nx-plugin@1.0.3\n  peer-requires exactly that. typescript is pinned to ~6.0.3 because\n  TypeScript 7 lacks the JS compiler API the Nx tooling needs.\n- apps/portfolio-web (@theory/portfolio-web): Vite host using\n  @module-federation/vite and @module-federation/runtime, with TanStack\n  Router. It is a placeholder home page with no remotes yet\n  (PROVIDERS = [] in src/mf.ts). The serve target is `dev`.\n- packages/ui (@theory/ui): shared theme CSS and a Badge. The template''s\n  demo product components and data were removed.\n- Tooling, matching theory-apps: Biome (biome.json copied), root ESLint\n  flat config (per-project lint targets are inferred), Vitest,\n  Playwright e2e, husky with the vendored git-secrets pre-commit hook,\n  and aws-nx-plugin.config.mts (Terraform, Docker).\n- README: stack section now describes the Vite/TanStack host and tooling,\n  and a Getting started section lists the real commands.\n- Also from the template: .github/ (CI workflow plus Nx skills), .agents/\n  (Nx skills), .claude/ plugin settings, editor/prettier config, tools/.\n  Agent config for other tools was deliberately not kept.\n\nDeviations from the issue as first written: Vite + TanStack Router +\nVitest instead of Rspack + React Router + Jest; `dev` instead of\n`serve`. Linear (THE-495 and the Epic 2 issues) was updated to match.\n\nVerification: `nx run-many -t lint test build --skip-nx-cache` passes;\nthe dev server serves the page at http://127.0.0.1:4200; the Playwright\nexample test passes in Chromium.\n\nNot done here: the template''s .github/workflows/ci.yml is unreviewed and\nbelongs to 1.4 (CI pipeline).\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"663ced09f9261fed447021bb18832fac4e55a83b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/trees/663ced09f9261fed447021bb18832fac4e55a83b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/theory-network/portfolio/git/commits/b4a0740c1992d19b708e0e13a57040b7099b5de7","verification":{"payload":"tree 663ced09f9261fed447021bb18832fac4e55a83b\nparent 439d4935d75a8774e34aee48435718a7d623ba44\nauthor Andre Davcev <andre.davcev@gmail.com> 1790312023 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790312023 -0400\n\n1.3 Agent setup: CLAUDE.md with Nx guidance (THE-496) (#6)\n\n* Add CLAUDE.md and AGENTS.md with Linear-driven \"what''s next\" rules (T