91/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commits/26b5f49d22dda4cf6033d23f18d2543f00b2f331/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:24:19Z","email":"ty.moodley@outlook.com","name":"Tyrone Moodley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T21:24:19Z","email":"ty.moodley@outlook.com","name":"Tyrone Moodley"},"message":"Add the Finance sub-app with the Absa artisanal gold mining loan\n\nBuilt from the Migodi-Auric application screens (1 October 2026). An ASM group\nchecks it''s eligible (Zambian-owned, registered, licensed, banked), describes\nitself and where it is, picks equipment to hire or buy plus months of running\ncosts (with a live ZMW estimate), uploads its four documents, declares and\nsubmits. The application then goes Village Productivity -> Ward Development ->\nChief -> Constituency CDF -> Provincial CDF committees -> collection at Absa;\neach can approve, send back or decline, and the applicant follows it live.\n\n- Admins set up committees per stage and area (the most specific covering an\n  application''s place handles it; admins can act where there''s none), equipment\n  prices (\"TBC\" until set) and constituency lists.\n- Documents are checked by content (PDF/JPEG/PNG/WebP, 10 MB) and opened through\n  short-lived signed links; only the applicant, admins and the application''s\n  committees can see an application.\n- One open application per registration number; a printable paper form.\n- Styled after the screens (deep green and gold), with dark mode.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d91bf5833b825493a1e5020dfd33db68aa5c526a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/git/trees/d91bf5833b