riptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commit/32b839640195934711673fcf6820da783a0c3d0e","node_id":"C_kwDOUoWZvtoAKDMyYjgzOTY0MDE5NTkzNDcxMTY3M2ZjZjY4MjBkYTc4M2EwYzNkMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commit/a88fbcc499ac08c6997d2dd8d3225699d3f638f3","sha":"a88fbcc499ac08c6997d2dd8d3225699d3f638f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commits/a88fbcc499ac08c6997d2dd8d3225699d3f638f3"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commit/6da5f2ca0b572ad419c063b7a1deaccda0b4c4c8","sha":"6da5f2ca0b572ad419c063b7a1deaccda0b4c4c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commits/6da5f2ca0b572ad419c063b7a1deaccda0b4c4c8"}],"sha":"32b839640195934711673fcf6820da783a0c3d0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commits/32b839640195934711673fcf6820da783a0c3d0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92172044?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/tyrone191","id":92172044,"login":"tyrone191","node_id":"U_kgDOBX5vDA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tyrone191","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/commits/6da5f2ca0b572ad419c063b7a1deaccda0b4c4c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:19:11Z","email":"ty.moodley@outlook.com","name":"Tyrone Moodley"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T01:19:11Z","email":"ty.moodley@outlook.com","name":"Tyrone Moodley"},"message":"Add the Ndeipi Chat web app at chat.ndeipi.com\n\nA Blazor WebAssembly app (src/NdeipiChat.Web), served by the API from the\nsame origin. It reuses Client.Core''s view models, API client and SignalR\nconnection, so the website behaves like the phone app: chats with live\nmessages and typing, Send money and token transfers with live status,\nShamwaris (add by email or phone, accept, decline, cancel, remove, groups),\nand Me/Wallet. Livestock stays in the phone app.\n\n- Sign-in leaves the page for the API''s sign-in page and returns to\n  /signin/callback, with the PKCE secrets in the tab''s sessionStorage. A\n  popup would have kept the app''s flow, but Google and other providers cut\n  a popup off from its opener. AuthService.SignInAsync is split into\n  StartSignIn and CompleteSignInAsync; the phone app is unchanged.\n- ClientOptions.SupportsLivestock (on by default) lets the web app skip the\n  livestock capture queue, whose SQLite can''t run in the browser.\n- The API serves the app with MapStaticAssets and falls back to index.html\n  for page URLs, while unknown paths under api/, hubs/, auth/, webhooks/\n  and openapi/ stay 404. index.html names blazor.webassembly.js plainly:\n  the fallback serves the file as-is, so fingerprint placeholders would\n  never be filled (that was a 404 on the first deploy).\n- The web callback URLs are on MobileAuth:RedirectUris.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9f094d1765d264f00b777dec452823172280af8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/git/trees/9f094d1765d264f00b777dec452823172280af8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tmoodley/ndeipi-chat/git/commits/6da5f2ca0b572ad419c063b7a1deaccda0b4c4c